{"raw": {"https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964379/": {"title": "HR-administrat\u00f6r", "description": "HR-administrat\u00f6r Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) HR-administrat\u00f6r Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Om arbetsplatsen Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r placerad vid HR-avdelningen inom Kansli S vid Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten. Kansli S best\u00e5r av cirka 70 medarbetare och ger kvalificerat verksamhetsst\u00f6d till fakultetsledning och institutioner inom bland annat ekonomi, HR, utbildning, forskning, kommunikation och ledningsst\u00f6d. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Som HR - administrat\u00f6r \u00e4r ditt huvudsakliga uppdrag att ge administrativt st\u00f6d inom HR-omr\u00e5det till chefer och medarbetare. Rollen inneb\u00e4r m\u00e5nga kontaktytor och n\u00e4ra samarbete med kollegor vid Kansli S samt andra HR-funktioner inom Lunds universitet. Du blir ett verksamhetsn\u00e4ra st\u00f6d och en viktig del i att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla kvalitet och effektivitet i HR-processerna. Dina huvudsakliga arbetsuppgifter \u00e4r: Administrativ hantering av anst\u00e4llningens livscykel: Fr\u00e5n rekrytering till avslut, inklusive handl\u00e4ggning av rekryterings- och anst\u00e4llnings\u00e4renden, st\u00f6d i HR-system, hantering av utl\u00e4gg och reser\u00e4kningar, diarief\u00f6ring och arkivering, bevakning av tidsbegr\u00e4nsade anst\u00e4llningar, semesteruttag och ledigheter, hantering av varsel samt st\u00f6d vid on- och offboarding. R\u00e5dgivning och st\u00f6d: Ge v\u00e4gledning i personaladministrativa fr\u00e5gor samt grundl\u00e4ggande arbetsr\u00e4tt och avtalsfr\u00e5gor. U tveckling av processer: I samverkan med kollegor inom fakultetens HR-avdelning utveckla och implementera HR-processer och administrativa rutiner. Detta inneb\u00e4r aktivt deltagande i n\u00e4tverk och arbetsgrupper. Rollen kombinerar praktiskt arbete med r\u00e5dgivande inslag. Vi s\u00f6ker dig som har erfarenhet av HR-administration, \u00e4r serviceinriktad och har relevant utbildning. Du \u00e4r strukturerad, noggrann och effektiv, med f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att prioritera och hantera flera uppgifter parallellt. Arbetet kan periodvis vara intensivt, vilket kr\u00e4ver stresst\u00e5lighet och sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndighet. Stor vikt l\u00e4ggs vid hur din kompetens och erfarenhet kompletterar v\u00e5rt team och bidrar till HR-avdelningens utveckling. Kvalifikationer Krav: Utbildning inom HR-omr\u00e5det eller annan utbildning/erfarenhet som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer likv\u00e4rdig. Aktuell erfarenhet av HR-administration och l\u00f6neadministration. Mycket god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att kommunicera p\u00e5 svenska och engelska. God digital kompetens och erfarenhet av att arbeta i HR-system. Meriterande: Aktuell erfarenhet av att arbeta med Primula. Erfarenhet av HR-administrativt arbete inom offentlig verksamhet. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r p\u00e5 heltid och \u00e4r ett vikariat p\u00e5 1 \u00e5r. Tilltr\u00e4de 1 februari eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r huvudsakligen placerad i Lund men tj\u00e4nsten inneb\u00e4r att st\u00f6tta tv\u00e5 institutioner p\u00e5 Campus Helsingborg. Detta inneb\u00e4r regelbundet resor till Helsingborg. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Ans\u00f6kan g\u00f6rs via universitetets rekryteringssystem och ska inneh\u00e5lla: Personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av tj\u00e4nsten och hur dina meriter matchar kraven. CV samt \u00f6vriga dokument du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa. Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra f\u00f6r forskning och utbildning inom samh\u00e4lls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg, \u00f6ver 700 anst\u00e4llda och cirka 5 700 hel\u00e5rsstudenter \u00e4r fakulteten en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. V\u00e5r huvuduppgift \u00e4r att utveckla, f\u00f6rmedla och f\u00f6rvalta kunskap om samh\u00e4lle, m\u00e4nniska och organisationer i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av \u00f6ppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 1 februari 2027 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2519 Kontakt Andr\u00e9a Bj\u00f6rk, HR-chef/avdelningschef, andrea.bjork@sam.lu.se Jennifer Condliffe, HR-specialist, jennifer.condliffe@sam.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-12 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-26 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975474/": {"title": "Forskningsingenj\u00f6r vid Lund Protein Production Platform", "description": "Forskningsingenj\u00f6r vid Lund Protein Production Platform Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Forskningsingenj\u00f6r vid Lund Protein Production Platform Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Arbetsuppgifter Lund Protein Production Platform (LP3) \u00e4r ett fakultets\u00f6vergripande centrum vid Lunds universitet f\u00f6r proteinproduktion, karakterisering, kristallografi och strukturbest\u00e4mning. LP3 \u00e4r en nod inom den nationella forskningsinfrastrukturen Protein Production Sweden (PPS) och har ett n\u00e4ra samarbete med forskare fr\u00e5n MAX IV-laboratoriet och European Spallation Source ERIC. Du kommer att spela en viktig roll vid LP3. Arbetsuppgifterna innefattar sk\u00f6tsel av utrustning, projektplanering, kontakt med klienter och administration. Du kommer ocks\u00e5 arbeta experimentellt p\u00e5 projektbasis, samt f\u00f6ra en kontinuerlig dialog med forskaren/klienten och med LP3-kollegorna. Du f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas ta ansvar och driva projekten med stor sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndighet. De laborativa arbetsuppgifterna innefattar: Att utarbeta och optimera uttryckssystem f\u00f6r varje projekt. Att utarbeta och optimera protein-uppreningssystem f\u00f6r varje projekt. Att skala upp befintliga protokoll f\u00f6r proteinuttryck och upprening. Att analysera proteinprover f\u00f6r kvalitetskontroll och optimering av protokoll. Att uttrycka och rena upp protein till f\u00f6rutbest\u00e4md kvalitet och kvantitet inom f\u00f6rutbest\u00e4mda tidsramar. Uppr\u00e4tth\u00e5lla ett cellodlings laboratorium med speciellt ansvar f\u00f6r insekt celler. Utveckla nya metoder till biologiska deutering. Vid behov genomf\u00f6ra neutron- och X-ray spridningsf\u00f6rs\u00f6k Att analysera, dokumentera och rapportera experimentella data. Laborativ handledning av bes\u00f6kande forskare. Kontinuerlig kommunikation och dialog med LP3-anv\u00e4ndare. Administrativa uppgifter som best\u00e4llning, fakturering etc. Uppr\u00e4tth\u00e5lla den senaste kunskapen om tekniker och aktuell litteratur f\u00f6r att anpassa och/eller utveckla nya metoder och experiment. Krav Den framg\u00e5ngsrika kandidaten \u00e4r en skicklig life-science-ut\u00f6vare med god k\u00e4nsla f\u00f6r service, som tilltalas av laboratoriebaserade projekt i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av lagarbete och tydliga tidsramar. Ph.D. inom biomedicin, biokemi, molekyl\u00e4rbiologi, biofysik eller andra relevanta \u00e4mnen Erfarenhet och djup f\u00f6rst\u00e5else av att arbeta med teknikerna bakom protein-produktion och karakterisering Erfarenhet och djup f\u00f6rst\u00e5else av att arbeta med anv\u00e4ndning av deutererate biomoleculer och kontrast Flera \u00e5rs erfarenhet av proteinrening i flera steg av rekombinant protein f\u00f6r struktur- och/eller funktionsstudier. Erfarenhet av odling av och proteinproduktion i E. coli och med BEVS Erfarenhet av analytiska tekniker f\u00f6r biofysikalisk och biokemisk karakterisering (t.ex. SDS-PAGE, SEC, MS, UV-VIS, UV-CD). Erfarenhet att l\u00e4ra sig och utveckla nya tekniker inom proteinproduktion, deuterering och biofysikalisk karakterisering Erfarenhet av att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla en v\u00e4lorganiserad och s\u00e4ker laboratoriemilj\u00f6 Goda datorkunskaper i windows och med system som anv\u00e4nds inom LP3 (t. ex. office paket, illaber, snapgene, FPLC software) Utm\u00e4rkt skriftlig och muntlig kommunikationsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga i engelska. Erfarenhet av att presentera resultat och metoder i rapport och f\u00f6redragsform \u00d6vriga meriter: Erfarenhet av SANS och SAXS och databehandling av SANS och SAXS f\u00f6rs\u00f6k Erfarenhet av odling av pro- och eukaryota celler i bioreaktor. Erfarenhet av projektplanering och genomf\u00f6rande. Vi kommer att l\u00e4gga stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. H\u00e4nsyn kommer ocks\u00e5 att tas till god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, drivkraft och sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndighet samt hur den s\u00f6kandes erfarenhet och kompetens kompletterar och st\u00e4rker LP3s verksamhet. Vi l\u00e4gger ocks\u00e5 vikt vid s\u00f6kandes f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att vara en effektiv lagspelare, att vara anv\u00e4ndar-och serviceinriktad samt att ha erfarenhet av att bidra till andras l\u00e4rande. Villkor Anst\u00e4llningsform: Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning i 6 m\u00e5nader Omfattning: 100 % Placering: Lund Protein Production Platform (LP3), Biologihus A, Lund Tilltr\u00e4de: Tilltr\u00e4de s\u00e5 snart som m\u00f6jligt den 15 november 2026, eller efter \u00f6verenskommelse. Kontakt Dr. Wolfgang Knecht Senior Lecturer & Manager LP3 Lund University Department of Biology, Molecular Biosciences S\u00f6lvegatan 35 22362 Lund, Sweden +46 46 2227785 Wolfgang.Knecht@biol.lu.se; www.lu.se/lp3 Instruktioner f\u00f6r ans\u00f6kan Din ans\u00f6kan m\u00e5ste skickas in elektroniskt via rekryteringssystemet Varbi. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla f\u00f6ljande dokument/bilagor: Ans\u00f6kningsbrev (ber\u00e4tta p\u00e5 en sida om dig sj\u00e4lv, din bakgrund och din motivation p\u00e5 ett s\u00e4tt som visar att du \u00e4r r\u00e4tt person f\u00f6r jobbet.). Vi uppmuntrar dig att specificera och motivera dina l\u00f6nef\u00f6rv\u00e4ntningar. CV (personuppgifter, utbildning, arbetslivserfarenhet/forskningserfarenhet, spr\u00e5kkunskaper och andra f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten relevanta f\u00e4rdigheter). En bestyrkt/signerad kopia av Ph.D. grad. Lista \u00f6ver publikationer (om till\u00e4mpligt). Minst tv\u00e5 referenser (Inklusive titel/befattning, namn, kontaktuppgifter och personens koppling till dig). Vid Naturvetenskapliga fakulteten bedrivs forskning och utbildning inom astronomi, biologi fysik, geovetenskap, kemi, matematik, medicinsk str\u00e5lningsfysik, milj\u00f6vetenskap och naturgeografi. Verksamheten bedrivs inom norra universitetsomr\u00e5det. Fakulteten har ca 1 900 studenter, 330 forskarstuderande och 730 anst\u00e4llda. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform S\u00e4rskild visstidsanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 15 november 2026 eller efter \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2867 Kontakt Wolfgang Knecht, universitetslektor, +46462227785, wolfgang.knecht@biol.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-12 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-26 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:976100/": {"title": "Bitr\u00e4dande Sektionschef", "description": "Bitr\u00e4dande Sektionschef Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Bitr\u00e4dande Sektionschef Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av Sektionen Vill du vara med och utveckla och forma IT-leveranser i en komplex och samh\u00e4llsviktig organisation?\u00a0 Som bitr\u00e4dande sektionschef vid Sektionen IT f\u00e5r du en central roll i att leda, samordna och utveckla sektionens operativa verksamhet. Du \u00e4r direkt underst\u00e4lld sektionschefen, tillika IT-direkt\u00f6ren, och ansvarar f\u00f6r att oms\u00e4tta strategisk inriktning till effektiv operativ verksamhet. Rollen inneb\u00e4r n\u00e4ra samverkan med avdelningschefer, medarbetare och verksamhetsf\u00f6retr\u00e4dare inom universitetet. Du bidrar aktivt till att skapa effektiva, moderna och behovsanpassade IT-tj\u00e4nster f\u00f6r hela Lunds universitet. Sektionen IT \u00e4r Lunds universitets gemensamma IT-funktion och ska bidra till en h\u00f6g kvalitet och effektivitet i universitetets digitalisering, genom att leverera tj\u00e4nster inom drift och utveckling av applikationer och infrastruktur. Lunds universitet har en gemensam IT-organisation, Sektionen IT, och IT-organisationer p\u00e5 fakultets- och institutionsniv\u00e5 som hanterar de mer verksamhetsn\u00e4ra IT-milj\u00f6erna. Vid sektionen finns fyra operativa avdelningar och en stabsavdelning. Sektionen har ca 120 medarbetare. L\u00e4s mer om Sektionen IT h\u00e4r . Vi Erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Som chef har du dessutom tillg\u00e5ng till s\u00e4rskilda utbildnings- och utvecklingsm\u00f6jligheter genom universitetets chefsplattform. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats, Jobba hos oss. Som anst\u00e4lld p\u00e5 Sektionen IT f\u00e5r du m\u00f6jlighet att arbeta i en inspirerande, sp\u00e4nnande och skiftande milj\u00f6. F\u00f6r dig som \u00e4r intresserad av och nyfiken p\u00e5 att l\u00e4ra sig om olika behov inom forskning och utbildning \u00e4r universitetet r\u00e4tt arbetsplats. Vi erbjuder en flexibel arbetsmilj\u00f6 f\u00f6r att s\u00e4kra en h\u00e5llbar balans mellan jobb och fritid f\u00f6r den enskilde medarbetaren. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Som bitr\u00e4dande sektionschef har du, p\u00e5 uppdrag av sektionschefen tillika IT-direkt\u00f6ren, det \u00f6vergripande ansvaret f\u00f6r ledning, samordning och utveckling av sektionens operativa verksamhet. Rollen inneb\u00e4r ett helhetsansvar f\u00f6r verksamhet, ekonomi, personal och arbetsmilj\u00f6 samt f\u00f6r att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla att sektionens tj\u00e4nster och leveranser m\u00f6ter universitetets behov. Detta sker i n\u00e4ra samverkan med sektionens avdelningschefer och medarbetare. Du leder sektionens ledningsgrupp och arbetar n\u00e4ra verksamheten f\u00f6r att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla att IT-leveranser sker effektivt och med h\u00f6g kvalitet, i linje med universitetets behov. I rollen ing\u00e5r bland annat att: Leda och utveckla sektionens operativa verksamhet S\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla sektionens leveransf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och att universitetets verksamheter erh\u00e5ller \u00e4ndam\u00e5lsenliga, kostnadseffektiva och drifts\u00e4kra IT-tj\u00e4nster Ha direkt chefsansvar f\u00f6r sektionens avdelningschefer och leda sektionens ledningsgrupp Ansvara f\u00f6r sektionens budget, ekonomiska uppf\u00f6ljning och verksamhetsstyrning Representera IT inom universitetets gemensamma f\u00f6rvaltning och bidra i \u00f6vergripande fr\u00e5gor Vara IT-system\u00e4gare f\u00f6r gemensamma f\u00f6rvaltningens och fakulteternas IT-tj\u00e4nster Bidra till utvecklingen av \u00e4ndam\u00e5lsenliga, s\u00e4kra och behovsanpassade IT-tj\u00e4nster Bitr\u00e4dande sektionschef rapporterar till sektionschef f\u00f6r sektionen IT. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen: Relevant akademisk examen eller annan erfarenhet som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer som likv\u00e4rdig. Dokumenterad erfarenhet av att leda st\u00f6rre verksamheter genom f\u00f6r\u00e4ndring, tillv\u00e4xt eller organisatorisk utveckling i komplexa och kunskapsintensiva milj\u00f6er. Fler\u00e5rig och dokumenterat framg\u00e5ngsrik erfarenhet av chefsuppdrag med personal-, verksamhets- och ekonomiansvar. Erfarenhet av att vara chef \u00f6ver chefer och av att leda genom underst\u00e4llda chefer. Dokumenterad erfarenhet av att leda och utveckla en IT-verksamhet med ansvar f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsteleverans, infrastruktur, applikationsf\u00f6rvaltning och verksamhetsutveckling Mycket god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga Dokumenterad erfarenhet av f\u00f6r\u00e4ndringsledning och l\u00e5ngsiktig verksamhetsutveckling Mycket god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att planera, prioritera, f\u00f6lja upp och driva utveckling i komplexa sammanhang Mycket god kommunikativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga samt f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att skapa dialog, f\u00f6rankring och samverkan Erfarenhet av arbete inom statlig myndighet och god f\u00f6rst\u00e5else f\u00f6r offentlig f\u00f6rvaltning. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen: Erfarenhet av IT-arbete inom universitets- och h\u00f6gskolesektorn Dokumenterad erfarenhet av att leda organisatorisk f\u00f6r\u00e4ndring och verksamhetsutveckling i komplexa kunskapsintensiva organisationer. Personliga egenskaper: Du \u00e4r en trygg och erfaren ledare som kan oms\u00e4tta strategiska m\u00e5l och prioriteringar till konkret verksamhet och m\u00e4tbara resultat. Du har ett helhetsperspektiv, ett gott omd\u00f6me och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att prioritera och fatta beslut i komplexa situationer. Samtidigt \u00e4r du lyh\u00f6rd f\u00f6r verksamhetens behov och kan anpassa arbetet utifr\u00e5n f\u00f6r\u00e4ndrade f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar. Du ut\u00f6var ett tillitsbaserat ledarskap och skapar f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r chefer och medarbetare att lyckas i sina uppdrag. Genom tydlighet, struktur och god kommunikation bygger du f\u00f6rtroende, engagemang och samsyn i organisationen. Rollen st\u00e4ller h\u00f6ga krav p\u00e5 samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att skapa goda relationer s\u00e5v\u00e4l inom som utanf\u00f6r den egna organisationen. Du \u00e4r prestigel\u00f6s, l\u00f6sningsorienterad och har f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att driva f\u00f6r\u00e4ndring och utveckling fr\u00e5n beslut till genomf\u00f6rande. Vid bed\u00f6mningen kommer stor vikt att l\u00e4ggas vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tills vidare med start i januari eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Provanst\u00e4llning kan komma att till\u00e4mpas. Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla ett personligt brev d\u00e4r du beskriver hur du uppfyller kvalifikationskraven och varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen samt ett CV. Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av examen, betyg, intyg, rekommendationsbrev, uppgifter till referenser etc). Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Intervjuer kommer \u00e4ga rum i Lund och planeras ske i november Sektionen IT \u00e4r Lunds universitets gemensamma IT-funktion och ska bidra till en h\u00f6g kvalitet och effektivitet i universitetets digitalisering, genom att leverera tj\u00e4nster inom drift och utveckling av applikationer och infrastruktur. Lunds universitet har en gemensam IT-organisation, Sektionen IT, och IT-organisationer p\u00e5 fakultets- och institutionsniv\u00e5 som hanterar de mer verksamhetsn\u00e4ra IT-milj\u00f6erna. Vid sektionen finns fyra operativa avdelningar och en stabsavdelning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2892 Kontakt John Westerlund, +46462221254, john.westerlund@it.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-12 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-26 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977517/": {"title": "Vikarierande Studiev\u00e4gledare", "description": "Vikarierande Studiev\u00e4gledare Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Vikarierande Studiev\u00e4gledare Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Historiska institutionen erbjuder en vital och stor undervisnings- och forskningsmilj\u00f6 med aktivt pedagogiskt utvecklingsarbete. P\u00e5 institutionen jobbar vi mycket tillsammans och som studiev\u00e4gledare kommer du ha st\u00f6d av kollegor, studierektor och administrat\u00f6r. Institutionen m\u00e5nar om en god arbetsmilj\u00f6 med \u00e5terkommande gemensamma personal- och l\u00e4rarm\u00f6ten, gemensamma fikor och \u00e5rlig psykosocial enk\u00e4t. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Arbetet som vikarierande studiev\u00e4gledare \u00e4r f\u00f6rdelat mellan \u00e4mnena M\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter (75%) och Historia (25%) som b\u00e5da tillh\u00f6r samma institution (historiska). P\u00e5 M\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter arbetar du tillsammans med studieadministrat\u00f6ren och studierektorn och p\u00e5 Historia tillsammans med studiev\u00e4gledaren. B\u00e5da \u00e4mnena har kandidatprogram, masterprogram och frist\u00e5ende kurser. Arbetsuppgifterna best\u00e5r bland annat i att: informera och v\u00e4gleda om studier i enskilt och i grupp organisera pedagogiskt studentst\u00f6d organisera och ansvara f\u00f6r introduktionsvecka p\u00e5 kandidatprogrammet i m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter samordna praktikkursen med studierektor anordna examensmingel f\u00f6r kandidatstudenter rekrytera, administrera och sk\u00f6ta kontakten med SI-ledare. Vidare ing\u00e5r i arbetsuppgifterna att ta fram beslutsunderlag i student\u00e4renden, exempelvis dispensans\u00f6kningar, tillgodor\u00e4knande, avbrott och beh\u00f6righeter, skapa och uppdatera inneh\u00e5ll i Canvas, samt organisera och ansvara f\u00f6r introduktionsvecka p\u00e5 kandidatprogrammet i m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter. I arbetsuppgifterna ing\u00e5r det ocks\u00e5 att delta i utvecklingsarbete och marknadsf\u00f6ring p\u00e5 avdelning och fakultet genom deltagande i n\u00e4tverk och m\u00f6ten. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Den s\u00f6kande skall: Ha l\u00e4gst filosofie kandidatexamen i relevant \u00e4mne f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten. Ha studieadministrativ erfarenhet och mycket god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga. Goda kunskaper i talad och skriven svenska och engelska \u00e4r en f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttning. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Kunskaper om och i \u00e4mnet M\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter \u00e4r meriterande, liksom erfarenhet av tidigare studiev\u00e4gledararbete inom humaniora och/eller samh\u00e4llsvetenskap. Kunskaper i de administrativa systemen Ladok, NyA, SoleMove och Canvas \u00e4r meriterande. En stor del av arbetet handlar om personliga kontakter med studenter varf\u00f6r den personliga l\u00e4mpligheten hos den s\u00f6kande v\u00e4rderas h\u00f6gt. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en vikariatsanst\u00e4llning som studiev\u00e4gledare p\u00e5 100 % med startdatum 2027-02-15 (eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse), dock l\u00e4ngst till och med 2028-02-28. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev om maximalt en sida med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis, lista \u00f6ver handlingar som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa samt kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser rekommendationsbrev etc. V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Om Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna har sju institutioner och bedriver en stor och varierad verksamhet inom forskning och utbildning. Vi har ca 700 anst\u00e4llda och ca 4 000 hel\u00e5rsstudenter. Om Historiska institutionen Historiska institutionen utg\u00f6r en av sju institutioner vid Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna. Den \u00e4r en stor institution med tre avdelningar: avdelningen f\u00f6r historia, avdelningen f\u00f6r m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter och Centrum f\u00f6r \u00d6st- och Syd\u00f6stasienstudier. H\u00e4r finns runt 100 l\u00e4rare och forskare. Inom institutionen bedrivs undervisning f\u00f6retr\u00e4desvis inom ramen f\u00f6r kandidatprogram i historia respektive m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter, masterprogram i historia samt internationella masterprogram i m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter respektive Asienstudier. Institutionen har ocks\u00e5 en stor forskarutbildning med doktorander i historia, m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter och \u00d6st- och Syd\u00f6stasienstudier bland annat genom en forskarskola i historiska studier. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2028-02-28 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-02-15 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2916 Kontakt Lina Sturfelt, Prefekt, 0462220000, lina.sturfelt@hist.lu.se Anna Nilsson Hammar, Bitr. Prefekt, 0462220000, anna.nilsson_hammar@hist.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-12 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-01 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:978010/": {"title": "Postdoctoral position in societal aspects of copyright and AI", "description": "Postdoctoral position in societal aspects of copyright and AI Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral position in societal aspects of copyright and AI Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace This two-year postdoc will be part of the Nordforsk research project COPY.AI, which is co-ordinated by the Norwegian Computing Centre. The aim of the project is to in cross-university and cross-disciplinary collaboration investigate the\u202ffuture of intellectual property\u202fin the light of current developments within generative AI. This postdoc will primarily work in the research group for AI and society led by Stefan Larsson at LTH in Lund. The group focuses on social science-oriented but multidisciplinary issues linked to AI. The group collaborates e.g. over several faculties, including medicine, law, the social sciences and the humanities, as well as with research environments in for example Finland, Brazil, Italy and Japan. Subject description The subject Technology and Society encompasses multi- and interdisciplinary studies on the role, interaction, regulation and significance of technology within society. This project deals with societal aspects in the intersection of copyright and AI model development. Work duties The main duties involved in a post-doctoral position is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position includes the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. The purpose of the position is to develop the independence as a researcher and to create the opportunity of further development. You will explore socio-legal aspects in the intersection of copyright and AI-model training. You will arrange workshops with legal and technical expertise where both legal and social norms are addressed around aspects of authorship, intellectual property, various impacts of large language model (LLM) development and deployments have on both law and society, on creative practices and their markets. You will design and co-author sub-studies jointly with primarily the research group at Lund University, but potentially also with scholars in the larger project group. The study can for example focus on: how model training on copyrighted content could or should be conceptualised with regards to possible or probable futures, including aspects of compensation; what level or type of transparency could be beneficial for AI model training and deployment from an authorship or copyright perspective. This could but does not have to include: studies of the development of a Swedish language model (SE.LLMA), including aspects of transparency, opt-out mechanisms, and how compensation may be balanced or distributed among or to copyright holders, following and analysing aspects of the US-oriented model development and connected court cases, for example the Anthropic Class Action Settlement, in terms of implications for a Nordic and Baltic context. Methodologically, the broad range of social scientific tools can be utilised, from the exploratory workshops to various qualitative or quantitative and legal analysis. The position may include some travels, primarily related to the Nordic collaboration, but also offer the opportunity to attend international conferences more broadly. Detailed description of the work duties: Conducting research in the research group connected to the project. Arranging workshops, analysing cases and writing scientific papers. Some teaching at the department. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position. The certificate proving the qualification requirement is met, must be received before the employment decision is made. Priority will be given to candidates who have graduated no more than three years ago before the last day for application. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: A PhD degree in a relevant social science discipline, for example sociology of law, science and technology studies, media and communication studies or other interdisciplinary combinations relevant for the intersection of AI, law and society. Very good oral and written proficiency in English. You can both work independently and have the ability to collaborate. You are structured and persistent. You have experience of research or studies in the intersection of new technologies \u2013 for example AI in terms of LLM \u2013 and social or societal concerns. You have experience of empirical studies, primarily qualitative. You have basic knowledge of intellectual property and copyright law. Assessment criteria This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high quality research. Teaching skills. Other qualifications: Basic understanding of the training of large language models (LLMs). Experience of teaching in higher education. Experience in arts, music or other creative expressions. Consideration will also be given to how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee. Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 2 years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d). Start in January 2027 or by agreement. How to apply Applications are to be written in English and submitted via the University\u2019s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. As part of the assessment we ask candidates to submit a proposal of a potential study plan, inspired by this call, on about 2 pages. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.). We welcome your application! About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 1 January 2027 or by agreement Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2926 Contact Stefan Larsson, associate professor, stefan.larsson@lth.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 12.Oct.2026 Last application date 09.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:978053/": {"title": "Projektassistent vid Ber\u00e4kningskemi", "description": "Projektassistent vid Ber\u00e4kningskemi Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Projektassistent vid Ber\u00e4kningskemi Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Arbetsuppgifter Som projektassistent kommer du att medverka i ett forskningsprojekt med fokus p\u00e5 utveckling av harmoniserade och reproducerbara analysarbetsfl\u00f6den f\u00f6r BioSAXS. Arbetet omfattar analys och j\u00e4mf\u00f6relse av experimentella data fr\u00e5n laboratoriebaserad SAXS-utrustning samt synkrotron- och neutronbaserade m\u00e4tningar. Arbetsuppgifterna innefattar bland annat att: Delta i planering och genomf\u00f6rande av spridningsexperiment vid Lunds universitet samt vid nationella och internationella forskningsinfrastrukturer, s\u00e5som MAX IV, ESRF, ILL och ISA med m\u00f6jlighet till resor i samband med m\u00e4tningar. bearbeta, kvalitetss\u00e4kra och analysera experimentella SAXS-data med etablerade analysprogram och Python-baserade verktyg. utveckla och dokumentera reproducerbara analysarbetsfl\u00f6den i Python/Jupyter. genomf\u00f6ra j\u00e4mf\u00f6rande analyser av data fr\u00e5n olika instrument och forskningsanl\u00e4ggningar f\u00f6r att identifiera systematiska skillnader och bidra till harmoniserade analysmetoder. medverka i utvecklingen av rekommendationer f\u00f6r kvalitetskontroll, dataanalys och visualisering. bidra till dokumentation, utbildningsmaterial och anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d inom projektet. samarbeta med forskare och experter vid Lunds universitet samt nationella och internationella forskningsinfrastrukturer. Arbetet bedrivs i n\u00e4ra samarbete med projektets forskargrupp och internationella samarbetspartners och ger m\u00f6jlighet att bidra till utvecklingen av framtida metoder f\u00f6r integrerad analys av spridningsdata fr\u00e5n b\u00e5de r\u00f6ntgen- och neutronbaserade forskningsanl\u00e4ggningar. Krav Masterexamen i kemi, fysik, biofysik, strukturbiologi, bioteknik eller annat n\u00e4rliggande naturvetenskapligt omr\u00e5de. Goda kunskaper i Python eller annat relevant programmeringsspr\u00e5k f\u00f6r vetenskaplig dataanalys. God f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka sig i tal och skrift p\u00e5 svenska och engelska. God samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga samt f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt och strukturerat. F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att planera, dokumentera och genomf\u00f6ra arbetsuppgifter med h\u00f6g noggrannhet. \u00d6vriga meriter: Erfarenhet av l\u00e5gvinkelspridning (SAXS och/eller SANS). Erfarenhet av analys av biologiska spridningsdata. Erfarenhet av Python-baserade analysmilj\u00f6er, exempelvis Jupyter Notebook. Dokumenterad f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att utveckla reproducerbara analysarbetsfl\u00f6den av biologisk spridningsdata. Erfarenhet av arbete vid synkrotron- eller neutronanl\u00e4ggningar. Erfarenhet av vetenskaplig programmering och utveckling av reproducerbara analysarbetsfl\u00f6den. Erfarenhet av dokumentation, anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d eller utveckling av utbildningsmaterial. Intresse f\u00f6r utveckling av forskningsinfrastruktur och tv\u00e4rvetenskapliga samarbeten. Vi kommer att l\u00e4gga stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. H\u00e4nsyn kommer att tas till god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, driv och sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndighet samt hur den s\u00f6kande genom sin erfarenhet och kompetens bed\u00f6ms komplettera och st\u00e4rka det arbetet inom avdelningen samt bidra till dess framtida utveckling. Villkor Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning med startdatum 2027-01-01 till och med 2027-07-31. Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning, heltid. Instruktioner f\u00f6r ans\u00f6kan Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.). Vid Naturvetenskapliga fakulteten bedrivs forskning och utbildning inom astronomi, biologi fysik, geovetenskap, kemi, matematik, medicinsk str\u00e5lningsfysik, milj\u00f6vetenskap och naturgeografi. Verksamheten bedrivs inom norra universitetsomr\u00e5det. Fakulteten har ca 1 900 studenter, 330 forskarstuderande och 730 anst\u00e4llda. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-01 L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2927 Kontakt Marie Skep\u00f6, +46462223366, marie.skepo@chem.lu.se Jessica Edwinsson, jessica.edwinsson@chem.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-12 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:978127/": {"title": "Systemspecialist inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det", "description": "Systemspecialist inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Systemspecialist inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Systemspecialist inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det Vi s\u00f6ker dig som kombinerar ett intresse f\u00f6r system och digitalisering med f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att samordna utvecklingsarbete och skapa effektiva arbetss\u00e4tt. Hos oss f\u00e5r du en central roll i arbetet med att utveckla systemst\u00f6d, processer och samverkan inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det. Du \u00e4r en person som tycker om att skapa struktur, driva utveckling och f\u00e5 olika intressenter att arbeta mot gemensamma m\u00e5l. Du har f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att se b\u00e5de helhet och detaljer och kan oms\u00e4tta verksamhetens behov till effektiva processer och \u00e4ndam\u00e5lsenliga systemst\u00f6d. Rollen inneb\u00e4r m\u00e5nga kontaktytor, vilket kr\u00e4ver god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga samt f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att bygga f\u00f6rtroendefulla relationer. Du blir en del av ett team som ansvarar f\u00f6r systemf\u00f6rvaltning, verksamhetsutveckling och anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det och som arbetar n\u00e4ra verksamheten f\u00f6r att utveckla effektiva arbetss\u00e4tt och systemst\u00f6d. Arbetsuppgifter Du arbetar b\u00e5de strategiskt och operativt med att utveckla processer, arbetss\u00e4tt och systemst\u00f6d. Rollen inneb\u00e4r att du samordnar utvecklingsinitiativ, skapar samsyn mellan olika intressenter och s\u00e4kerst\u00e4ller att systemen ger b\u00e4sta m\u00f6jliga st\u00f6d till verksamheten. Dina arbetsuppgifter omfattar bland annat att: F\u00f6rvalta och utveckla systemst\u00f6d inom ink\u00f6ps- och ekonomiomr\u00e5det. Samordna och leda utvecklingsinitiativ som involverar flera avdelningar, funktioner och intressenter. Analysera verksamhetens behov och oms\u00e4tta dem till krav p\u00e5 processer och system. Medverka i kravst\u00e4llning i upphandlingar av system och tj\u00e4nster. Planera och genomf\u00f6ra tester vid f\u00f6r\u00e4ndringar och systemuppgraderingar. Ta fram anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d, v\u00e4gledningar och utbildningsinsatser. Ge st\u00f6d till anv\u00e4ndare och bidra till ett kontinuerligt f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttringsarbete. Kvalifikationer Krav H\u00f6gskoleutbildning inom ekonomi, ink\u00f6p, logistik, systemvetenskap eller annat relevant omr\u00e5de, alternativt motsvarande kunskaper och erfarenheter som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer likv\u00e4rdiga. Erfarenhet av systemf\u00f6rvaltning eller motsvarande arbete med utveckling och f\u00f6rvaltning av verksamhetssystem. Erfarenhet av ekonomi- och/eller ink\u00f6psadministrativa processer. Erfarenhet av att driva och samordna arbete \u00f6ver organisatoriska gr\u00e4nser. Mycket god kommunikativ och pedagogisk f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga. Mycket god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka dig p\u00e5 svenska i tal och skrift. Meriterande Erfarenhet av att analysera verksamhetsbehov, samordna utvecklingsinsatser och oms\u00e4tta behov till effektiva processer och systeml\u00f6sningar. Erfarenhet av kravhantering, testarbete och projektledning. Erfarenhet av arbete med ink\u00f6psprocesser och tillh\u00f6rande systemst\u00f6d samt god f\u00f6rst\u00e5else f\u00f6r samspelet mellan e-handel, avtal och upphandling. Erfarenhet av arbete enligt f\u00f6rvaltningsmodeller s\u00e5som pm3. Kunskap om offentlig upphandling. Personliga egenskaper Vi s\u00f6ker dig som har ett stort intresse f\u00f6r hur system och digitala l\u00f6sningar kan st\u00f6dja verksamhetens behov. Du \u00e4r analytisk, strukturerad och har f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att se b\u00e5de helhet och detaljer. Du trivs i en roll med m\u00e5nga kontaktytor och har l\u00e4tt f\u00f6r att skapa goda samarbeten. Eftersom rollen inneb\u00e4r att h\u00e5lla samman arbete mellan flera funktioner beh\u00f6ver du vara kommunikativ, initiativrik och ha f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att driva fr\u00e5gor fram\u00e5t. Du har f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att skapa engagemang och f\u00e5 m\u00e4nniskor med olika perspektiv att arbeta mot gemensamma m\u00e5l. Vidare \u00e4r du pedagogisk och tycker om att oms\u00e4tta komplex information till praktiska och anv\u00e4ndarv\u00e4nliga l\u00f6sningar. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats, Jobba hos oss . Som anst\u00e4lld p\u00e5 sektionen Ekonomi f\u00e5r du en central roll i utvecklingen av organisationens ekonomiadministrativa st\u00f6d. Du arbetar i en milj\u00f6 d\u00e4r ekonomi, verksamhet och system m\u00f6ts och d\u00e4r du har m\u00f6jlighet att p\u00e5verka b\u00e5de processer, arbetss\u00e4tt och systeml\u00f6sningar. Rollen erbjuder stort utrymme att p\u00e5verka utvecklingen av b\u00e5de processer och systemst\u00f6d samt att f\u00f6rdjupa din kompetens inom systemf\u00f6rvaltning, verksamhetsutveckling och digitalisering. \u00d6vrigt Tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r en tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning med start s\u00e5 snart som m\u00f6jligt eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Provanst\u00e4llning kan komma att till\u00e4mpas. Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla ett personligt brev d\u00e4r du beskriver hur du uppfyller kvalifikationskraven och varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen samt ett CV. Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av examen, betyg, intyg, rekommendationsbrev, uppgifter till referenser etc). Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Sektionen Ekonomis huvuduppgift \u00e4r att ge verksamheten vid Lunds universitet st\u00f6d f\u00f6r en rationell ekonomiadministrativ hantering och tillgodose behoven av h\u00f6gkvalitativ ekonomisk information f\u00f6r att underl\u00e4tta beslutsfattande inom och utanf\u00f6r universitetet. Detta inneb\u00e4r bl.a. att sektion Ekonomi: ansvarar f\u00f6r universitetets ekonomimodell och redovisningssystem, ger institutionerna st\u00f6d i deras dagliga ekonomihantering, kvalitetskontrollerar bokf\u00f6ringen, samordnar bokslutsarbetet, rapporterar till myndigheter, tar fram ekonomiska sammanst\u00e4llningar som beh\u00f6vs f\u00f6r uppf\u00f6ljning och beslutsfattande, ger utbildning och information i ekonomiadministrativa fr\u00e5gor. Sektion Ekonomi ansvarar ocks\u00e5 f\u00f6r universitetets likviditetshantering, l\u00e5nehantering, r\u00e4nteber\u00e4kning samt stiftelse- och fondf\u00f6rvaltning. D\u00e4rut\u00f6ver bist\u00e5r sektion Ekonomi universitetet i upphandlings\u00e4renden med syfte att skapa f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r effektiv och rationell anskaffning. Avdelningen ink\u00f6p och upphandling handl\u00e4gger dessutom anslutningar kring e-fakturering och e-ink\u00f6p via Lupin, ett system f\u00f6r elektroniskt fakturafl\u00f6de och ink\u00f6p via webb-portal. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de Snarast m\u00f6jligt eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2930 Kontakt Filip Bengtsson, +46462228620, filip.bengtsson@eken.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-12 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-01 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:962298/": {"title": "Doctoral student in Technology and Society on regulatory learning and supervisory competence", "description": "Doctoral student in Technology and Society on regulatory learning and supervisory competence Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Technology and Society on regulatory learning and supervisory competence Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace This doctoral position is part of REGULAIRE, which is a MSCA doctoral pan-European network that studies how regulation can learn and adapt in situations where technologies, risks, and expectations change quickly. The network will train fifteen fellows to examine this learning process from different angles. They will look at how authorities detect early signals, design and test interventions, evaluate what works, and share findings across organisations. REGULAIRE stands for Regulatory Learning for the Governance of Transformative Technologies, and the consortium is led by Technical University Munich. The consortium includes technical universities, business schools, social and legal scientists, and public sector actors. This call is of a doctoral position at LTH, Lund University. The research group environment at LTH in Lund, led by Stefan Larsson, focuses on social science-oriented but multidisciplinary issues linked to AI, with affiliated researchers at both junior and senior levels. The research group has a working space at LTH and is part of the Department of Technology and Society. Read more about the research group on the Research Portal of Lund University . Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Subject and project description The doctoral subject Technology and Society encompasses multi- and interdisciplinary studies on the role, interaction, regulation and significance of technology within society. Research includes both qualitative and quantitative studies and is often characterized by a diversity of methods and theories. Regulatory flexibility helps law keep pace with fast-moving technologies, but law also needs predictable norms. This doctoral project studies how the two sit together, asking whether flexibilities, delegations, open-textured duties and codes of practice shift authority among legislators, the Commission, standardisers, private actors, and with a special attention to supervisory authorities. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. You will map supervisory competence, organisation and tooling in selected jurisdictions, using the AI Act to structure comparison, and combine document analysis, interviews and process tracing to link design choices to predictability for firms and protection for citizens. The work will from a critical perspective analyse flexibility mechanisms and their governance implications. It could be grounded in supervisory practice, comparative case reports and contribute to an assessment framework for supervisory capability. It will also translate evidence into guidance on aligning flexibility with foresight without eroding legal certainty, if possible. This project offers a focused route into socio-legal research, AI governance and the study of technology-oriented supervision. The employment will include a three-month intersectoral secondment in another country. The work duties include: Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team, and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Collect, manage and analyse research data using the approved project-specific methods. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the doctoral programme and the REGULAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, network reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement, including three residential summer schools and monthly paper development seminars. Undertake the planned three-month intersectoral secondment with a partner institution within REGULAIRE. The duties may also include participation in teaching and other departmental work (however, a maximum of 20% of working hours). Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Technology and Society if the applicant has: at least 30 credits awarded in the second cycle relevant to the subject area. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: An educational background in relevant field, for example law, socio-legal studies, political science, science and technology studies, or related social science and interdisciplinary fields. You take initiatives, are structured and persistent. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills Good ability to cooperate Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must also, on the first day of employment: not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning you must not have resided or carried out your main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Sweden for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: experience of qualitative methods, such as document analysis, interviews or process tracing. sociolegal knowledge on how society and law interacts. technological knowledge of emerging technologies. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se. About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting 1 January 2027 or by agreement, but no later than 1 June 2027. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. You will receive a monthly salary according to the regulations of the MSCA Grant Agreement. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staff pages. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment 1 January 2027, or by agreement, but no later than 1 June 2027 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2479 Contact Stefan Larsson, associate professor, stefan.larsson@lth.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 09.Oct.2026 Last application date 08.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974465/": {"title": "Studie- och karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledare vid fysiska institutionen, vikariat", "description": "Studie- och karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledare vid fysiska institutionen, vikariat Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Studie- och karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledare vid fysiska institutionen, vikariat Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Naturvetenskapliga fakulteten, Fysiska institutionen Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Vid fysiska institutionen, naturvetenskapliga fakulteten, har vi utbildningar p\u00e5 kandidat- och masterniv\u00e5 med sammanlagt ca 300 heltidsstudenter och n\u00e4rmare 50 l\u00e4rare. Utbildningarna t\u00e4cker ett brett spektrum av modern fysik och omfattar ca 80 kurser p\u00e5 kandidat- och masterniv\u00e5. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 http://www.fysik.lu.se/utbildning . Institutionens grundutbildningsgrupp best\u00e5r i dagsl\u00e4get av 5 personer som st\u00f6ttar studenter och l\u00e4rare med service inom bland annat studieadministration och kommunikation. Vi s\u00f6ker nu en vikarierande karri\u00e4r- och studiev\u00e4gledare p\u00e5 grund av en kommande f\u00f6r\u00e4ldraledighet. Arbetsuppgifter Som studie- och karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledare f\u00f6r kandidat- och masterutbildningarna i fysik arbetar du sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt samtidigt som du ing\u00e5r i ett arbetslag vid fysiska institutionen tillsammans med tv\u00e5 utbildningsadministrat\u00f6rer, forskningsingenj\u00f6rer, programkoordinatorer och studierektor som leder arbetet. I arbetet kommer du \u00e4ven att ha daglig kontakt med l\u00e4rare och studenter, s\u00e5v\u00e4l svenska som med internationell bakgrund. Din uppgift \u00e4r att introducera, st\u00f6dja och v\u00e4gleda studenterna, b\u00e5de individuellt och i grupp . Som studiev\u00e4gledare v\u00e4gleder du studenterna genom utbildningen, fr\u00e5n blivande student via examen till steget ut i arbetslivet. Du bedriver ut\u00e5triktad verksamhet samt representerar fysiska institutionens utbildningar i olika sammanhang. I arbetet ing\u00e5r \u00e4ven administrativa uppgifter s\u00e5som bed\u00f6mning av f\u00f6rkunskaper, antagning till och registrering p\u00e5 kurser, registrering och rapportering av resultat, information till studenter och l\u00e4rare och deltagande i m\u00f6ten med beredande organ. Arbetet \u00e4r komplext och f\u00f6ljer en \u00e5rscykel som inneb\u00e4r att m\u00e5nga till synes avgr\u00e4nsade delar h\u00e4nger samman, och hur de utf\u00f6rs har stor betydelse f\u00f6r helheten. Arbetet inneb\u00e4r myndighetsut\u00f6vning, i synnerhet de administrativa delarna som n\u00e4mns ovan. Arbetet inkluderar ocks\u00e5 hantering av k\u00e4nslig information om enskilda studenter vilket kr\u00e4ver stor integritet. Exempel p\u00e5 arbetsuppgifter som ing\u00e5r i rollen Arbeta med institutionens mottagning av nya studenter och utveckling av densamma, f\u00f6r att fr\u00e4mja en god studiemilj\u00f6. H\u00e5lla informationsm\u00f6ten f\u00f6r studenterna och ansvara f\u00f6r l\u00f6pande information via Canvas och andra kanaler, till exempel inf\u00f6r val av kurser, om ans\u00f6kningsfr\u00e5gor och CSN samt informera om allm\u00e4nna och programspecifika fr\u00e5gor. Hj\u00e4lpa studenter med praktiska fr\u00e5gor, som en del av den studieadministrativa gruppen . Kontinuerligt f\u00f6lja upp studenters resultat och kontakta studenter som \u00e4r p\u00e5 v\u00e4g att hamna efter i studierna. Genomf\u00f6ra enskild studiev\u00e4gledning och studieplanering f\u00f6r studenter p\u00e5 kandidat- och masterprogrammen och vid behov uppr\u00e4tta individuella studieplaner. Genomf\u00f6ra karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledning samt v\u00e4gledning vid studieuppeh\u00e5ll och avbrott. Genomf\u00f6ra enskild studieplanering f\u00f6r studenter och vara kontaktperson f\u00f6r Pedagogiskt st\u00f6d vid LU. Information till presumtiva studenter: arbete med rekryterings- och informationsmaterial, fr\u00e5n Lunds universitet, naturvetenskapliga fakulteten och institutionen samt att ta fram underlag till dessa och bedriva ut\u00e5triktad verksamhet (inspirationsdagar, utbildningsm\u00e4ssor, ta emot studiebes\u00f6k etc.). Samverka med fakultetens \u00f6vriga studiev\u00e4gledare (till exempel i studiev\u00e4gledarn\u00e4tverket). Administrativa uppgifter s\u00e5som bed\u00f6mning av f\u00f6rkunskaper, antagning till och registrering p\u00e5 kurser, registrering och rapportering av resultat. Adjungerad till institutionens grundutbildningsn\u00e4mnd och kandidat- och masterprogramr\u00e5d. Kvalifikationer f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen Vi s\u00f6ker dig som: Har studie- och yrkesv\u00e4gledarutbildning eller motsvarande arbetslivserfarenhet som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer likv\u00e4rdig Har arbetslivserfarenhet av studiev\u00e4gledning Har mycket goda kunskaper om och arbetslivserfarenhet av samtalsmetodik Har arbetslivserfarenhet av att h\u00e5lla informationssessioner och presentationer inf\u00f6r stora grupper Har mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska, b\u00e5de i tal och skrift Har god datorvana och \u00e4r van att arbeta med studieadministrativa system Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har: Erfarenhet av liknande arbete inom h\u00f6gskolev\u00e4rlden Erfarenhet av studieadministrativa system som NyA, Ladok, Canvas, TimeEdit Erfarenhet av arbete med unga vuxna Arbetet \u00e4r periodvis mycket intensivt, vilket f\u00f6ruts\u00e4tter god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att hantera och prioritera en stor m\u00e4ngd arbetsuppgifter. Du beh\u00f6ver ocks\u00e5 vara \u00f6ppen och flexibel, l\u00e4tt att samarbeta med och kunna arbeta b\u00e5de sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt och i grupp. Dessutom beh\u00f6ver du f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att hantera m\u00e5nga sociala kontakter och att kommunicera p\u00e5 ett tydligt och smidigt s\u00e4tt. Vi kommer l\u00e4gga stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. Vi s\u00f6ker en person som \u00e4r sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndig, initiativtagande, stabil, strukturerad och har god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga med stort ordningssinne och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att se st\u00f6rre sammanhang. H\u00e4nsyn kommer att tas till hur den s\u00f6kande genom sin erfarenhet och kompetens bed\u00f6ms komplettera och st\u00e4rka arbetslaget samt bidra till dess framtida utveckling. Villkor Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning (vikariat) till och med 2028-01-31 med tilltr\u00e4de snarast eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Heltid 100 % . S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla CV och personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc). V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Vid Naturvetenskapliga fakulteten bedrivs forskning och utbildning inom astronomi, biologi fysik, geovetenskap, kemi, matematik, medicinsk str\u00e5lningsfysik, milj\u00f6vetenskap och naturgeografi. Verksamheten bedrivs inom norra universitetsomr\u00e5det. Fakulteten har ca 1 900 studenter, 330 forskarstuderande och 730 anst\u00e4llda. Fysiska institutionen \u00e4r en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta institutioner med cirka 400 anst\u00e4llda. Institutionen \u00e4r gemensam f\u00f6r naturvetenskaplig och teknisk (LTH) fakultet. Vid institutionen finns sju forskningsavdelningar och ett antal st\u00f6rre forskningscentra. Forskningen vid institutionen omfattar ett brett spektrum av modern fysik. www.fysik.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de snarast L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2839 Kontakt Martin Magnusson, studierektor, +46462224110, martin.magnusson@fysik.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-09 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-31 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975818/": {"title": "Eventansvarig Projektledare", "description": "Eventansvarig Projektledare Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Eventansvarig Projektledare Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. LU Innovation \u00e4r Lunds universitets innovationsavdelning. V\u00e5r uppgift \u00e4r att se till att kunskap och forskningsresultat fr\u00e5n hela universitetet kommer samh\u00e4llet till nytta. Det g\u00f6r vi genom att verka f\u00f6r en innovativ kultur, inspirera till innovation och etablera samarbeten med externa parter. Men framf\u00f6r allt hj\u00e4lper vi studenter och forskare vid universitetet att omvandla id\u00e9er och forskningsresultat till nya h\u00e5llbara produkter, tj\u00e4nster eller metoder. Tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r placerad vid avdelningen LU Innovation som har ca 20 medarbetare och \u00e4r en del av sektionen Forskning, samverkan och innovation. H\u00e5llbarhet, j\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet och lika villkor \u00e4r av st\u00f6rsta vikt f\u00f6r LU Innovation. H\u00e4r arbetar vi med korta beslutsv\u00e4gar, flexibla arbetsf\u00f6rh\u00e5llanden och frihet under ansvar. Universitetets bredd g\u00f6r att v\u00e5rt team best\u00e5r av en m\u00e4ngd kompetenser och erfarenheter som arbetar tillsammans f\u00f6r att fr\u00e4mja innovation vid universitetet. Vi s\u00f6ker nu en eventansvarig som kan st\u00e4rka avdelningens marknadsf\u00f6ringsarbete i f\u00f6rsta hand mot universitetets student- och forskningsmilj\u00f6er, men i viss m\u00e5n ocks\u00e5 externt. Du tar dig an hela eventrollen och tycker det \u00e4r givande \u2013 allt fr\u00e5n att rigga m\u00e4ssplats till att utveckla nya koncept f\u00f6r att skapa intresse bland m\u00e5lgrupper. Du ser eventverksamheten som ett strategiskt verktyg f\u00f6r att uppn\u00e5 organisationens m\u00e5l, och du arbetar strukturerat tillsammans med medarbetarna f\u00f6r att n\u00e5 dit. Ditt fr\u00e4msta fokus kommer vara att via en stark eventverksamhet \u00f6ka synligheten av v\u00e5r verksamhet p\u00e5 universitetet och att bidra till att innovationsid\u00e9er kommer in fr\u00e5n universitetets studenter, forskare och anst\u00e4llda. Vi ser att samarbete mellan olika funktioner i v\u00e5r verksamhet \u00e4r nyckeln till att n\u00e5 v\u00e5ra m\u00e5l, vilket g\u00f6r att vi just nu arbetar f\u00f6r att st\u00e4rka en prestigel\u00f6s och teamorienterad kultur. I tj\u00e4nsten som eventansvarig \u00e4r d\u00e4rf\u00f6r samarbete med LU Innovations kommunikationsstrateg, avdelningens innovationsutvecklare, inkubatoransvarig och det \u00f6vriga teamet p\u00e5 LU Innovation avg\u00f6rande f\u00f6r att lyckas. Arbetsuppgifter Verka f\u00f6r att \u00f6ka LU Innovations synlighet p\u00e5 Lunds universitet genom att planera och utf\u00f6ra engagerande aktiviteter och event f\u00f6r att \u00f6ka antalet forskare och studenter som s\u00f6ker sig till LU Innovation. Utveckla eventverksamheten f\u00f6r olika m\u00e5lgrupper vid Lunds universitet f\u00f6r att n\u00e5 LU Innovations m\u00e5l. Koordinera, projektleda och utf\u00f6ra event i egen regi, men \u00e4ven tillsammans med kollegor och samarbetspartners. Ansvara f\u00f6r avdelningens planering av kommunikationsaktiviteter relaterade till event. Utveckla nya strategiska v\u00e4gar f\u00f6r att \u00f6ka intresset f\u00f6r innovation hos identifierade m\u00e5lgrupper vid universitetet. Planera och producera eventmaterial (trycksaker, nyhetsbrev med mera) och inneh\u00e5ll f\u00f6r interna och externa kanaler (sociala medier och LU Innovations webbplats med mera). Rekrytera och projektleda studentmedarbetare f\u00f6r att st\u00f6dja verksamheten kring event. Hantera budget f\u00f6r event och inspirationsaktiviteter. Skapa och v\u00e5rda relationer med samarbetspartners, samt andra nyckelpersoner som t.ex. l\u00e4rare vid olika fakulteter, forskningsgrupper p\u00e5 universitetet och studentorganisationer. Utveckla koncept f\u00f6r design och marknadsf\u00f6ringsmaterial relaterat till event, samt medverka till att \u00f6ka intresset via v\u00e5ra digitala kanaler. Presentera LU Innovations erbjudande och leda olika typer av event, s\u00e5som workshops. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Minst en kandidatexamen inom relevant omr\u00e5de som inte \u00e4r \u00e4ldre \u00e4n 5 \u00e5r. Minst 2 \u00e5rs erfarenhet i en liknande roll. Goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska, b\u00e5de muntligt och skriftligt. Erfarenhet av att driva projekt med budgetansvar och att koordinera gruppaktiviteter Erfarenhet av att p\u00e5 ett inkluderande och strukturerat s\u00e4tt leda och genomf\u00f6ra olika typer av event. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen: Kunskaper i grafisk design och layout samt marknadsf\u00f6ring. K\u00e4nnedom om hur universitetsv\u00e4rlden fungerar. Vana vid att tala inf\u00f6r m\u00e5nga \u00e5h\u00f6rare och att etablera nya kontakter. Erfarenhet av att planera och driva st\u00f6rre event. Intresse f\u00f6r innovation och entrepren\u00f6rskap. Personliga egenskaper Du \u00e4r en driven och ansvarsfull person som kan hantera parallella projekt och gillar att ligga steget f\u00f6re. Du har god struktur i ditt arbete och trivs med att projektleda andra. Du \u00e4r samarbetsvillig och nyfiken av naturen. Du \u00e4r l\u00f6sningsorienterad och flexibel, och hugger g\u00e4rna i d\u00e4r det beh\u00f6vs . \u00d6vrigt Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Provanst\u00e4llning kan bli aktuellt. Thomas Rundqvist finns tillg\u00e4nglig f\u00f6r fr\u00e5gor under perioden 8 oktober - 14 oktober. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de Snarast eller efter \u00f6verenskommelse. L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100% Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2881 Kontakt Thomas Rundqvist, Tf avdelningschef, +46462221266, thomas.rundqvist@innovation.lu.se Niclas Nilsson, Avdelningschef, +46462221551, niclas.nilsson@innovation.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-09 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-01 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975905/": {"title": "Projektassistent vid Milj\u00f6 och geovetenskapliga institutionen", "description": "Projektassistent vid Milj\u00f6 och geovetenskapliga institutionen Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Projektassistent vid Milj\u00f6 och geovetenskapliga institutionen Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Forskning och utbildning vid Milj\u00f6- och geovetenskapliga institutionen (MGeo) behandlar grundl\u00e4ggande och till\u00e4mpade fr\u00e5gor om jordens tidigare, nuvarande och framtida klimat och milj\u00f6, inklusive m\u00e4nniskors interaktion med naturen och konsekvenser f\u00f6r m\u00e4nniskors v\u00e4lbefinnande. MGeo utvecklar och till\u00e4mpar banbrytande metoder, modeller och tekniker inom milj\u00f6vetenskap, kvart\u00e4r- och berggrundsgeologi, paleontologi, naturgeografi, biodiversitet och ekosystemvetenskap, fj\u00e4rranalys, geografisk informationsvetenskap (GIS) och ber\u00e4kningsvetenskap inom milj\u00f6- och h\u00e4lsa f\u00f6r att studera processer som str\u00e4cker sig fr\u00e5n det mikroskopiska till det planet\u00e4ra, \u00f6ver alla tidsskalor. Tr\u00e4dringar ger ett direkt observationsf\u00f6nster om hur skogstillv\u00e4xten svarar p\u00e5 klimatvariationer, men vegetationsmodeller saknar f\u00f6r n\u00e4rvarande rumsligt kontinuerliga benchmarkingprodukter f\u00f6r att utv\u00e4rdera deras simulerade tillv\u00e4xtssvar. Denna anst\u00e4llningen kommer att fokusera p\u00e5 detta problem. Arbetsuppgifter Kandidaten kommer att utveckla en rumsligt kontinuerlig, klimatinformerad tillv\u00e4xts\u00f6kningsprodukt h\u00e4rledd fr\u00e5n tr\u00e4dringsdata och interpolerad \u00f6ver rum och tid, och leda publiceringen av denna produkt i en vetenskaplig publikation. Tr\u00e4ringsdata \u00e4r r\u00e5data och m\u00e5ste\u00a0 d\u00e4rmed behandlas p\u00e5 en l\u00e4mpligt s\u00e4tt f\u00f6r att anv\u00e4ndas som tillv\u00e4xt\u00f6kningsprodukt. Klimatdata ska laddas ned, kontrolleras f\u00f6r kvalitet och transformeras f\u00f6r att vara l\u00e4mplig f\u00f6r projektet. Kandidaten kommer att skapa en lista \u00f6ver och montera f\u00f6rmentiva variabler s\u00e5som ekoregioner, arter, satellitdata, jordtyper, bland annat (tbd). F\u00f6r att kombinera tr\u00e4ring- och klimatdata, samt interpolera dem, ska maskininl\u00e4rningsbaserade metoder utforskas och anv\u00e4ndas tillsammans med enklare statistiska metoder. Kandidaten kommer att utarbeta en rapport och dokumentera codebase om de slutliga modellresultaten. Krav Utbildning: Masterexamen i ber\u00e4kningsvetenskap, klimat vetenskap eller ekosystem vetenskap Mycket goda muntliga och skriftliga kunskaper i engelska. Dokumenterad erfarenhet av att arbeta med tr\u00e4dringsdata, inklusive rensning, trendanalys, kronologisk konstruktion och j\u00e4mf\u00f6relse med milj\u00f6data Dokumenterade f\u00e4rdigheter i efterbehandling av stora klimatdata och kvalitetskontroll. Dokumenterad erfarenhet av maskininl\u00e4rningstekniker f\u00f6r rumslig interpolering F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att till\u00e4mpa minst ett tredje generationens programmeringsspr\u00e5k (t.ex. R, Python) \u00d6vriga meriter: F\u00f6rst\u00e5else av tr\u00e4dv\u00e4xtmekanismer och skogsekologi. Tonvikt kommer att l\u00e4ggas p\u00e5 f\u00e4rdigheter som \u00e4r relevanta f\u00f6r att uppn\u00e5 projektets m\u00e5l och f\u00f6rm\u00e5gan att producera resultat fr\u00e5n tidigare projekt. Vi kommer att l\u00e4gga stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. H\u00e4nsyn kommer att tas till god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att utf\u00f6ra forskning sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt och agera p\u00e5 eget initiativ. F\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r det viktigt att ha starka organisatoriska f\u00f6rm\u00e5gor s\u00e5 som tidshantering. Villkor S\u00e4rskild visstidsanst\u00e4llning (S\u00c4VA) med \u00f6nskad start 2026-11-09 och d\u00e4refter 4 m\u00e5naders arbete med planerat slutdatum 2027-03-07. Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning, 50% av heltid. Instruktioner f\u00f6r ans\u00f6kan Ans\u00f6kningar ska vara skrivna p\u00e5 engelska och sammanst\u00e4llas i en PDF-fil inneh\u00e5llande: ett ans\u00f6kningsbrev som beskriver din motivation och l\u00e4mplighet f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten, med exempel p\u00e5 varje kr\u00e4vande kriterium (h\u00f6gst en sida!) CV, inklusive en publikationslista om till\u00e4mpligt kontaktuppgifter till minst tv\u00e5 referenser kopior av certifikat/betyg som du \u00f6nskar bli beaktade V\u00e4lkommen att ans\u00f6ka! Vid Naturvetenskapliga fakulteten bedrivs forskning och utbildning inom astronomi, biologi fysik, geovetenskap, kemi, matematik, medicinsk str\u00e5lningsfysik, milj\u00f6vetenskap och naturgeografi. Verksamheten bedrivs inom norra universitetsomr\u00e5det. Fakulteten har ca 1 900 studenter, 330 forskarstuderande och 730 anst\u00e4llda. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform S\u00e4rskild visstidsanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2027-03-07 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2026-11-09 eller enl \u00f6k. L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 50 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2886 Kontakt Annemarie Eckes-Shephard, +46462224019, annemarie.eckes-shephard@mgeo.lu.se Stefan Olin, 046-2227200, stefan.olin@mgeo.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-09 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-23 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:976840/": {"title": "Projektassistent i tum\u00f6rbiologi", "description": "Projektassistent i tum\u00f6rbiologi Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Projektassistent i tum\u00f6rbiologi Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Medicinska fakulteten, Inst f\u00f6r laboratoriemedicin Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Forskargruppen, ledd av universitetslektor Charlotte Rolny, bedriver experimentell och translationell forskning Vi \u00e4r en del av Lund University Cancer Centre vid Medicon Village och tillh\u00f6r enheten f\u00f6r translationell cancerforskning vid Institutionen f\u00f6r laboratoriemedicin. Vi s\u00f6ker nu en projektassistent som kan analysera avancerad fl\u00f6descytometri\u00a0 samt. Bildanalys p\u00e5 tum\u00f6rprover. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss Jobba hos oss Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Du kommer att arbeta med analys och tolkning av komplexa dataset inom fl\u00f6descytometri och imaging samt bidra till vetenskaplig rapportering och manuskriptskrivande. Du kommer ha s\u00e4rskilt ansvar f\u00f6r att: analysera och kvalitetss\u00e4kra komplexa fl\u00f6descytometriska dataset analysera och tolka bilddata fr\u00e5n avancerade bildbaserade metoder utveckla och till\u00e4mpa l\u00e4mpliga analysstrategier f\u00f6r multidimensionella biologiska data bidra till biologisk och statistisk tolkning av resultat sammanst\u00e4lla och visualisera data f\u00f6r vetenskapliga presentationer och publikationer bidra till manuskriptskrivande, inklusive resultatbeskrivning, metodavsnitt och vetenskaplig diskussion samarbeta med forskare kring analysstrategi, datatolkning och vetenskaplig kommunikation Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Du har doktorsexamen inom medicinsk vetenskap, biomedicin, immunologi, cellbiologi eller annat relevant omr\u00e5de. Du har dokumenterad erfarenhet av avancerad fl\u00f6descytometrisk dataanalys styrkt genom vetenskapliga publikationer. Du har dokumenterad erfarenhet inom translationell reglering av genuttryck i tum\u00f6rmikromilj\u00f6n, med s\u00e4rskilt fokus p\u00e5 signaleringsv\u00e4gen MNK1/2\u2013eIF4E, styrkt genom vetenskapliga publikationer. Du har dokumenterad erfarenhet av interaktioner mellan immunceller, fibroblaster och tum\u00f6rceller i tum\u00f6rmikromilj\u00f6n, styrkt genom vetenskapliga publikationer. Du har erfarenhet av analys av komplexa biologiska dataset. Du har erfarenhet av vetenskapligt skrivande och medverkan i vetenskapliga publikationer. Du har god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt tolka och kritiskt granska experimentella data. Du kan kommunicera vetenskapliga resultat tydligt p\u00e5 engelska i tal och skrift. Du har god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och kan arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt med flera parallella projekt. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av spektral eller avancerad multiparameterfl\u00f6descytometri. Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av avancerad och kvantitativ bildanalys. Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av analysverktyg s\u00e5som FlowJo, R, GraphPad Prism eller motsvarande. Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av tum\u00f6rimmunologi, immunologi eller stamcellsbiologi. Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av att integrera resultat fr\u00e5n flera experimentella metoder i en sammanh\u00e5llen biologisk analys. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en tidsbegr\u00e4nsad S\u00c4VA 4 m\u00e5nader p\u00e5 heltid med tilltr\u00e4de 2026-11-02 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV och examensbevis. Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Medicinska fakulteten \u00e4r ett verksamhetsomr\u00e5de inom Lunds universitet, med ansvar f\u00f6r utbildning och forskning inom medicin, v\u00e5rd och h\u00e4lsa. Utbildningen sker i n\u00e4ra samverkan med sjukv\u00e5rden och \u00e4r v\u00e4l f\u00f6rankrad i fakultetens starka forskningstradition. Fakultetens forskning sp\u00e4nner \u00f6ver ett brett f\u00e4lt inom experimentell grundforskning, patientn\u00e4ra klinisk forskning och h\u00e4lsovetenskaplig forskning. Medicinska fakulteten, med drygt 1800 anst\u00e4llda och 3000 studenter i Lund, Malm\u00f6 och Helsingborg, \u00e4r en kunskapsintensiv m\u00f6tesplats f\u00f6r studenter, l\u00e4rare och forskare fr\u00e5n hela v\u00e4rlden. Institutionen f\u00f6r laboratoriemedicin (ILM) \u00e4r en av sex institutioner vid Medicinska fakulteten. Vi bedriver ledande forskning inom det laboratoriemedicinska f\u00e4ltet med fokus p\u00e5 hur sjukdomar uppkommer och hur vi kan f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra patienters diagnostik och behandling. N\u00e5gra av v\u00e5ra starkaste omr\u00e5den med forskning i v\u00e4rldsklass, handlar om cancer-, genetik- och blodforskning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform S\u00e4rskild visstidsanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2026-11-02 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2901 Kontakt Charlotte Rolny, Rekryterande chef, 0462220000, charlotte.rolny@med.lu.se Adam Niekrasz, HR-partner, +46462220000, adam.niekrasz@med.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-09 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977183/": {"title": "Projektassistent vid Socialh\u00f6gskolan", "description": "Projektassistent vid Socialh\u00f6gskolan Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Projektassistent vid Socialh\u00f6gskolan Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten, Socialh\u00f6gskolan Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Socialh\u00f6gskolan \u00e4r en del av Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten och har utbildat studenter i socialt arbete sedan 1947. H\u00e4r arbetar omkring 100 medarbetare inom utbildning, forskning och verksamhetsst\u00f6d. Socionomutbildningen \u00e4r v\u00e5r st\u00f6rsta utbildning och har cirka 1 200 studenter. V\u00e5r forskning har fokus p\u00e5 bland annat sociala problem, utsatta gruppers levnadsvillkor, socialpolitik och m\u00e4nniskobehandlande organisationer och professioner. Beskrivning av projektet En ny betydelse av den tredje \u00e5ldern: Pension\u00e4rer som omsorgsgivare till sina f\u00f6r\u00e4ldrar i ett \"super\u00e5ldrat\" samh\u00e4lle. Den \u00f6kande livsl\u00e4ngden inneb\u00e4r att allt fler personer som sj\u00e4lva \u00e4r pension\u00e4rer har omsorgsansvar f\u00f6r \u00e4ldre f\u00f6r\u00e4ldrar eller sv\u00e4rf\u00f6r\u00e4ldrar. Projektet unders\u00f6ker denna v\u00e4xande form av informell omsorg och dess konsekvenser f\u00f6r familjerelationer och ansvarsf\u00f6rdelning mellan generationer. Projektet syftar till att generera ny kunskap och teori om betydelser av \u00e5ldrandet i ett f\u00f6r\u00e4nderligt samh\u00e4lle. Projektet leds av docent Tove Harnett. Medverkar g\u00f6r \u00e4ven professor H\u00e5kan J\u00f6nson och filosofie doktor Glenn M\u00f6llergren. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss Jobba hos oss . Arbetsuppgifter Insamling av data i form av intervjuer och enk\u00e4ter. Bearbetning av data samt projektadministration. Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen: \u2022 Socionomexamen eller motsvarande. \u2022 Erfarenhet av arbete i forskningsprojekt. \u2022 Eftersom datainsamling sker p\u00e5 svenska kr\u00e4vs mycket goda kunskaper i svenska i tal och skrift. \u2022 Eftersom arbetet bedrivs i n\u00e4ra samarbete med projektets medarbetare kr\u00e4vs h\u00f6g fysisk n\u00e4rvaro p\u00e5 arbetsplatsen. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen: \u2022 Erfarenhet av att anv\u00e4nda kvalitativa metoder f\u00f6r analys av data \u2022 Erfarenhet av att anv\u00e4nda statiska program f\u00f6r analys av data \u2022 B-k\u00f6rkort \u00d6vrigt Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som projektassistent p\u00e5 100 % i ett \u00e5r med f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntad start 1 februari 2027. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, eventuella publikationer, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.) Varmt v\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra f\u00f6r forskning och utbildning inom samh\u00e4lls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg, \u00f6ver 700 anst\u00e4llda och cirka 5 700 hel\u00e5rsstudenter \u00e4r fakulteten en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. V\u00e5r huvuduppgift \u00e4r att utveckla, f\u00f6rmedla och f\u00f6rvalta kunskap om samh\u00e4lle, m\u00e4nniska och organisationer i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av \u00f6ppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Vid Socialh\u00f6gskolan finns socionomprogrammet, h\u00e4lso- och sjukv\u00e5rdskuratorsprogrammet, grundl\u00e4ggande psykoterapiutbildning, frist\u00e5ende kurser, masterutbildning och en v\u00e4lutvecklad forskning inom det sociala arbetets centrala forskningsomr\u00e5den (se www.soch.lu.se). Socialh\u00f6gskolan bedriver verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 1 februari 2027 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2910 Kontakt Tove Harnett, Docent, tove.harnett@soch.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-09 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-15 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974541/": {"title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Eco-Evolutionary Microbiome and Thermal Biology", "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Eco-Evolutionary Microbiome and Thermal Biology Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher in Eco-Evolutionary Microbiome and Thermal Biology Login and apply Lunds universitet Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Subject description The position is part of the research project \u201cFrom Guts to Growth: Unravelling the Gut Microbiome\u2019s Role in Ontogenetic Trajectories toward Climate Stress Resilience\u201d (HOTGUT). The project investigates how environmental stress, the gut microbiome, and host physiology interact across early development to shape growth, metabolism, thermoregulation, and resilience to climate-induced thermal stress. The research uses wild great tits (Parus major) breeding in nest box populations and combines controlled field experiments with laboratory based microbiology, physiological measurements, and bioinformatic analyses. The successful candidate will take a leading operational role in planning, establishing, coordinating, and conducting the project\u2019s research activities. These include experiments on early-life thermal and hormonal stress, microbiome function transmission. The position therefore requires a highly independent researcher who is motivated by combining fieldwork and manipulative studies with laboratory analyses and data analyses. Work duties The main duty is to implement and coordinate research within HOTGUT in close collaboration with the principal investigator and project partners. The successful candidate will be expected to: \u2022 Plan, establish, coordinate, and conduct experimental studies in wild nest-box breeding passerines. \u2022 Collect and process biological samples, including faecal, oral, cloacal, blood, and environmental samples, and contribute to laboratory workflows for microbiome and physiological analyses. \u2022 Perform microbiome laboratory work, including DNA extraction, library preparation, quality control, and preparation for 16S rRNA amplicon sequencing. \u2022 Develop, maintain, and apply reproducible bioinformatic and statistical workflows. \u2022 Contribute to data analyses, \u00a0scientific publications, conference presentations, data and code management, open-science practices, and communication of results to scientific and wider audiences. Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the date of employment decision. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Applicants must have: \u2022 A PhD in evolutionary ecology, ecological physiology, microbiology, bioinformatics, ornithology, or another field relevant to the position. \u2022 Strong bioinformatic skills and experience with reproducible analysis of amplicon-sequencing data. \u2022 Strong quantitative skills, including advanced statistical analysis in R and experience with mixed-effects and multivariate models. \u2022 Very good oral and written proficiency in English. \u2022 A valid driving licence to be able to perform fieldwork. Assessment criteria and other qualifications This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. The following qualifications will be considered merits: \u2022 Experience of working with wild birds, particularly hole-nesting passerines, including bird handling, ringing, nest monitoring, blood sampling, or other relevant field procedures. \u2022 Experience with thermal-physiology methods such as respirometry and body temperature measurement. \u2022 Experience with endocrine, oxidative-stress, metabolomic, or other molecular and physiological analyses relevant to the project. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high quality research. Teaching skills. Particular emphasis will be placed on scientific maturity, independence, careful and controlled working practices, problem-solving ability, and the capacity to take responsibility for the practical implementation of the research programme. Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Terms of employment This is a fixed-term postdoctoral researcher position at 100% of full time for 2 years, starting on March 1st 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The position is based at the Department of Biology, Lund University, Sweden. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d) between Lund University, SACO-S and OFR/S, dated 1st February 2022. Fieldwork will be conducted primarily during the bird breeding season and may require flexible working hours during intensive experimental periods. Contact information Dr Katharina Ruthsatz, Principal Investigator: katharina.ruthsatz@biol.lu.se Dr Andreas Nord, Associate Professor: andreas.nord@biol.lu.se, +46 704 953 262 Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English and compiled into a single PDF file containing: \u2022 A cover letter describing the applicant\u2019s motivation and suitability for the position, \u2022 a curriculum vitae, including a complete publication list and details of relevant technical, field, laboratory, bioinformatic, teaching, and supervisory experience, \u2022 a brief description of previous research and how the applicant would contribute to the implementation of HOTGUT (maximum one DIN A4 page), \u2022 contact information for at least two academic references, and \u2022 a copy of the doctoral degree certificate and any other certificates or documentation the applicant wishes to be considered. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-03-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2841 Contact Katharina Ruthsatz, Forskare, katharina.ruthsatz@biol.lu.se Andreas Nord, Forskare, andreas.nord@biol.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 08.Oct.2026 Last application date 30.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977737/": {"title": "Kommunikat\u00f6r till Teaterh\u00f6gskolan och Konsth\u00f6gskolan (vikariat)", "description": "Kommunikat\u00f6r till Teaterh\u00f6gskolan och Konsth\u00f6gskolan (vikariat) Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Kommunikat\u00f6r till Teaterh\u00f6gskolan och Konsth\u00f6gskolan (vikariat) Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Vi s\u00f6ker nu en vikarierande kommunikat\u00f6r till Teaterh\u00f6gskolan och Konsth\u00f6gskolan i Malm\u00f6. Vikariatet \u00e4r tidsbegr\u00e4nsat till 11 m\u00e5nader. Teaterh\u00f6gskolan i Malm\u00f6 och Konsth\u00f6gskolan i Malm\u00f6 \u00e4r en del av Konstn\u00e4rliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet. B\u00e5da institutionerna \u00e4r bel\u00e4gna i Malm\u00f6 och erbjuder konstn\u00e4rlig utbildning och forskning i internationella milj\u00f6er. L\u00e4s g\u00e4rna mer om verksamheterna p\u00e5 v\u00e5r hemsida . Som kommunikat\u00f6r ing\u00e5r du i institutionernas tekniska och administrativa personal, och arbetar n\u00e4ra ledning, l\u00e4rare, forskare, studenter och administrativ personal. Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r delad lika mellan Teaterh\u00f6gskolan och Konsth\u00f6gskolan, och en mindre del inneb\u00e4r att ge st\u00f6d i fakultetens kommunikationsarbete. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Tj\u00e4nsten inneb\u00e4r huvudsakligen operativt arbete med institutionens interna och externa kommunikation. I arbetsuppgifterna ing\u00e5r utbildningsinformation, inneh\u00e5llsproduktion, webbredakt\u00f6rsarbete och kommunikationsst\u00f6d: Intern kommunikation till studenter och personal. Utbildningsinformation till presumtiva studenter. Inneh\u00e5ll f\u00f6r webb, nyhetsbrev och sociala medier. Webbpublicering och utveckling av digitala kanaler. Skriva texter p\u00e5 svenska och engelska. Kommunikation om f\u00f6rest\u00e4llningar, utst\u00e4llningar, evenemang, forskning och studentrekrytering. Kommunikationsst\u00f6d till ledning och verksamhet. Samverkan med kommunikat\u00f6rer inom fakulteten och universitetet. Planering, genomf\u00f6rande och uppf\u00f6ljning av kommunikationsinsatser. Synligg\u00f6ra Teater- och Konsth\u00f6gskolans utbildningar, forskning och verksamhet. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r H\u00f6gskoleexamen p\u00e5 l\u00e4gst kandidatniv\u00e5 (180 hp eller motsvarande) inom kommunikation, media eller annat omr\u00e5de som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer som likv\u00e4rdigt. F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt driva, prioritera och f\u00f6lja upp kommunikationsinsatser. Mycket god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka dig i tal och skrift p\u00e5 svenska och engelska. Erfarenhet av webbredakt\u00f6rsarbete och digital kommunikation. Erfarenhet av arbete med sociala medier. God f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att anpassa kommunikation till olika m\u00e5lgrupper. Personliga egenskaper som kr\u00e4vs f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r att du \u00e4r sj\u00e4lvg\u00e5ende, kreativ och strukturerad. Du beh\u00f6ver ocks\u00e5 ha en god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, vara lyh\u00f6rd f\u00f6r verksamhetens behov och trivas i en milj\u00f6 d\u00e4r m\u00e5nga olika aktiviteter p\u00e5g\u00e5r samtidigt. Du har l\u00e4tt f\u00f6r att skapa f\u00f6rtroende och oms\u00e4tta komplex information till tydlig och engagerande kommunikation. Meriterande \u00e4r Erfarenhet av kommunikationsarbete i offentlig verksamhet. Erfarenhet av kommunikation inom h\u00f6gskolesektorn. Kunskaper inom konst, kultur eller scenkonst. Erfarenhet av grafisk formgivning, bildhantering och enklare videoproduktion. Erfarenhet av studentrekrytering och marknadsf\u00f6ring. Stor vikt kommer att l\u00e4ggas vid dina personliga egenskaper. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Universitetet har ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r ett vikariat p\u00e5 heltid med placering i Malm\u00f6. Arbetet utf\u00f6rs huvudsakligen p\u00e5 plats eftersom n\u00e4rvaro \u00e4r viktig f\u00f6r verksamheten. Arbete under kv\u00e4llar och helger kan f\u00f6rekomma. Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Konstn\u00e4rliga fakulteten i Malm\u00f6 \u00e4r en av nio fakulteter inom Lunds universitet och best\u00e5r av Konst-, Musik- och Teaterh\u00f6gskolan, samt Inter Arts Center. Vid konstn\u00e4rliga fakulteten finns kandidat-, magister- och mastersprogram inom fri konst, musik och teater, samt ett antal kurser av olika omfattning. H\u00e4r bedrivs ocks\u00e5 forskarutbildning och forskning med konstn\u00e4rlig inriktning och i musikpedagogik. Teaterh\u00f6gskolan Malm\u00f6, som \u00e4r placerad mitt i Malm\u00f6s kreativa M\u00f6llev\u00e5ngskvarter, \u00e4r en del av den konstn\u00e4rliga fakulteten vid Lunds Universitet. \u00c5rligen har drygt 100 personer Teaterh\u00f6gskolan som sin studie- eller arbetsplats. Utbildningsuppdraget \u00e4r 60 hel\u00e5rsplatser i form av frist\u00e5ende kurser, program p\u00e5 grund s\u00e5v\u00e4l som masterniv\u00e5 och forskning inom teater. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2027-10-31 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2026-12-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Malm\u00f6 L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2921 Kontakt Daniel Bengmark, Administrativ chef, +46761357186, daniel.bengmark@thm.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-08 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-01 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973142/": {"title": "Postdoctoral position in Lighting, Visual Ergonomics and the Visual Environment", "description": "Postdoctoral position in Lighting, Visual Ergonomics and the Visual Environment Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral position in Lighting, Visual Ergonomics and the Visual Environment Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The position is based at the Division of Ergonomics and Aerosol Technology at the Department of Design Sciences, Faculty of Engineering (LTH), Lund University. The Ergonomics Group aims to study and improve the interaction between people and the products, technical systems and environments they use. We have established collaborations with organisations in both the public and private sectors and conduct research with a clear connection to societal and working-life issues. Within the Ergonomics Group, interdisciplinary research is conducted in areas including visual ergonomics, work environment, and the interaction between people and the physical and technical environment. The research includes both experimental studies and field studies in real-world environments, using both subjective and objective measurement methods. Subject description Visual ergonomics concerns the interaction between human visual capabilities and the visual environment. The position focuses on lighting for older people in working life, with particular interest in visual comfort and discomfort in modern office environments and how workplaces can be lit to meet the needs of older workers. With increasing age, changes occur in the eye and visual system that may affect the need for and sensitivity to different types of lighting. At the same time, more people are expected to remain in the workforce at older ages. There is therefore a need for increased knowledge of how future workplaces and lighting solutions can be designed to provide good visual comfort and reduce discomfort among older workers. The research addresses the relationship between the technical characteristics of lighting, the visual environment, and human perceptual and physiological responses. The project combines experimental laboratory studies with field studies in real office environments. The results will contribute to improved recommendations and guidelines for lighting design for older people in working life . Work duties The main duties involved in a post-doctoral position are to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position includes the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. The purpose of the position is to develop independence as a researcher and to create the opportunity of further academic development. The postdoctoral researcher will play a central role in carrying out the research project and will work closely with the project leader and other researchers in the research team. Detailed description of the work duties Planning, conducting and analysing experimental studies of visual discomfort under different lighting conditions. Planning and participating in the laboratory and field studies, including the development and pilot testing of experimental designs, measurement methods and study protocols. Conducting visual tests and computer-based tasks under different lighting conditions. Collecting and analysing subjective assessments of visual function, symptoms, well-being and quality of life in relation to lighting characteristics. Conducting and analysing light measurements, eye-tracking measurements and other relevant objective measurements. Presenting and communicating research findings to researchers, lighting designers and other relevant stakeholders through workshops and other activities. Writing scientific articles and reports, presenting research findings at national and international conferences, and contributing to the development of new recommendations. Administrative tasks related to the above work duties. Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position. The certificate proving the qualification requirement is met, must be received before the employment decision is made. Priority will be given to candidates who have graduated no more than three years ago before the last day for application. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in both English and Swedish. Documented experience in planning and conducting empirical studies involving human participants within the research field of light and lighting. Documented experience of quantitative data collection and analysis within the research field of light and lighting. Good ability to independently plan and carry out research tasks. Documented experience of scientific writing and publication within the research field of light and lighting. Experience of working in multidisciplinary research environments. The requirement for very good knowledge of Swedish is motivated by the fact that the position involves recruitment and communication with participants as well as data collection in Swedish workplaces. The field study will be conducted with older workers in Swedish office environments and will include validated assessment scales in Swedish. Assessment criteria This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high-quality research. Teaching skills. Other qualifications Knowledge and experience in research related to lighting, light, visual function or related research fields. Experience of experimental laboratory studies and/or field studies in working environments, as well as statistical analysis. Experience of eye tracking or other objective measurement methods. Experience of research involving older people or within working life and work environment research. Knowledge of relevant lighting solutions and the technical characteristics of lighting, or education in related fields. Ability to work independently while also actively contributing to an interdisciplinary research team. Consideration will also be given to how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. The position offers the opportunity to develop as an independent researcher by combining experimental research, field studies and scientific publication, as well as through collaboration with researchers and societal stakeholders. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 2 years (2027-01-01\u20142028-12-31). The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d). How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University\u2019s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.)\u201d We welcome your application! LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2790 Contact Hillevi Hemph\u00e4l\u00e4, Lektor, +46462223936, hillevi.hemphala@design.lth.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 07.Oct.2026 Last application date 21.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973815/": {"title": "Systemspecialist", "description": "Systemspecialist Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Systemspecialist Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, sektionen Kommunikation Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss Jobba hos oss Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Du kommer att bli ansvarig f\u00f6r att f\u00f6rvalta och utveckla universitetets centrala nyhetsbrevsverktyg. I arbetet med nyhetsbrevsverktyg kommer du att agera som systemspecialist och anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d. Du kommer att ge anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d till de verksamheter som kommer att nyttja verktyget samt forts\u00e4tta utveckla verktyget och mallar tillsammans med den externa leverant\u00f6ren och interna specialister. Du kommer att ge svar p\u00e5 fr\u00e5gor och hj\u00e4lpa till vid problem. Tillsammans med den interna systemf\u00f6rvaltningen och den externa leverant\u00f6ren f\u00f6r att vidareutveckla och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra verktyget utifr\u00e5n verksamheternas behov. Du kommer ocks\u00e5 att delta i m\u00f6ten och arbetsgrupper kring systemf\u00f6rvaltning och utveckling av verktyget samt ta fram beslutsunderlag och genomf\u00f6ra utredningar kopplat till systemet eller verksamhetsutveckling. I rollen ing\u00e5r ocks\u00e5 att dokumentera rutiner, skapa anv\u00e4ndarguider och utbildningsmaterial f\u00f6r verktyget. Du kommer \u00e4ven att vara delaktig i sektionen Kommunikations gemensamma arbete. Kravprofil Du har: h\u00f6gskoleutbildning i kommunikation, digital strategi eller motsvarande erfarenhet av arbete som kommunikat\u00f6r, systemspecialist eller arbete som vi bed\u00f6mer som likv\u00e4rdigt erfarenhet av arbete inom h\u00f6gskola, universitet eller annan statlig myndighet erfarenhet av att leda m\u00f6ten, arbetsgrupper och/eller projekt mycket god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka dig i tal och skrift, b\u00e5de p\u00e5 svenska och engelska aktuella kunskaper i att kommunicera p\u00e5 webben samt vana av att arbeta i webbpubliceringssystem Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av f\u00f6ljande: leverant\u00f6rskontakter och upphandling inom offentlig sektor ta fram beslutsunderlag och genomf\u00f6ra utredningar kopplat till system eller verksamhetsutveckling nyhetsbrevsverktyg webbpublicering i Drupal \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tillsvidare med tilltr\u00e4de den 1 januari 2027 med omfattningen 60% procent. Intervjuer kommer att genomf\u00f6ras l\u00f6pande p\u00e5 plats i v\u00e5ra lokaler i Lund. Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.) Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Sektionen Kommunikation, en av Universitetsf\u00f6rvaltningens tio sektioner, arbetar f\u00f6r att \u00f6ka universitetets synlighet, attraktivitet och kommunikativa f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga. Sektionen best\u00e5r av avdelningarna Forsknings- och externkommunikation, Internkommunikation och ledningsst\u00f6d, Studentkommunikation och marknadsf\u00f6ring samt Varum\u00e4rke och digitala plattformar. Sektionen har cirka 60 medarbetare. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 20270101 L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 60 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2823 Kontakt Jill J\u00f6nsson, avdelningschef, 046-2220000, jill.jonsson@kommunikation.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-07 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-21 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974152/": {"title": "Control System Software Engineer", "description": "Control System Software Engineer Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Control System Software Engineer Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Your team At MAX IV, the Technical Division builds and supports the technologies that enable cutting-edge research, while continuously improving how the facility operates. Within this division, the Software team develops and maintains the control systems, data acquisition software, and user interfaces that researchers rely on every day. We focus on increasing functionality and reliability across the facility to meet the demands of world-class science. We provide laboratory wide software solutions following international collaborations in synchrotrons, such as data acquisition, control system, web-based user interfaces, distributed hardware control, scanning tools for running experiments, and metadata harvesting, to meet the continuously evolving research requirements. You will join an open and friendly team of 25 developers of diverse backgrounds, where continuous improvement and mentorship is part of our DNA. As part of the Software group, you will work in close collaboration with scientists as well as network, system, software and hardware engineers and scientific software experts. We promote a DevOps style cross functional team and encourage mutual support between all team members. Would you like to work at one of the brightest light sources in the world? MAX IV is looking for a control system software engineer, that can boost research capabilities for our scientists, and increase operational excellence. Being part of the Software group means participating in different international collaborations about control and acquisition, across Scandinavian and European countries. Finally, this is an opportunity to learn and to increase your skills, competence, and experience. In an international facility such as MAX IV you will meet open-minded people from different perspectives. Your main work tasks will be Developing mission critical software used at the beamlines to conduct their experiments. Support the beamlines to achieve operational excellence by following up their needs and addressing issues. Developing software projects from low level hardware interfaces to high level optimized applications mainly in Python and under Linux. Increasing the functionality and reliability of the beamlines in order to realize their scientific potential. Troubleshooting and finding simple user-friendly solutions to complex problems. Participating in team planning and resource estimation as well as improving the group infrastructure. To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications A university degree in a relevant technical or scientific field. At least 2 years professional Python 3 programming experience. Knowledge of distributed control systems, such as Tango, Epics, or similar. Experience of software development in a Linux operating system environment. Experience with an Agile team environment and familiarity with unit tests, continuous integration and delivery. Solution focused and user driven . Excellent communication skills in English, both written and spoken. Below are seen as merits Experience with operation support in a scientific environment Experience in development for Tango Controls or EPICS Experience with scanning frameworks like Sardana or Bluesky Other software programming languages: C, C++, Rust etc. Software development for scientific applications Knowledge of code lifecycle management: git, Conda, packaging, Ansible, etc Experience of network and distributed systems: TCP/IP layers, OS configuration etc. Evidence of participating in an open-source community collaboration Experience working in an international research-oriented environment As a person you are first and foremost a team player and can demonstrate your communication and collaborative skills. You are open to peer review and willing to share your own knowledge. We expect you to be service minded and have the capability to support a user environment that is under continuous development, with a strong focus on maintaining reliability. What we offer When you join the MAX IV team, you step into a world of front edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world, generating scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer you a multicultural work environment with great opportunities for personal development with respect for a healthy work-life balance. - On call service may apply. - Probation period may apply. -Three positions are being recruited through this recruitment process. https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position \u2013 (starting with a temporary contract) Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 3 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2830 Contact Peter Sj\u00f6blom, +46702999397, peter.sjoblom@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 07.Oct.2026 Last application date 25.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974764/": {"title": "Amanuens inom digitalhistoria", "description": "Amanuens inom digitalhistoria Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens inom digitalhistoria Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Avdelningen f\u00f6r historia tillh\u00f6r Institutionen f\u00f6r Historia vid Lunds universitet. \u00a0I historia erbjuder vi sp\u00e4nnande kurser som str\u00e4cker sig fr\u00e5n forntidens h\u00f6gkulturer till den samtida kulturen \u2013 p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5, avancerad niv\u00e5 och forskarniv\u00e5. Institutionen \u00e4r en stor arbetsplats som varje \u00e5r tar emot hundratals nyfikna studenter. Den \u00e4r ocks\u00e5 en av landets ledande forskningsmilj\u00f6er i historia och hemvist f\u00f6r Nationella forskarskolan i historiska studier. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Du kommer att arbeta som amanuens med att planera, arrangera och genomf\u00f6ra m\u00f6ten. Du kommer ocks\u00e5 att arbeta med att assistera forskare i deras arbete med med k\u00e4llmaterial. I detta kan ing\u00e5 att arbeta med digitala verktyg f\u00f6r anv\u00e4ndning inom historie\u00e4mnet, och/eller att koda. Kvalifikationer Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som amanuens \u00e4r den som aktivt bedriver studier p\u00e5 grund- eller avancerad niv\u00e5 vid aktuell fakultet och som \u00e4nnu inte tagit ut sin examen. Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: \u00e4r antagen till och ska l\u00e4sa en utbildning vid Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna under h\u00f6stterminen 2026 och v\u00e5rterminen 2027 . F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att arbeta p\u00e5 b\u00e5de engelska och svenska Grundl\u00e4ggande kunskap om hur Lunds universitet fungerar som organisation (s\u00e4rskilt Historiska institutionen) Erfarenhet av att arrangera m\u00f6ten samt f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att ta egna initiativ Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Kunskap om digitala verktyg f\u00f6r anv\u00e4ndning inom historie\u00e4mnet och/eller kodning. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning med omfattningen 20 procent av heltid, med tilltr\u00e4de den 2027-01-15 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse, till och med 2027-06-15. Anst\u00e4llningen f\u00e5r inte p\u00e5verka amanuensens studier negativt och f\u00e5r inte kombineras med andra anst\u00e4llningar. Best\u00e4mmelser g\u00e4llande utbildningsanst\u00e4llning som amanuens finns i H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8-12 \u00a7\u00a7. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska/b\u00f6r inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska/b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.) V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Om Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna har sju institutioner och bedriver en stor och varierad verksamhet inom forskning och utbildning. Vi har ca 700 anst\u00e4llda och ca 4 000 hel\u00e5rsstudenter. Om Historiska institutionen Historiska institutionen utg\u00f6r en av sju institutioner vid Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna. Den \u00e4r en stor institution med tre avdelningar: avdelningen f\u00f6r historia, avdelningen f\u00f6r m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter och Centrum f\u00f6r \u00d6st- och Syd\u00f6stasienstudier. H\u00e4r finns runt 100 l\u00e4rare och forskare. Inom institutionen bedrivs undervisning f\u00f6retr\u00e4desvis inom ramen f\u00f6r kandidatprogram i historia respektive m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter, masterprogram i historia samt internationella masterprogram i m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter respektive Asienstudier. Institutionen har ocks\u00e5 en stor forskarutbildning med doktorander i historia, m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter och \u00d6st- och Syd\u00f6stasienstudier bland annat genom en forskarskola i historiska studier. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-15 eller enligt \u00f6.k L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 20 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2850 Kontakt Lina Sturfelt, Prefekt, 046-2220000, lina.sturfelt@hist.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-07 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-21 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974795/": {"title": "Amanuens inom kunskapshistoria", "description": "Amanuens inom kunskapshistoria Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens inom kunskapshistoria Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. \u200bBeskrivning av arbetsplatsen \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b Avdelningen f\u00f6r historia tillh\u00f6r Institutionen f\u00f6r Historia vid Lunds universitet. I historia erbjuder vi sp\u00e4nnande kurser som str\u00e4cker sig fr\u00e5n forntidens h\u00f6gkulturer till den samtida kulturen \u2013 p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5, avancerad niv\u00e5 och forskarniv\u00e5. Institutionen \u00e4r en stor arbetsplats som varje \u00e5r tar emot hundratals nyfikna studenter. Den \u00e4r ocks\u00e5 en av landets ledande forskningsmilj\u00f6er i historia och hemvist f\u00f6r Nationella forskarskolan i historiska studier. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b Vi erbjuder\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b \u200b\u200bLunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. \u200b\u00a0Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid.\u00a0L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss. \u200bArbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den\u200b Du kommer att arbeta med att samla in och ordna k\u00e4llmaterial. Du kommer ocks\u00e5 att bist\u00e5 i forskningsprojekt, utf\u00f6ra adminstrativa uppgifter samt assistera vid arrangemang (seminarier, workshops) etc. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bKvalifikationer\u200b\u200b\u200b Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som amanuens \u00e4r den som aktivt bedriver studier p\u00e5 grund- eller avancerad niv\u00e5 vid aktuell fakultet och som \u00e4nnu inte tagit ut sin examen. \u200b\u200bKrav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r:\u200b L\u00e4ser en utbildning vid Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna vid Lunds universitet Har minst 60 h\u00f6gskolepo\u00e4ng historia eller id\u00e9historia Har mycket goda kunskaper i svenska, i b\u00e5de tal och skrift Intresse f\u00f6r kunskapshistoria och vilja att arbeta med olika kunskapshistoriska forskningsprojekt som t\u00e4cker s\u00e5v\u00e4l tidigmodern som modern historia. Tidigare erfarenhet av sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt arbete med insamling och uppordning av k\u00e4llmaterial. Har f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt och strukturera arbetsuppgifter Har god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga \u200b\u200bMeriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r:\u200b Tidigare erfarenhet av administrativt arbete \u00d6vrigt\u200b Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tidsbegr\u00e4nsad amanuensanst\u00e4llning med omfattningen 20 procent av heltid, med tilltr\u00e4de den 2027-01-15 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse,\u00a0 till och med 2027-06-15. Anst\u00e4llningen f\u00e5r inte p\u00e5verka amanuensens studier negativt och f\u00e5r inte kombineras med andra anst\u00e4llningar. Best\u00e4mmelser g\u00e4llande utbildningsanst\u00e4llning som amanuens finns i H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8-12 \u00a7\u00a7. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska/b\u00f6r inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska/b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.) V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Om Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna har sju institutioner och bedriver en stor och varierad verksamhet inom forskning och utbildning. Vi har ca 700 anst\u00e4llda och ca 4 000 hel\u00e5rsstudenter. Om Historiska institutionen Historiska institutionen utg\u00f6r en av sju institutioner vid Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna. Den \u00e4r en stor institution med tre avdelningar: avdelningen f\u00f6r historia, avdelningen f\u00f6r m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter och Centrum f\u00f6r \u00d6st- och Syd\u00f6stasienstudier. H\u00e4r finns runt 100 l\u00e4rare och forskare. Inom institutionen bedrivs undervisning f\u00f6retr\u00e4desvis inom ramen f\u00f6r kandidatprogram i historia respektive m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter, masterprogram i historia samt internationella masterprogram i m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter respektive Asienstudier. Institutionen har ocks\u00e5 en stor forskarutbildning med doktorander i historia, m\u00e4nskliga r\u00e4ttigheter och \u00d6st- och Syd\u00f6stasienstudier bland annat genom en forskarskola i historiska studier. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-15 eller enligt \u00f6.k L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 20 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2851 Kontakt Lina Sturfelt, Prefekt, 0462220000, lina.sturfelt@hist.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-07 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-21 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975480/": {"title": "Assistant researcher to the Diagnostic Radiology research group", "description": "Assistant researcher to the Diagnostic Radiology research group Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Assistant researcher to the Diagnostic Radiology research group Login and apply Lund University, Medical Faculty, Department of translational medicine Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Diagnostic Radiology research group performs research related to clinical imaging diagnostics. LUCI (Lund University breast Cancer Imaging) is an interdisciplinary group of scientists and medical professionals, mainly focused on innovative clinical imaging methods in breast cancer diagnostics, with a particular focus on cancer screening and artificial intelligence. Located at the Skane University Hospital (SUS) Malm\u00f6, Diagnostic Radiology and LUCI are both headed by Professor Sophia Zackrisson and consist of scientists with diverse professional background as well as technical staff. More information can be found here. The LUCI research group has collaborated with the Quantum Information Group at the Department of Atomic Physics, Department of Physics, on optical imaging of tissue for the past 10 years. This collaboration has deepened over time and is now in a very active phase with clinical studies on optical imaging of breast tissue by combining light and ultrasound using the Ultrasound Optical Tomography (UOT) technology. A first goal at present is to investigate to what extent UOT could be used to reduce the number of biopsies through UOT-based diagnostics of suspicious tumor indications. The hypothesis is that UOT could determine whether the current indication is benign or malignant and thereby reduce the number of women requiring a biopsy. The clinical studies are being conducted in collaboration with the start-up company Deep Light Vision. However, the current research would need to be supplemented with theory development and image analysis studies, and we are looking for a qualified assistant researcher for this task. Within the research group, we are committed to providing a good working environment characterised by respect and consideration in our interactions with one another, and we strive to create a workplace that is both stimulating and offers opportunities for professional development for all employees. We continuously work to create the right conditions for job satisfaction, development and participation for all employees. We are committed to ensuring both physical safety and a good psychosocial work environment. What we offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that you will have special benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension. We also have a flexitime agreement that creates good conditions for work/life balance. Read more on the University\u2019s website about being a Lund University employee, Work at Lund University . Work duties and responsibilities In this position, you will contribute to research in two main areas. First, you will investigate how a database of digital UOT images can be established through clinical studies. Your research will focus on evaluating the feasibility of creating a comprehensive image database that can support further optimization of the UOT imaging technique and enable the development of AI-based tools for UOT data analysis. Second, you will conduct theoretical and computational research to support the development of UOT technology. This includes modelling and simulation of UOT signals to study factors such as the effects of tissue scattering on signal strength and resolution, interactions between ultrasound and optical properties, and how surrounding tissue influences image formation. You will also contribute to the development, validation, and evaluation of software and experimental UOT systems for clinical research studies, as well as the analysis of clinically acquired UOT data. Throughout the employment period, you will spend part of your time in a clinical environment, gaining valuable insight into breast cancer diagnostic workflows and their relevance for the future implementation of UOT imaging. You will actively participate in research meetings, present your findings, and be encouraged to disseminate your results through national and international scientific conferences. Qualifications: Requirements for the position: PhD in physics, or in a related field Experience in modeling light scattering in tissue and modeling the interaction between light and ultrasound in tissue. Proficiency in English (speaking, reading, and writing) Previous research experience within the subject area of the project. Great emphasis will be placed on personal qualities. The duties require you to be able to work independently; have high analytical skills; and have good collaboration and communication skills. Further information The position is a fixed-term employment (s\u00e4rskild visstidsanst\u00e4llning) of 9 months, full-time position (100%), with a preliminary start date of 1 December 2026, or as agreed. How to apply You apply for the position via the University's recruitment system. Applications must include a personal motivation letter, a CV, a diploma and other documents you wish to be considered (e.g. letters of recommendation). The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Translational Medicine is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We conduct basic science in a laboratory setting, point-of-care and clinical research as well as carry out epidemiological studies. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time First day of employment 2026-12-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Malm\u00f6 County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2869 Contact Mikaela F\u00f6nss, HR-partner, +4640391071, mikaela.fonss@med.lu.se Sophia Zackrisson, Rekryterande chef, +4640338797, sophia.zackrisson@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 07.Oct.2026 Last application date 22.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972765/": {"title": "Beamline Scientist", "description": "Beamline Scientist at MAXPEEM Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Beamline Scientist at MAXPEEM Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV, Science Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is looking for a beamline scientist at the state-of-the-art AC-SPELEEM beamline MAXPEEM to further develop the spectromicroscopy program, including advancing the instrumentation, growing user communities, and pursuing their own scientific research. Your team The MAXPEEM beamline is dedicated to spectromicroscopy with nanometer resolution on magnetic materials, semiconductor devices, metal alloys, heterogeneous catalysts, and other nanostructured surfaces using SPELEEM. The beamline provides variable-polarization VUV and soft X-ray light to the state-of-the-art Aberration-Corrected SPELEE\u039c microscope. The team consists of six members - three scientists, two postdocs, and a technician, who are actively driving multiple research and development projects within magnetism, 2D materials, surface science, and industrial applications. Would you like to work at one of the brightest lightsources in the world? Your main work tasks will be Ensure the robust, optimal day-to-day operation of the beamline, including all instruments, software, and adjacent facilities, and prepare it for the planned user experiments. Provide support to the users during the setup and execution of beamline experiments. Organise the constant availability of technical infrastructure and work towards improvements for a user-friendly beamline. Contribute to the continuous development and implementation of methods and beamline instrumentation. Carry out procurements for developing and maintaining the technical infrastructure. Together with the beamline lead, perform proposal feasibility checks. Communicate with the beamline team members and other relevant staff at MAX IV and external partners. Communicate to the existing and potential new users the current capabilities and the upgrade plans of the beamline. Create and maintain beamline documentations. Have a solid knowledge of the general and organizational safety rules and requirements, and instruct users and team members. Pursue own research program in collaboration with users or members of team and acquire external funding. Play an active role in the development of the research portfolio of the beamline. Supervise temporary staff (PostDocs, PhD, and Master students). To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications PhD in Physics, Materials Science, Chemistry, or related area. Demonstrated experience in performing experiments, with soft x-ray synchrotron-based techniques within fields of magnetism, ferroelectricity, 2D materials, surface science, or related. A good track record of published articles in peer-reviewed journals highlighting findings from your research and experimental activities. Demonstrated experience in performing experiments with photoemission electron microscopy (PEEM) or low-energy electron microscopy (LEEM). Experience\u00a0in\u00a0programming\u00a0(e.g., Python, C++, Matlab, Igor Pro, or other) for data analysis. Experience in using and\u00a0maintaining\u00a0ultrahigh vacuum instrumentation. Demonstrated ability to work independently. Excellent\u00a0command of the English language,\u00a0good communication, and teamwork skills. Below are seen as merits Hands-on experience with photoemission electron microscopy (PEEM) or low-energy electron microscopy (LEEM). Experience in programming for automation or data acquisition. Experience in user support at\u00a0synchrotrons. What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you step into a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientist from all over the world, generating scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer you a multicultural work environment with great opportunities for personal development with respect for a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supporting environment? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference! How to apply You apply through our recruitment system Varbi. You will be asked to answer questions as part of your application. Some of these are for statistical purposes, while others are connected to the vacant position. Questions related to the position will follow the standard questions; please be sure to answer them, as they form the basis for our selection process. For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university https://www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ Probationary period may apply. On call services may apply in the future. MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position \u2013 (starting with a temporary contract) Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2785 Contact Andrey Shavorskiy, group manager, +46702281657, andrey.shavorskiy@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 06.Oct.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975071/": {"title": "Amanuens i EU law and cross-border Internet defamation in context", "description": "Amanuens i EU law and cross-border Internet defamation in context Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens i EU law and cross-border Internet defamation in context Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av projektet \u201dEU law and cross-border Internet defamation in context\u201d Projektet syftar till att bidra till utvecklingen av Europeiska unionens reglering av gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande \u00e4rekr\u00e4nkningar p\u00e5 internet samt vissa n\u00e4rliggande r\u00e4ttsomr\u00e5den. Projektet behandlar d\u00e4rvid flera centrala forskningsfr\u00e5gor, bland annat fr\u00e5gan om hur EU:s reglering av gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande \u00e4rekr\u00e4nkningar p\u00e5 internet b\u00f6r utformas med beaktande av behovet av att balansera de olika relevanta intressen som ber\u00f6rs och fr\u00e5gor om i vilken utstr\u00e4ckning EU:s reglering av gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande \u00e4rekr\u00e4nkningar p\u00e5 internet kan bidra till att hantera och bidra till utformningen av regleringen av gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande r\u00e4ttsliga fr\u00e5gor inom omr\u00e5den s\u00e5som dataskyddsr\u00e4tt och regleringen av desinformation. Projektet kommer att generera forskningsresultat som st\u00e4rker skyddet f\u00f6r EU-medborgarnas anseende samtidigt som en l\u00e4mplig balans uppr\u00e4tth\u00e5lls i f\u00f6rh\u00e5llande till yttrandefriheten. Projektet kommer ocks\u00e5 att ge insikter som kan bidra till utvecklingen av regleringen inom n\u00e4rliggande omr\u00e5den och medf\u00f6ra ekonomiska och samh\u00e4lleliga f\u00f6rdelar. Projektet \u00e4r s\u00e4rskilt aktuellt eftersom Europeiska unionen f\u00f6r n\u00e4rvarande arbetar med betydande f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttringar av s\u00e5v\u00e4l 2012 \u00e5rs Bryssel I-f\u00f6rordning (nr. 1215/2012), som reglerar fr\u00e5gor om domstols beh\u00f6righet, som Rom II-f\u00f6rordningen (nr. 864/2007), som reglerar till\u00e4mplig lag men f\u00f6r n\u00e4rvarande undantar \u00e4rekr\u00e4nkningsm\u00e5l fr\u00e5n sitt till\u00e4mpningsomr\u00e5de. Inom ramen f\u00f6r projektet kommer reformf\u00f6rslag att diskuteras och presenteras med utg\u00e5ngspunkt i det bredare sammanhang inom vilket den centrala fr\u00e5gan om gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande \u00e4rekr\u00e4nkningar p\u00e5 internet m\u00e5ste behandlas \u2013 en fr\u00e5ga vars konsekvenser str\u00e4cker sig fr\u00e5n den mest personliga niv\u00e5n till fr\u00e5gor om nationell s\u00e4kerhet. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet som erbjuder goda anst\u00e4llningsvillkor. Med en anst\u00e4llning som amanuens f\u00e5r du som student en m\u00f6jlighet att f\u00f6rena studier med arbete f\u00f6r att komplettera dina teoretiska kunskaper med praktisk arbetslivserfarenhet inom akademin. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna omfattar administrativt st\u00f6d och forskningsst\u00f6d inom ramen f\u00f6r det ovan beskrivna projektet. I arbetsuppgifterna ing\u00e5r bland annat arbete med att bist\u00e5 i samband med forskningsans\u00f6kningar, insamling och systematisering av k\u00e4llmaterial, sammanst\u00e4llning av forskningsresultat, samt planering och administration i samband med m\u00f6ten, seminarier och konferenser. Kvalifikationer och krav Enligt 5 kap 10 \u00a7 HF kan bara den som \u00e4r antagen till utbildning p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 eller avancerad niv\u00e5 anst\u00e4llas som amanuens. Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som amanuens \u00e4r den som aktivt bedriver studier p\u00e5 grund- eller avancerad niv\u00e5 vid aktuell fakultet och som \u00e4nnu inte tagit ut sin examen. S\u00f6kanden ska antingen l\u00e4sa kursen LAGE01 (Civilr\u00e4ttskipning och internationell privatr\u00e4tt) innevarande termin eller sedan tidigare ha godk\u00e4nd tentamen p\u00e5 kursen Goda kunskaper inom internationell privatr\u00e4tt S\u00f6kanden ska ha f\u00f6rkunskaper och erfarenheter som \u00e4r l\u00e4mpliga f\u00f6r att p\u00e5 ett noggrant, systematiskt och sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt s\u00e4tt kunna sammanst\u00e4lla, l\u00e4sa och analysera ett komplext k\u00e4llmaterial samt kunna formulera akademiska texter med r\u00e4ttsvetenskaplig metod. S\u00f6kanden ska d\u00e4rut\u00f6ver ha god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att sammanst\u00e4lla och presentera analysresultat i skrift. Goda kunskaper i b\u00e5de svenska och engelska S\u00f6kanden b\u00f6r ha ett intresse f\u00f6r juridisk och samh\u00e4llsvetenskaplig forskning och det \u00e4r meriterande om s\u00f6kanden har erfarenhet av forskningsrelaterat arbete sedan tidigare. Eftersom arbetsuppgifterna utf\u00f6rs b\u00e5de tillsammans med andra och p\u00e5 egen hand kr\u00e4vs att du har god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, \u00e4r sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndig och har f\u00f6rm\u00e5gan att ta egna initiativ. Vi l\u00e4gger stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. Varaktighet och villkor Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tidsbegr\u00e4nsad under perioden 2026-12-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse under 6 m\u00e5nader, med m\u00f6jlighet till f\u00f6rl\u00e4ngning och avser omfattning p\u00e5 20 % av heltid. Anst\u00e4llningen f\u00e5r inte p\u00e5verka amanuensens studier negativt och b\u00f6r inte kombineras med andra anst\u00e4llningar. Best\u00e4mmelser g\u00e4llande utbildningsanst\u00e4llning som amanuens finns i H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8\u201312 \u00a7\u00a7. Anst\u00e4llningen omfattas av flextidsavtalet . Ans\u00f6kan Till ans\u00f6kan bifogas CV, personligt brev som sammanfattar s\u00f6kandens f\u00f6rkunskaper och erfarenheter relevanta f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten, samt en egenf\u00f6rfattad l\u00e4ngre text som visar prov p\u00e5 s\u00f6kandens f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att skriva akademiska texter med r\u00e4ttsvetenskaplig metod. Du beh\u00f6ver \u00e4ven bifoga utdrag fr\u00e5n LADOK som intygar din beh\u00f6righet. Juridiska fakulteten \u00e4r en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 och avancerad niv\u00e5 och ett 160-tal anst\u00e4llda varav ett 40-tal \u00e4r doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns p\u00e5 v\u00e5r hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2026-12-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 20 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2857 Kontakt Ulf Maunsbach, +462221039, ulf.maunsbach@jur.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-06 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-03 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975475/": {"title": "Supporttekniker", "description": "Supporttekniker Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Supporttekniker Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Humaniora och teologi, IT-enheten Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen IT-enheten \u00e4r en sp\u00e4nnande och dynamisk arbetsplats som tillhandah\u00e5ller IT-st\u00f6d till hela verksamheten vid Humaniora och Teologi tack vare sin bredd av IT-kompetenser. Det \u00e4r en mogen IT-organisation som har funnits i snart 17 \u00e5r och som \u00e4r redo att anta nya utmaningar. IT-enheten \u00e4r en infrastrukturenhet och har ett n\u00e4ra samarbete med \u00f6vriga st\u00f6dverksamheter inom HT, liksom med fakultetens 8 institutioner. P\u00e5 IT-enheten arbetar f\u00f6r n\u00e4rvarande12 personer, med allt fr\u00e5n IT-support och AV-st\u00f6d till systemadministration och webbutveckling. V i erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld vid Lunds universitet, Jobba hos oss . Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna inneba\u0308r fra\u0308mst att ge teknisk support a\u030at va\u030ara ansta\u0308llda, ba\u030ade personligen och via fja\u0308rrsupport. Du kommer att inga\u030a i ett team som arbetar med IT-support fo\u0308r alla institutioner och enheter inom Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna vid Lunds universitet. Arbetsuppgifterna utfo\u0308r du ba\u030ade sja\u0308lvsta\u0308ndigt och i samarbete med andra. Din placering kommer i huvudsak att vara pa\u030a LUX. Supporten innefattar sa\u030ava\u0308l installationer som felso\u0308kning och avhja\u0308lpande av fel pa\u030a klientdatorer (Mac OS X, Windows OS) och eventuell kringutrustning, skrivare, n\u00e4tverk, AV-utrustning samt enklare webba\u0308renden. I rollen som supporttekniker arbetar du med att besvara supporta\u0308renden som kommer in via IT-enhetens a\u0308rendehanteringssystem eller via telefon/beso\u0308k. Kommunikation med anva\u0308ndare sker ba\u030ade pa\u030a svenska och engelska, ibland muntligen och ibland skriftligen, vilket inneba\u0308r att det a\u0308r viktigt att du har goda kunskaper i sa\u030ava\u0308l det svenska som det engelska spra\u030aket. Viss systemadministration samt arbete i projektform kan ocksa\u030a bli aktuellt. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: En relevant utbildning i IT eller dokumenterad relevant arbetslivserfarenhet Tekniska kunskaper om ba\u030ade Mac OS och Windows OS Mycket goda kunskaper i Microsoft Office Du talar och skriver b\u00e5de svenska och engelska obehindrat Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r kunskaper i: System Center Configuration Manager JAMF Projektkompetens/arbete i projektform Digital ljud- och bildhantering samt erfarenhet av support pa\u030a avancerad AV-utrustning i fo\u0308rela\u0308sningssalar AD TCP/IP n\u00e4tverk \u00c4rendehanteringssystem Serveroperativsystemen Linux (Ubuntu) och Microsoft Windows Server Anv\u00e4ndning av AD f\u00f6r beh\u00f6righetsstyrning Vi kommer att l\u00e4gga stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. Vi f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntar oss att du a\u0308r serviceinriktad och har ett gott bemo\u0308tande. Du beh\u00f6ver \u00e4ven ha en god pedagogisk fo\u0308rma\u030aga, fo\u0308rma\u030aga att hantera ma\u0308nniskor och l\u00e4tt f\u00f6r att samarbeta. Eftersom vissa perioder a\u0308r va\u0308ldigt arbetsintensiva kra\u0308vs en ho\u0308g arbetskapacitet, liksom stressta\u030alighet och ett strukturerat arbetssa\u0308tt. Du ma\u030aste ha en fo\u0308rma\u030aga att arbeta sja\u0308lvsta\u0308ndigt och att pa\u030a egen hand skaffa dig den kunskap du beho\u0308ver. Dessa egenskaper a\u0308r lika viktiga som den tekniska kompetensen. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tillsvidare med omfattningen 100 procent och med tilltr\u00e4de den 1 februari 2027 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Provanst\u00e4llning kan komma att till\u00e4mpas. Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Intervjuer kommer att genomf\u00f6ras i v\u00e5ra lokaler i Lund. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, utbildningsbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc). Om Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna har sju institutioner och bedriver en stor och varierad verksamhet inom forskning och utbildning. Vi har ca 700 anst\u00e4llda och ca 4 000 hel\u00e5rsstudenter. Om IT-enheten IT-enheten \u00e4r en av de fem infrastrukturenheterna inom de Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna och tillhandah\u00e5ller IT-st\u00f6d till alla anst\u00e4llda. IT-enheten har funnits sedan 2009 och best\u00e5r av totalt 12 medarbetare. IT-enheten samverkar med universitetets \u00f6vriga IT-verksamheter och \u00e4r en kundfokuserad IT-verksamhet med en platt organisation. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-02-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2868 Kontakt Edin Kuckovic, IT-chef, 046-2220000, edin.kuckovic@ht.lu.se Malin Rehnstam, HR-chef, 046-2220000, malin.rehnstam@kansliht.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-06 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-29 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975610/": {"title": "Amanuens till internationella avdelningen vid Ekonomih\u00f6gskolans kansli", "description": "Amanuens till internationella avdelningen vid Ekonomih\u00f6gskolans kansli Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens till internationella avdelningen vid Ekonomih\u00f6gskolans kansli Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Ekonomih\u00f6gskolan vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r en internationellt framst\u00e5ende handelsh\u00f6gskola som har s k trippel kvalitetsackreditering. Vi arbetar i en internationell milj\u00f6 och har eftertraktade utbildningar p\u00e5 grund-, masters- och forskarniv\u00e5. Ekonomih\u00f6gskolan har ett n\u00e4ra samarbete med f\u00f6retag och myndigheter s\u00e5v\u00e4l nationellt som internationellt. Vi m\u00e5nar om en god, stimulerande arbetsmilj\u00f6 och arbetar kontinuerligt med att utvecklas som en attraktiv arbetsgivare. Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet och erbjuder goda anst\u00e4llningsvillkor. H\u00e4r kan du l\u00e4sa om hur det \u00e4r att arbeta hos oss och om f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner f\u00f6r v\u00e5ra anst\u00e4llda. Om arbetsplatsen Internationella avdelningen hanterar processerna f\u00f6r alla inresande och utresande utbytesstudenter p\u00e5 Ekonomih\u00f6gskolan. Vi s\u00f6ker nu en amanuens p\u00e5 20% / 8 h per vecka, med start 26 oktober 2026 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse, till och med 15 juni 2027. Med en anst\u00e4llning som amanuens f\u00e5r du som student en m\u00f6jlighet att f\u00f6rena studier med arbete f\u00f6r att komplettera dina teoretiska kunskaper med praktisk arbetslivserfarenhet inom akademin. Arbetsuppgifter St\u00f6d i det administrativa arbetet och tillsammans med kollega organisera f\u00f6rekommande event f\u00f6r studenter. Kvalifikationer Beh\u00f6righet Enligt 5 kap 10 \u00a7 HF kan bara den som \u00e4r antagen till utbildning p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 eller avancerad niv\u00e5 anst\u00e4llas som amanuens. Krav Goda spr\u00e5kkunskaper i engelska Grundl\u00e4ggande spr\u00e5kkunskaper i svenska . Studerar p\u00e5 masterniv\u00e5, alternativt sista \u00e5ret p\u00e5 kandidatniv\u00e5. Gedigen erfarenhet av engagemang inom studentk\u00e5r, f\u00f6retr\u00e4desvis Lundaekonomerna Meriterande Erfarenhet av att arbeta i de administrativa systemen Solemove, Canvas och Ladok. Ytterligare spr\u00e5kkunskaper f\u00f6rutom engelska och svenska. Tidigare erfarenhet av administrativt arbete i universitetsmilj\u00f6 Tidigare vana av att arrangera studentevent Ans\u00f6kan CV och personligt brev bifogas i ans\u00f6kan Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 20/10. Vid fr\u00e5gor, h\u00f6r av dig till Ulrika Qvist Mathiesen, chef p\u00e5 internationella avdelningen vid Ekonomih\u00f6gskolan, via ulrika.qvist_mathiesen@ehl.lu.se eller 046\u2013222 32 59. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 20 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2876 Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-06 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-20 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975769/": {"title": "PhD student in Political Science", "description": "PhD student in Political Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD student in Political Science Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Duties The PhD program in political science consists of 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time studies) and is concluded with the public defense of a printed doctoral thesis. The appointed doctoral student will receive a salary from the University for four years, and the primary obligation is to complete the PhD studies. The position may involve departmental duties, for instance in the form of teaching, of up to 20 percent of full-time working hours, in which case the appointment will be extended accordingly. The doctoral student will have access to a workspace at the Department of Political Science. The terms of employment for doctoral students are regulated in the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5, Sections 1\u20137. The position is part of the research project \u201cA Divisive Spiral? Elite Communication, Voter Engagement, and Algorithmic Amplification of Affective Polarization\u201d. The project is funded by the Swedish Research Council (Vetenskapsr\u00e5det) 2027\u20132030 and led by Professor Hanna B\u00e4ck at the Department of Political Science, Lund University. The project focuses on how affective polarization, strong negative feelings toward political opponents, emerges from the interplay between politicians\u2019 communication and voters\u2019 engagement on social media. Large language models are used to analyze polarizing communication in text and audio from Sweden and Finland at scale, and experiments test how forms of communication and algorithms affect voters. Read more about the project here The doctoral student is expected to contribute to the study of affective polarization among elected representatives and voters, in line with the overall aim of the project. Within these parameters and in dialogue with the other project participants, the doctoral student will conduct independent research and formulate their own research questions, theoretical ideas and methodological approaches. The doctoral student is expected to be present at the department and actively participate in its research and teaching environment, as well as take part in the work of the project. Qualifications The requirements for admission to third-cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with (HF ch. 7 \u00a7 35) are that the applicant: meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program (Swedish Code of Statutes 2010:1064). Applicants meet the general entry requirements for third-cycle courses and study programs if they: have been awarded a second-cycle qualification, have satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits, of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific entry requirements In addition to the general entry requirements, the applicant must have completed at least 30 second-cycle credits within the main field of political science, or have acquired equivalent knowledge in Sweden or abroad. The applicant must also have completed an independently written thesis of at least 15 second-cycle credits in political science or in a discipline deemed equivalent in relation to the project. The thesis must have been examined and graded at the time of application. Assessment criteria Only applicants who are admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral studentship. Admission is primarily to be based on the applicant\u2019s ability to benefit from the third-cycle program. The applicants will be ranked based on an overall assessment of the quality of their submitted thesis or theses and research plan, grades from previous studies, and their personal suitability. As third-cycle studies in political science are very demanding, the applicant must be highly motivated and able to work independently under time constraints. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as is proficiency in both written and spoken English. Documented experience of research related to the project\u2019s themes, and of automated text analysis, is a strong merit. Further merits include experience of programming and of working with large-scale social science data, as well as knowledge of languages relevant to the project\u2019s empirical material. Interviews will be conducted with a short-listed number of applicants during the final stages of the admission process. About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment for four years in accordance with the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5, Sections 1\u20137. Starting date January 1, 2027, or by agreement. The main language of the PhD program is English. However, non-Swedish speaking students are expected to acquire basic skills in Swedish during the period of employment. There are opportunities to participate in language courses taught at the University.\u00a0 The general syllabus and other information about the PhD program in political science is available at https://www.svet.lu.se/en/internal/research-education-external-engagement/doctoral-studies-introduction More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staffpages. https://www.staff.lu.se/research-and-education/research-support/doctoral-education/terms-employment-doctoral-students How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the Lund University recruitment portal. The evaluation of applicants is based on documents submitted by the application deadline. Only complete applications will be considered. It is not possible to add documentation after the deadline. The application must include: a cover letter in Swedish or English of max 1 000 words, which contains a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a brief explanation of why you are interested in third-cycle studies at the Department of Political Science at Lund University; a CV in Swedish or English that demonstrates your eligibility for the third-cycle program in political science; degree and grade certificates in Swedish or English; a thesis in Swedish or English corresponding to at least 15 second-cycle credits in political science or a discipline deemed equivalent (where applicable, a Bachelor\u2019s thesis may also be submitted in addition to the second-cycle thesis); a brief research plan in Swedish or English of max 2 000 words, including references; the names and contact information of two references, preferably active in academia (letters of reference are not required at the application stage); any other documentation you wish to submit in support of your application. We look forward to receiving your application! The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. The Department of Political Science combines ancient traditions with modern research and education. The department safeguards disciplinary breadth and diversity and has long been successful in competition for external research funding. Key research fields include democracy and democratisation, power and administration, diplomacy, peace and conflict, intelligence analysis, political psychology, gender, environmental policy and welfare. The strong research profile of the Department of Political Science is reflected in its teaching. The educational environment has long been strongly international. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2879 Contact Hanna B\u00e4ck, Project leader, hanna.back@svet.lu.se Sara Kalm, Head of PhD studies, sara.kalm@svet.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 06.Oct.2026 Last application date 27.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:976086/": {"title": "Postdoctoral researcher in structural bioinformatics and bacteriophage protein evolution", "description": "Postdoctoral researcher in structural bioinformatics and bacteriophage protein evolution Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral researcher in structural bioinformatics and bacteriophage protein evolution Login and apply This content is hosted by a third party. By showing the external content you accept the cookie terms and conditions of www.youtube.com Lund University, Department of experimental medical science Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The postdoctoral researcher will join the Protein Evolution research group, led by Gemma C. Atkinson, at the Department of Experimental Medical Science, Lund University. We use comparative genomics, sensitive protein function prediction and structural bioinformatics to investigate the evolution and molecular mechanisms of microbial biological conflict, particularly interactions between bacteria and bacteriophages. Our computational research is closely integrated with experimental work through collaborations in microbiology, biochemistry and structural biology. Description of the project Bacteriophages encode many proteins whose functions and interaction partners remain unknown. This project will combine protein structure and complex prediction with comparative genomics and evolutionary analysis to investigate interactions among bacteriophage proteins and between phage proteins and their bacterial hosts. The aim is to uncover previously uncharacterised molecular interactions and understand how protein evolution shapes their functions in phage biology and virus\u2013host interactions. Computational predictions will provide hypotheses for experimental investigation in collaboration with our research partners. Tasks and responsibilities You will conduct computational research involving Python programming and high-throughput protein structure prediction using high-performance computing infrastructure. You will work closely with other members of the research team and external collaborators. The position offers opportunities to develop your independence as a researcher and broaden your scientific expertise. You may also have opportunities to contribute to teaching and gain experience in supervising Master\u2019s students. Qualifications Requirements for the position are: You have a doctoral degree or equivalent foreign degree in bioinformatics, molecular biology, microbiology or a related discipline. The doctoral degree must have been obtained no later than the date on which the appointment decision is made. You have the ability to develop and conduct high-quality research. You have strong programming skills You have in-depth knowledge of bacteriophage molecular biology. You have extensive experience in protein structure prediction and its application to biological research. Your bacteriophage-related research has been published in reputable journals. Meritorious for the position are: Applicants who graduated no more than three years before the closing date for applications. You have experience in predicting the functions of uncharacterised proteins by integrating sequence, structural and genomic context information. You have experience in interdisciplinary research collaborations. You have made open source bioinformatics tools. You have teaching ability. The assessment of applicants will primarily be based on their scientific merits and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on scientific ability within the subject area. We offer We offer a multidisciplinary research environment where bioinformatics, microbiology, biochemistry and structural biology come together to investigate protein function and evolution. You will work closely with computational and experimental researchers, with access to high-performance computing resources. The position offers opportunities to develop your own research ideas, build international collaborations and gain experience in teaching and supervision. Lund University has generous support for parental leave and favourable offers for training and wellness and an occupational pension. Read more about being employed at Lund University on the university\u2019s website, Work with us . About the employment The position is a fixed-term position for two years, 100% with a start date of 2027-02-01 or as agreed. Employment at Lund University is based in Sweden and You will be based at the Biomedical Centre (BMC) in Lund and\u00a0you are expected to be able to perform your work on site in Lund. The position is limited to a minimum of two years and a maximum of three years, in accordance with the collective agreement on fixed-term employment as a postdoctoral researcher (Arbetsgivarverket). A position as a postdoctoral researcher is intended as an initial step in your career and as an opportunity to further deepen and broaden your research expertise How to apply You apply for the position via the university's recruitment system. The application should include a personal letter explaining why you are interested in the position and how the position matches your qualifications. The application should also include copies of degree certificates and a CV that includes publications, links to code such as on GitHub, and contact details of two referees. More information regarding the Faculty of Medicine The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-02-01 or as agreed Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2889 Contact Gemma Atkinson, Forskargruppschef, 046-2220000, gemma.atkinson@med.lu.se Tyra Lundquister, HR-partner, 046-2229876, tyra.lundquister@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 06.Oct.2026 Last application date 20.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:976089/": {"title": "Amanuens forskningsassistent", "description": "Amanuens forskningsassistent Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens forskningsassistent Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Arbetsuppgifter Inom forskningsprojektet De Rika och den Sociale Kontrakten , som leds av Robert Klemmensen, s\u00f6ker vi en forskningsassistent som ska arbeta med projektets datainsamling. Du kommer att programmera en enk\u00e4t i Qualtrics och testa den inf\u00f6r datainsamlingen. D\u00e4refter f\u00f6rbereder du pilotdata och g\u00f6r prelimin\u00e4ra analyser av dem. Resultaten sammanst\u00e4ller du i en kort rapport till projektgruppen. Kvalifikationer Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som amanuens \u00e4r den som \u00e4r antagen till och bedriver studier p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 eller avancerad niv\u00e5 vid Lunds universitet. Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llning goda kunskaper i kvantitativ metod och vana att arbeta i R eller Stata goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska Du b\u00f6r ocks\u00e5 vara noggrann, strukturerad och kunna arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llning studier i nationalekonomi eller statsvetenskap intresse f\u00f6r och erfarenhet av datahantering och dataanalys intresse f\u00f6r att programmera enk\u00e4ter i Qualtrics \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tidsbegr\u00e4nsad och omfattar 20 procent av heltid under tre m\u00e5nader. Tilltr\u00e4de sker enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Anst\u00e4llningen f\u00e5r inte p\u00e5verka amanuensens studier negativt. Best\u00e4mmelser g\u00e4llande utbildningsanst\u00e4llning som amanuens finns i H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8-12 \u00a7\u00a7. Anst\u00e4llningen omfattas av Arbetstidsavtal f\u00f6r l\u00e4rare. S\u00e5 s\u00f6ker du Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla CV och personligt brev (h\u00f6gst en A4) med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Vi ber dig bifoga utdrag fr\u00e5n LADOK som intygar din beh\u00f6righet. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet som erbjuder goda anst\u00e4llningsvillkor. Med en anst\u00e4llning som amanuens f\u00e5r du som student en m\u00f6jlighet att f\u00f6rena studier med arbete f\u00f6r att komplettera dina teoretiska kunskaper med praktisk arbetslivserfarenhet inom akademin. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss. Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra f\u00f6r forskning och utbildning inom samh\u00e4lls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg, \u00f6ver 700 anst\u00e4llda och cirka 5 700 hel\u00e5rsstudenter \u00e4r fakulteten en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. V\u00e5r huvuduppgift \u00e4r att utveckla, f\u00f6rmedla och f\u00f6rvalta kunskap om samh\u00e4lle, m\u00e4nniska och organisationer i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av \u00f6ppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Statsvetenskapliga institutionen kombinerar gamla anor med modern forskning och utbildning. Institutionen v\u00e4rnar \u00e4mnesbredd och metodologisk m\u00e5ngfald och har under l\u00e5ng tid varit framg\u00e5ngsrik i konkurrensen om externa forskningsmedel. Centrala forskningsomr\u00e5den \u00e4r bl.a. demokrati och demokratisering, makt och f\u00f6rvaltning, diplomati, fred och konflikt, underr\u00e4ttelseanalys, politisk psykologi, genus, milj\u00f6politik samt v\u00e4lf\u00e4rd. Statsvetenskapliga institutionens starka forskningsprofil avspeglas i undervisningen. Utbildningsmilj\u00f6n \u00e4r sedan l\u00e4nge starkt internationaliserad. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de Snarast enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 20 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2890 Kontakt Robert Klemmensen, Projektledare, robert.klemmensen@svet.lu.se Erik Wengstr\u00f6m, erik.wengstrom@nek.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-06 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-20 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973392/": {"title": "Associate researcher", "description": "Associate researcher Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Associate researcher Login and apply This content is hosted by a third party. By showing the external content you accept the cookie terms and conditions of www.youtube.com Lund University, Department of experimental medical science Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The research group Translational Neuroendocrine Research Unit, TNU, at the Department of Experimental Medical Science, at the Faculty of Medicine, conducts research on Huntington disease and ALS, and is in the forefront of this research area and is active internationally. Professor \u00c5sa Peters\u00e9n is the head of the research group, which includes researchers, technician and administrator. The group works closely with, and shares labs and staff with, another research group that focuses on Parkinson\u2019s disease and Huntington disease. It is important for us to offer a stimulating workplace that encourages development for all staff. Respect and care for each other are essential components to create a good work environment. Read more about our exciting research here: Translational Neuroendocrinology - Lund University . We offer Lund University is a government agency, which means you receive special benefits, generous vacation, and a favourable occupational pension. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee Work for us | Lund University. Work duties and areas of responsibility Your specific responsibility will be research projects on TDP43 and huntingtin. You will generate and analyse data and present these in manuscripts. Writing both original and review articles in this research area will be significant part of your work. These tasks require a very good knowledge and experience in the area. Qualifications Requirements for the position include: Doctoral degree in medical science, Documented experience in research on TDP43 and Huntington disease, in the form of several published scientific original articles on TDP43 and huntingtin, Documented experience in scientific presentations, both oral and in the format of posters, Documented experience in histological methods and following analyses of brain tissue. Meritorious for the position: Good ability to work independently and work in international collaborations. Further information The employment is a fixed-term position for approximately five months, with a start date of 2027-01-01. How to Apply The position is applied for via the university\u2019s recruitment system. The application should include a cover letter explaining why you are interested in the position and how your qualifications match the requirements. The application should also include a CV, degree certificate or equivalent, and any other documents you wish to refer to (copies of grades, references, letters of recommendation, etc.). More information regarding the Faculty of Medicine The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-01-01 Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2805 Contact \u00c5sa Peters\u00e9n, Forskargruppschef, asa.petersen@med.lu.se Johanna Dahlin, HR Partner, johanna.dahlin@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 05.Oct.2026 Last application date 18.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974051/": {"title": "Ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r till LU Service", "description": "Ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r till LU Service Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r till LU Service Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Vill du kombinera kvalificerat ekonomiadministrativt arbete med m\u00f6jligheten att utveckla framtidens ekonomiprocesser vid ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta universitet? D\u00e5 kan detta vara rollen f\u00f6r dig. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen LU Service \u00e4r en k\u00f6p- och s\u00e4ljorganisation, vilket inneb\u00e4r att verksamheten erbjuder och levererar tj\u00e4nster till universitetets olika delar utifr\u00e5n deras behov. H\u00e4r finns allt fr\u00e5n posthantering och lokalv\u00e5rd till tryckeri, konferensservice och tekniskt underh\u00e5ll \u2013 och dessutom tillhandah\u00e5ller LU Service bostadsl\u00f6sningar f\u00f6r g\u00e4stforskare och studenter. V\u00e5rt kontor ligger centralt i Lund med goda kommunikationsm\u00f6jligheter. H\u00e4r delar du arbetsdagen med ett engagerat g\u00e4ng kollegor fr\u00e5n olika st\u00f6dfunktioner och ledningsgrupp. Vi sitter tillsammans under samma tak, vilket bidrar till en naturlig gemenskap och ett enkelt samarbete. St\u00e4mningen \u00e4r \u00f6ppen och v\u00e4lkomnande - h\u00e4r uppskattas nya id\u00e9er och det finns stor frihet att p\u00e5verka och utvecklas. Om rollen Som ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r ansvarar du f\u00f6r att st\u00f6dja verksamheten inom ekonomiomr\u00e5det genom att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla korrekt och effektiv hantering av ekonomiska processer. Rollen omfattar arbete med l\u00f6pande bokf\u00f6ring, redovisning, fakturahantering och ekonomisk administration enligt g\u00e4llande regelverk, rutiner och riktlinjer. Du bidrar \u00e4ven till utveckling och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttring av administrativa processer och arbetar aktivt f\u00f6r att skapa effektiva arbetsfl\u00f6den och h\u00f6g kvalitet i ekonomiarbetet. Du ing\u00e5r i LU Services ekonomi- och verksamhetsst\u00f6dsfunktion och arbetar n\u00e4ra controllerfunktionen, avdelningschef och \u00f6vriga st\u00f6dfunktioner. Arbetsuppgifter Som ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r arbetar du brett inom det ekonomiadministrativa omr\u00e5det. Du ansvarar sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt f\u00f6r ekonomiadministrationen inom utvalda verksamhetsomr\u00e5den och arbetar n\u00e4ra controller vid bokslut, uppf\u00f6ljning och ekonomiska analyser. Dina huvudsakliga arbetsuppgifter kommer att vara: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0L\u00f6pande bokf\u00f6ring och ekonomisk administration. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Hantering av kund- och leverant\u00f6rsfakturor. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Kontering och uppf\u00f6ljning av ekonomiska transaktioner. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Avst\u00e4mningar av konton och ekonomiska underlag. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Medverkan i m\u00e5nads-, tertial- och \u00e5rsbokslutsarbete. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0St\u00f6d till chefer och verksamhet i ekonomiadministrativa fr\u00e5gor. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0S\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla att ekonomiska processer f\u00f6ljer interna och externa regelverk. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Identifiera, analysera och genomf\u00f6ra f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttringar av ekonomiadministrativa processer. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Delta i utvecklings- och digitaliseringsinsatser inom ekonomiomr\u00e5det. Ut\u00f6ver ovanst\u00e5ende arbetsuppgifter kan \u00e4ven andra administrativa uppgifter inom ekonomiomr\u00e5det f\u00f6rekomma. Vi s\u00f6ker Vi s\u00f6ker nu en engagerad och utvecklingsorienterad ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r som vill vara med och st\u00f6dja verksamheten genom kvalificerat ekonomiadministrativt arbete. Hos oss f\u00e5r du arbeta i en dynamisk milj\u00f6 d\u00e4r kvalitet, service och samverkan st\u00e5r i fokus. I rollen kombinerar du traditionellt ekonomiadministrativt arbete med ett aktivt deltagande i utveckling och effektivisering av administrativa processer. Du \u00e4r trygg i redovisningsfr\u00e5gor, har god systemvana och kan bidra b\u00e5de operativt och utvecklingsinriktat i verksamhetens ekonomiarbete. Du trivs med att samarbeta med b\u00e5de verksamheten och controllerfunktion. Genom ditt engagemang bidrar du till att skapa ett professionellt och verksamhetsn\u00e4ra ekonomist\u00f6d. Kvalifikationer F\u00f6r att vara aktuell f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten beh\u00f6ver du uppfylla f\u00f6ljande krav: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Eftergymnasial utbildning inom ekonomi, redovisning eller motsvarande. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av l\u00f6pande redovisning, bokf\u00f6ring och avst\u00e4mningar. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0God kunskap av arbete i ekonomisystem. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av fakturahantering och kontering. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Mycket goda kunskaper i Excel. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0God f\u00f6rst\u00e5else f\u00f6r redovisningsprinciper. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka sig v\u00e4l i tal och skrift p\u00e5 svenska och engelska. Personliga egenskaper Vi l\u00e4gger stor vikt vid dina personliga egenskaper och l\u00e4mplighet. F\u00f6r att lyckas i rollen ser vi att du: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Arbetar strukturerat, noggrant och kvalitetsmedvetet. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Har god analytisk f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och ett intresse f\u00f6r ekonomiska samband. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00c4r serviceinriktad och har l\u00e4tt f\u00f6r att samarbeta med olika yrkesgrupper. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Tar initiativ och driver f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttringar inom ditt ansvarsomr\u00e5de. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Har god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att planera och prioritera ditt arbete. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00c4r f\u00f6r\u00e4ndringsben\u00e4gen och motiveras av att utveckla arbetss\u00e4tt och processer. Meriterande Meriterande f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet fr\u00e5n offentlig verksamhet, g\u00e4rna universitet eller h\u00f6gskola. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av att arbeta i relevanta ekonomisystem s\u00e5som Raindance, EOS, Kuben eller liknande verktyg. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av bokslutsarbete. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av processkartl\u00e4ggning, verksamhetsutveckling eller digitalisering. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Vana av att arbeta med intern styrning och kontroll. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att strukturera, skapa ordning samt t\u00e4nka nytt och effektivisera. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet, vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer om hur det \u00e4r att jobba hos oss p\u00e5 universitetets hemsida, l\u00e4nk nedan. Jobba hos oss | Lunds universitet Ut\u00f6ver detta s\u00e5 erbjuder vi: En nyckelroll i en organisation d\u00e4r du ges stort ansvar och m\u00f6jlighet att p\u00e5verka M\u00f6jligheten att utveckla och forma LU Service ekonomifunktion f\u00f6r framtiden Ett engagerat och v\u00e4lkomnande team med god sammanh\u00e5llning! \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning p\u00e5 100 %, med tilltr\u00e4de snarast enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Provanst\u00e4llning i 6 m\u00e5nader kan komma att till\u00e4mpas. L\u00f6nespannet f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r 34 000 - 45 000 kr. Vid fr\u00e5gor kring tj\u00e4nsten, kontakta controller Tobias Axelsson p\u00e5 +73 804 63 29 eller tobias.axelsson@service.lu.se . Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. LU Service \u00e4r en sektion inom universitetets gemensamma f\u00f6rvaltning och erbjuder s\u00e5v\u00e4l tj\u00e4nster som produkter till universitetets verksamheter: bl.a. lokalv\u00e5rd, vaktm\u00e4steri, reception, tryckeri, post, parkering, universitetsbutik, konferens och bost\u00e4der. LU Service har ca 240 medarbetare. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidare med provanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2829 Kontakt Mikael Olofsson, +46462223892, mikael.olofsson@service.lu.se Tobias Axelsson, +46738046329, tobias.axelsson@service.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-05 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-18 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974506/": {"title": "Universitetslektor i Specialdidaktik vikariat", "description": "Universitetslektor i Specialdidaktik vikariat Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetslektor i Specialdidaktik vikariat Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, HT, Institutionen f\u00f6r utbildningsvetenskap Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Vid Institutionen f\u00f6r utbildningsvetenskap bedrivs utbildningsvetenskaplig forskning med en rad olika inriktningar inom s\u00e5v\u00e4l skola som h\u00f6gre utbildning. Institutionen \u00e4r den centrala noden i det n\u00e4tverk som utg\u00f6r \u00e4mnesl\u00e4rarutbildningen vid Lunds universitet och ansvarar f\u00f6r undervisningen inom \u00e4mnesl\u00e4rarutbildningens utbildningsvetenskapliga k\u00e4rnkurser (UVK), f\u00f6r den kompletterande pedagogiska utbildningen (KPU) f\u00f6r blivande \u00e4mnesl\u00e4rare och samordningen av den verksamhetsf\u00f6rlagda utbildningen (VFU). Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter Undervisning p\u00e5 frist\u00e5ende kurser med temat specialdidaktik, fr\u00e4mst kv\u00e4llstid. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: avlagt doktorsexamen eller har motsvarande vetenskaplig kompetens eller n\u00e5gon annan yrkesskicklighet som \u00e4r av betydelse med h\u00e4nsyn tagen till anst\u00e4llningens inneh\u00e5ll och de arbetsuppgifter som ing\u00e5r i anst\u00e4llningen. visat pedagogisk skicklighet samt genomg\u00e5tt h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller p\u00e5 annat s\u00e4tt inh\u00e4mtat motsvarande kunskaper. Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska i tal och skrift Goda kunskaper i engelska i tal och skrift Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: har erfarenhet av att ha undervisat inom omr\u00e5det specialdidaktik med fokus p\u00e5 ADHD och AST har erfarenhet av pedagogiskt utvecklingsarbete inom utbildningsomr\u00e5det. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r ett vikariat p\u00e5 10% under perioden 2027-01-01 \u2013 2027-06-30 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, kopia p\u00e5 doktorsexamen eller motsvarande, samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.). Om Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna har sju institutioner och bedriver en stor och varierad verksamhet inom forskning och utbildning. Vi har ca 700 anst\u00e4llda och ca 4 000 hel\u00e5rsstudenter. Om Institutionen f\u00f6r utbildningsvetenskap Vid institutionen f\u00f6r utbildningsvetenskap bedrivs utbildningsvetenskaplig forskning med en rad olika inriktningar, exempelvis \u00e4mnesdidaktisk, skol- och utbildningshistorisk samt skol- och utbildningssociologisk forskning och forskning om h\u00f6gre utbildning. Institutionen f\u00f6r utbildningsvetenskap \u00e4r den centrala noden i det omfattande n\u00e4tverk som utg\u00f6r \u00e4mnesl\u00e4rarutbildningen vid Lunds universitet och ansvarar f\u00f6r undervisningen inom \u00e4mnesl\u00e4rarutbildningens utbildningsvetenskapliga k\u00e4rnkurser (UVK), f\u00f6r den kompletterande pedagogiska utbildningen (KPU) f\u00f6r blivande \u00e4mnesl\u00e4rare, samordningen av den verksamhetsf\u00f6rlagda utbildningen (VFU) samt studieadministration, studiev\u00e4gledning och arbete med information till l\u00e4rarstudenterna. Vid institutionen finns ocks\u00e5 Avdelningen f\u00f6r h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utveckling (AHU) som bedriver kursverksamhet f\u00f6r Lunds universitets l\u00e4rare, h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utvecklingsverksamhet samt forskning om h\u00f6gre utbildning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2027-06-30 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 20270101 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 10 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2840 Kontakt Sinikka Neuhaus, prefekt, 046-2220000, sinikka.neuhaus@uvet.lu.se Helena Berglund, bitr utbildningschef, 046-2220000, helena.berglund@uvet.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-05 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975037/": {"title": "Post-doctoral fellow in assesment of global forest dynamics", "description": "Post-doctoral fellow in assesment of global forest dynamics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Post-doctoral fellow in assesment of global forest dynamics Login and apply Lunds universitet Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Research and education at the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences (MGeo) addresses fundamental and applied questions on the Earth\u2019s past, present and future climate and environment, including people\u2019s interactions with the natural world and consequences for human wellbeing. MGeo advances and deploys cutting-edge methods, models and technologies in environmental science, quaternary sciences, bedrock geology, paleontology, physical geography, biodiversity and ecosystem science, remote sensing, Geographic Information Science (GIS), and computational science for health and environment, to study processes spanning from the microscopic to the planetary, across all time scales. The world\u2019s forests are changing rapidly around us. Rates of tree mortality are increasing in many regions, growth rates of trees are changing and the enormous sink of carbon that they provide may be under threat. Yet we currently lack consistent and reliable global-scale assessments of how the dynamics of tree growth and death are changing and likely to change in the future. In the TreeChange project, we are combining information on life history traits, derived from field observations, with demographic vegetation modelling in order to understand unpick the future of the world\u2019s forests and the global forest carbon sink. The fellow will join the TreeChange team at Lund University and work directly with other project nodes in Switzerland and the United Kingdom. They will work under the supervision of Thomas Pugh and alongside a wider team of researchers working on forest dynamics and ecosystem modelling at Lund University. The fellow will develop new methodology utilising the LPJ-GUESS dynamic vegetation model and applying it for assessment of dynamics and carbon cycling in forests around the world. They can expect opportunities to substantially build their professional network, interfacing with a large team of collaborators worldwide. The fellow will also become part of the BECC research platform, a collaboration between Lund University and the University of Gothenburg, which brings together over 250 researchers working on the topics related to biodiversity and ecosystem services under a changing climate. Work duties The main duties involved in a post-doctoral position is to conduct research. Opportunities for teaching may also be included, but shall constitute a minor part of the role. The position shall include the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. The fellow will be expected to lead/contribute to research linking vegetation modelling with the LPJ-GUESS model with tree demographic information derived from ground-based inventory plot data and related tasks, as laid out in the TreeChange project description. This will include the planning of model developments, carrying out model developments, preparing and analysing observational datasets, designing experimental protocols, carrying out the related simulations and analysis, and leading writing of peer-reviewed papers based on the results. The fellow is expected to contribute substantially to the intellectual development of the work. Participation in national and international meetings and workshops related to the above is expected, as is carrying out related administration and communication activities. Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the date of employment decision. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Documented proficiency in computer programming. Track record of preparing and publishing high-quality scientific publications. PhD in biology, ecology or related numerate scientific disciplines. Assessment criteria and other qualifications This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high-quality research. Teaching skills. Additional assessment criteria: Depth of knowledge of forest ecological processes. Level of experience in working with process-based modelling approaches, especially vegetation modelling. Competence in computer programming, with C++ an advantage. Evidence of ability to develop and execute own research ideas, and act upon own initiative. Organisational skills, including ability and willingness to contribute to and coordinate community activities, such as model intercomparisons. Emphasis will be placed on the quality and quantity of scientific publications and other academic achievements indicative of emerging independence as a researcher. Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 2 years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d) between Lund University, SACO-S and OFR/S, dated 1st February 2022. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English and be compiled into a PDF-file containing: r\u00e9sum\u00e9/CV, including a list of publications, an application letter detailing your motivation for this position, a general description of past research and future research interests (no more than one page), contact information of at least two references, copy of the doctoral degree certificate, and other certificates/grades that you wish to be considered. Welcome to apply! Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Employment expires 2029-01-14 Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-01-15 or due agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2856 Contact Thomas Pugh, +46462220000, thomas.pugh@mgeo.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 05.Oct.2026 Last application date 02.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975583/": {"title": "Postdoctoral position in Human-Computer Interaction focusing on AI-mediated programming", "description": "Postdoctoral position in Human-Computer Interaction focusing on AI-mediated programming Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral position in Human-Computer Interaction focusing on AI-mediated programming Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Department of Computer Science Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The position is placed in the NEX (Notations, Environments, and eXperiences) research group within the Software Development and Environments (SDE) unit at the Department of Computer Science. The group is led by Associate Professor Emma S\u00f6derberg and conducts research at the intersection of software engineering, developer tool construction and human\u2013computer interaction. Ongoing projects in and around the group address, among other things, AI-supported code review, semi-automatic code improvement, trust calibration in LLM-assisted refactoring and the design of trustworthy agents in software development. The group collaborates with industry through, for example, the competence centre NextG2Com and the strategic research area ELLIIT, with partners such as Ericsson, Volvo Cars, Axis and Bosch. The position is part of the project Intention Drifting: Ethics, Authorship and Critical Judgment in AI-Mediated Programming, funded jointly by WASP and WASP-HS. The project is a collaboration between Lund University and S\u00f6dert\u00f6rn University, led by Professor Martin Jonsson (S\u00f6dert\u00f6rn University, WASP-HS) and Associate Professor Emma S\u00f6derberg (Lund University, WASP). Through the collaboration with S\u00f6dert\u00f6rn University, you will also take part in the WASP-HS InterSynth Lab and the Future Interactions research group, both engaged in research on AI, design and critical inquiry closely related to the questions of the project. As a postdoctoral researcher in the project, you become part of the research communities of both WASP and WASP-HS. More information about the SDE unit Subject description AI-assisted programming shifts the work of developers from writing code towards articulating intentions and interpreting AI-generated output. The project studies intention drifting, the gradual displacement between developers\u2019 expressed intentions, the interpretations made by AI systems and the actual behaviour of the resulting code, and what this displacement means for authorship, responsibility and critical judgement. The work combines conceptual development, workshop-based empirical studies with developers and research through design. The subject of the position is human\u2013computer interaction with a focus on programming with generative AI. The subject covers studies of how intention, authorship, responsibility and critical judgement are shaped when software is developed together with AI systems, using empirical and design-oriented methods such as qualitative studies of programming practice and research through design. The subject also includes critical perspectives on agency and responsibility in human\u2013AI relations, for example from more-than-human design, science and technology studies (STS) and post-phenomenology. Work duties The main duties involved in a post-doctoral position is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position includes the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. The purpose of the position is to develop the independence as a researcher and to create the opportunity of further development. You will have main responsibility for the day-to-day research in the project and will work closely with both Emma S\u00f6derberg in Lund and Martin Jonsson at S\u00f6dert\u00f6rn University, who takes an active part in planning, conducting and analysing the studies. The project runs over 24 months. The position involves travel between Lund and Stockholm for joint working meetings and writing sessions, as well as travel for workshops with industry partners and international conferences. The work duties include: Developing intention drifting as a concept and analytical framework, together with the project leaders. Planning, conducting and analysing workshop-based studies with developers using AI coding tools, with methods such as think-aloud sessions and retrospective interviews. Designing and evaluating design probes that make intention drifting visible and support critical reflection within programming work. Publishing results at international conferences and in journals in human\u2013computer interaction and adjacent areas of software engineering. Collaboration with industry partners in the recruitment of participants and the conduct of studies. Contributing to the organisation of a concluding workshop for the WASP and WASP-HS research communities. Supervision of degree projects within the area of the project, to a limited extent. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position. The certificate proving the qualification requirement is met, must be received before the employment decision is made. Priority will be given to candidates who have graduated no more than three years ago before the last day for application. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: You have a PhD in human\u2013computer interaction, interaction design or a closely related field. You have documented experience of planning and conducting qualitative empirical studies of technology use or practice, for example interviews, observations, think-aloud studies or workshops. You have very good oral and written proficiency in English. You are independent and able to collaborate across disciplines and institutions. Assessment criteria This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high quality research. Teaching skills. Other qualifications: It is an additional qualification if you have: Experience of research through design or other design-oriented research methods, for example design probes, interactive prototypes or speculative and critical design. Experience of working analytically with theoretical perspectives on human\u2013technology relations, for example from more-than human perspectives, post-phenomenology, posthumanism or critical AI studies. Knowledge of software development, programming practice or developer experience, for example through your own programming experience or research on developers\u2019 work. Experience of research on generative AI or human\u2013AI interaction. Knowledge of research on ethics in design and technology practice, for example in-action ethics or reflection-in-action. Publications in leading international venues in human\u2013computer interaction, such as CHI, DIS, CSCW or TOCHI. Experience of working in interdisciplinary environments that bring together technical and humanistic or social science research. Experience of research collaboration with industry. Consideration will also be given to how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of two years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d). Start date 2026-12-01 or by agreement. For further information, please contact Emma S\u00f6derberg, emma.soderberg@cs.lu.se, or Martin Jonsson, martin.jonsson@sh.se. How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University\u2019s recruitment system and written in English. The application should include a CV including a list of publications, and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your research qualifications. The application should also include a research statement of no more than two pages describing how your theoretical and methodological experience relates to the questions of the project, as well as a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.). We welcome your application! LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2026-12-01 or according to agreement Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2875 Contact Emma S\u00f6derberg, emma.soderberg@cs.lth.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 05.Oct.2026 Last application date 26.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974346/": {"title": "Avdelningschef till Development Office", "description": "Avdelningschef till Development Office Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Avdelningschef till Development Office Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Vill du leda och utveckla Lunds universitets arbete med donationer och l\u00e5ngsiktiga relationer med donatorer? Vi s\u00f6ker en trygg, social och handlingskraftig avdelningschef som kan f\u00f6rena strategiskt ledarskap, stark relationsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och f\u00f6rst\u00e5else f\u00f6r universitetets forskning, innovation och utbildning. Om uppdraget Lunds universitet befinner sig i en snabb utvecklingsfas med excellent forskning, utbildning i v\u00e4rldsklass och starka internationella samarbeten. Att universitet rankas h\u00f6gst i Sverige och st\u00e5r starkt internationellt visar att vi tillsammans skapar kunskap och innovation i v\u00e4rldsklass. Nu s\u00f6ker vi en ny avdelningschef till v\u00e5r donationsavdelning. Som avdelningschef leder och utvecklar du arbetet inom Development Office, Lunds universitets donationsavdelning. Avdelningens uppdrag \u00e4r att strategiskt skapa de b\u00e4sta f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningarna f\u00f6r donationer och g\u00e5vor till forskning och utbildning. Du leder en grupp best\u00e5ende av fem kompetenta och sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndiga medarbetare med olika specialistomr\u00e5den. I ditt ledarskap skapar du riktning och tydliga prioriteringar, tar vara p\u00e5 teamets samlade kompetens och ger medarbetarna goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar att ta ansvar och lyckas tillsammans. Du ansvarar f\u00f6r att skapa goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r nya donationer samtidigt som befintliga donatorrelationer v\u00e5rdas med kontinuitet och l\u00e5ngsiktighet. Du \u00e4r sj\u00e4lv aktiv i det relationsskapande arbetet och f\u00f6retr\u00e4der Lunds universitet i m\u00f6ten med donatorer, alumner, f\u00f6retag, stiftelser och andra samarbetspartners. En central del av rollen \u00e4r att f\u00f6rst\u00e5 forskarnas och fakulteternas behov, f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar och verklighet. Du bygger relationer inom universitetet och bidrar till att oms\u00e4tta akademiska ambitioner och samh\u00e4llsrelevanta initiativ till tydliga och engagerande m\u00f6jligheter f\u00f6r filantropiskt st\u00f6d. Du arbetar n\u00e4ra universitetets och fakulteternas ledningar och bidrar b\u00e5de med kvalificerat ledningsst\u00f6d och i det l\u00e5ngsiktiga strategiarbetet. Avdelningschefen ing\u00e5r i sektionens ledningsgrupp och medverkar tillsammans med sektionschefen f\u00f6r ett samordnat st\u00f6d till forskning, samverkan och innovation. Ditt ansvar leda, utveckla och f\u00f6lja upp avdelningens arbete; med ansvar f\u00f6r medarbetare, arbetsmilj\u00f6 och budget s\u00e4tta m\u00e5l, g\u00f6ra prioriteringar och fatta beslut i dialog med medarbetare och sektionschef utveckla arbetss\u00e4tt och portf\u00f6lj s\u00e5 att ny donatorbearbetning och l\u00e5ngsiktig stewardship f\u00f6rst\u00e4rker varandra bygga och utveckla relationer med potentiella och befintliga donatorer s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla h\u00f6g kvalitet, professionalitet och l\u00e5ngsiktighet genom hela givarresan skapa god samverkan med forskare, fakulteter, universitetsledning och andra delar av universitetet representera Lunds universitet regionalt, nationellt och n\u00e4r det \u00e4r relevant internationellt initiera och driva strategiska utvecklingsinsatser fr\u00e5n id\u00e9 till genomf\u00f6rande och uppf\u00f6ljning. Kvalifikationer Vi s\u00f6ker dig som har: relevant akademisk examen eller motsvarande yrkeserfarenhet fler\u00e5rig chefserfarenhet med personal-, arbetsmilj\u00f6- och budgetansvar dokumenterad erfarenhet av filantropi, fundraising, aff\u00e4rsutveckling eller annat kvalificerat relations- och int\u00e4ktsarbete med tydliga resultat dokumenterad f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att etablera nya relationer, utveckla befintliga kontakter och komma till avslut i komplexa processer erfarenhet av att initiera, leda och slutf\u00f6ra projekt enligt plan mycket god kommunikativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga p\u00e5 svenska och engelska, i b\u00e5de tal och skrift, ett etablerat n\u00e4tverk med relevans f\u00f6r uppdraget och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att kontinuerligt bygga nya n\u00e4tverk god strategisk, strukturell och administrativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga ett genuint intresse f\u00f6r forskning, utbildning och universitetets roll i samh\u00e4llet. Meriterande erfarenhet av operativt arbete med st\u00f6rre g\u00e5vor som lett till dokumenterade resultat erfarenhet fr\u00e5n universitet, eller annan kunskapsintensiv verksamhet erfarenhet av att arbeta n\u00e4ra seniora beslutsfattare, forskare, stiftelser, f\u00f6retag eller privatpersoner i l\u00e5ngsiktiga finansierings- och relationsprocesser. Ditt ledarskap och din person Du \u00e4r social, f\u00f6rtroendeskapande och genuint intresserad av m\u00e4nniskor. Du trivs i m\u00f6tet med andra, tar initiativ till nya kontakter och har l\u00e4tt f\u00f6r att r\u00f6ra dig mellan akademi, n\u00e4ringsliv, stiftelser och andra samh\u00e4llsakt\u00f6rer. Ditt ledarskap \u00e4r dialoginriktat och inkluderande. Du lyssnar in, involverar och tar vara p\u00e5 medarbetarnas sakkunskap, samtidigt som du \u00e4r tydlig med riktning, prioriteringar och ansvar. N\u00e4r det beh\u00f6vs \u00e4r du trygg i att fatta beslut och driva arbetet fram\u00e5t. Du har omd\u00f6me och integritet och kan balansera ett l\u00e5ngsiktigt relationsperspektiv med ambitionen att skapa konkreta resultat. Du f\u00f6rst\u00e5r att framg\u00e5ngsrik fundraising bygger b\u00e5de p\u00e5 att \u00f6ppna nya d\u00f6rrar och p\u00e5 att v\u00e5rda f\u00f6rtroendet hos dem som redan valt att st\u00f6dja universitetet. Du \u00e4r nyfiken p\u00e5 och vill f\u00f6rst\u00e5 fakulteternas och forskarnas skilda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar. Vi erbjuder En strategiskt viktig chefsroll med m\u00f6jlighet att tillsammans med ett erfaret team vidareutveckla Lunds universitets donationsarbete. Du f\u00e5r arbeta n\u00e4ra forskning i internationell framkant och bidra till l\u00e5ngsiktiga relationer som kan g\u00f6ra verklig skillnad f\u00f6r universitetets utveckling och samh\u00e4llet i stort. Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 1 mars 2027 eller efter \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2836 Kontakt Magnus Nilsson, Sektionschef, 046-2220000, magnus.nilsson@fsi.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-04 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-01 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964778/": {"title": "Senior Lecturer in Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives", "description": "Senior Lecturer in Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Department of Building and Environmental Technology at LTH, Lund University, is recruiting an Senior Lecturer. The Division of Risk Management and Societal Safety, within the Department of Building and Environmental Technology, conducts research and education in the field of societal risk and crisis management. The focus of both our research and teaching is to develop knowledge of how individuals, organizations, and societies prevent, prepare for, manage, recover from, learn from, and adapt to events that may threaten something of value. We also conduct research aimed at developing methods, processes, and other types of artefacts that can be used to better understand and manage risks, crises, and disasters across a wide range of contexts. The division currently employs 23 staff members, and an additional 8 individuals are affiliated with the division, such as adjunct faculty staff and industrial PhD students. The division's academic staff and researchers represent a broad range of backgrounds and expertise, including engineering, psychology, and sociology. This position is intended to strengthen the division's capacity in the field of crisis preparedness and management, and civil defence, with a particular focus on social vulnerability. Crisis preparedness and management in general, and civil defence in particular, are areas experiencing rapid growth in Sweden. We anticipate that substantial research funding will be allocated to these fields in the coming years, creating significant opportunities for research and development . Subject Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives Subject description The position of Senior Lecturer primarily involves research and teaching focusing on social vulnerability, power, identity, and critical perspectives on complex crises, both in peacetime and during periods of heightened preparedness. During crises, disasters, and conflicts, different groups in society are affected in different ways depending on their social, economic, and organizational circumstances. Crises often expose and amplify existing inequalities, making it more difficult for some groups to access information, resources, support, and influence over decision-making processes. At the same time, power relations between public authorities, civil society organizations, voluntary initiatives, and individual citizens emerge and evolve, shaping both the distribution of responsibilities and opportunities for different actors to make their voices heard. To understand the societal consequences of crises, it is therefore essential to analyse how different forms of vulnerability are created, reinforced, and managed, as well as how power is exercised, negotiated, and contested during acute events. Such perspectives can contribute to a more nuanced understanding of which groups are at risk of marginalization during crises and which measures are required to create more equitable and inclusive approaches to crisis management and societal resilience. Particular emphasis in this position is placed on qualitative research approaches. The ability to employ qualitative methods to analyse influence, power dynamics, and social relationships is therefore essential. The focus is especially on understanding the factors beyond formal structures and hierarchies that shape how crisis management, emergency preparedness, and civil defence actually function in practice, which may differ considerably from how they have been planned and designed in advance. Furthermore, qualitative research methods are employed in the majority of master's degree projects conducted within the Division of Risk Management and Societal Safety. For this reason, the division seeks to strengthen its competence and capacity in qualitative research methodology. Work duties Work duties include: Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Strategic work aimed at establishing and strengthening collaborations between LTH and relevant national and international partners Qualification requirements Appointment to senior lecturer requires that the applicant has: A PhD or corresponding research competence or professional expertise considered important with regard to the subject matter of the post and the work duties it will involve. Demonstrated teaching expertise. Completed five weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning, or acquired equivalent knowledge by other means, unless there are valid reasons. Assessment criteria When assessing the applicants, special importance will be given to research and teaching expertise within the subject, assessing research and teaching expertise equally. The assessment criteria specify the aspects to be taken into account, and the level to be achieved, in order for the assessment criteria to be deemed fulfilled. The following assessment criteria must be fulfilled for appointment to senior lecturer: A good national and international standing as a researcher. The requirement for international experience shall be assessed with consideration to the character and traditions of the subject. Good teaching ability, including a good ability to conduct, develop and lead teaching and other educational activities on different levels and using a variety of teaching methods. An ability to supervise doctoral students to achieve a PhD. An ability to collaborate with wider society and communicate his or her activities. A general ability to lead and develop activities. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Good oral and written proficiency in Swedish. Experience of teaching, course development, and research using qualitative research methodology. Collaborative skills, initiative and the ability to solve work tasks independently. Other qualifications Significant documented research experience (e.g. from postdoc or doctoral studies) from another university/institute or relevant experience from industry/public sector. Experience of conducting research, both independently and collaboratively, within the fields of crisis preparedness, crisis management, social vulnerability, civil society issues, and critical perspective. The extent to which the applicant, through their experience and skills, may complement and strengthen ongoing research, undergraduate education, departmental innovation, and how they can contribute to the future development of the department will also be taken into consideration. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme.\u00a0\u00a0Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English. Please draw up the application in accordance with LTH\u2019s Academic qualifications portfolio \u2013 see link below. Upload the application as PDF-files in the recruitment system. Read more: http://www.lth.se/english/working-at-lth/to-apply-for-academic-positions-at-lth/ We welcome your application! LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2529 Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364,kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362,st@st.lu.se Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970914/": {"title": "Research Engineer", "description": "Research Engineer Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Research Engineer Login and apply Lunds universitet Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the Research Group The research group for Diabetes and Cardiovascular Disease \u2013 Genetic Epidemiology conducts clinical/epidemiological research in diet, genes, gut microbiome and their connection to type 2 diabetes and other cardiometabolic diseases. Research has been at the forefront of the field of diet, multifactorial genetics and gut microbiota for several years. The group is led by Professor Marju Orho-Melander and consists of both research and technical staff. The activities are located at the Clinical Research Center (CRC) in Malm\u00f6. Within the research group, we care about a good work environment with respect and consideration in our relationships with each other and strive for a workplace that is experienced as developing and stimulating for all employees. We are constantly working to create conditions for job satisfaction, development and participation for all employees. We protect both physical safety and the psychosocial work environment. What We Offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that you are entitled to special benefits, generous annual leave, and a favorable occupational pension. We also have a flextime agreement, which contributes to good conditions for a healthy work\u2013life balance. Read more on the University\u2019s website about being employed at Lund University: Work with us Work duties and areas of responsibility We are looking for a driven research engineer to assist researchers and students in the research group with genetic and bioinformatic analyses of genome wide association data, gut microbiome- and other omics data, and clinical data. Qualifications Requirements for this position: MSc in medical sciences, public health sciences or equivalent. Knowledge and documented experience in epidemiological and genetic/epigenetic analyses and research on type 2 diabetes or related cardiometabolic diseases. Documented programming and statistical analysis skills in both R and Python. Documented experience in analyzing large complex data sets with advanced analysis methods. Experience in working with molecular, clinical, epidemiological and/or lifestyle related data and integrating information from different data sources. Documented experience in summarizing and presenting results in a reproducible report including publication-ready tables and figures, and writing scientific articles. Great importance will be placed on personal qualities. The tasks require that you have good collaboration skills that fit in an interdisciplinary team, that you are self-motivated, flexible and can work independently in a well-documented manner. Other personal qualities required are that you are easy to take initiative, are flexible and have good communication skills. Desirable Qualifications: Experience in scientific data communication of complex quantitative results. Understanding of clinical research questions, experience of patient-facing work and/or clinical education (medical doctor, nurse or other) Additional Information This is a speciall fixed-term employment (S\u00c4VA) for the period 2026-12-01 until 2027-04-30 , at 100 % full-time. How to Apply The position must be applied for through the University\u2019s recruitment system. Your application should include a cover letter describing how you meet the qualification requirements and why you are interested in the position. The application should also include your CV, a copy of your degree certificate, and any other documents you wish to submit in support of your application (such as transcripts, contact details for references, letters of recommendation, etc.). The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Clinical Sciences, Malm\u00f6 is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We have a strong focus on clinical and epidemiological research and also conduct an extensive preclinical laboratory research. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time First day of employment 2026-12-01 Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Malm\u00f6 County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2729 Contact Marju Orho-Melander, Rekryterande chef, +4640391210, marju.orho-melander@med.lu.se Sarah Quist, HR-partner, +4640391055, sarah.quist@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 17.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972522/": {"title": "Researcher in nanowire solar cell development for space applications", "description": "Researcher in nanowire solar cell development for space applications Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Researcher in nanowire solar cell development for space applications Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The position is placed at the Division of Solid-State Physics at the Department of Physics, a division with around 100 employees where extensive research is carried out centered on various aspects of nanophysics, ranging from materials science to bio- and quantum physics to various applications. The division is a central part of NanoLund, Lund University's large interdisciplinary research center on nanoscience and nanotechnology. The research center includes also Lund Nano Lab, a central and shared cleanroom facility for the production of materials and components at the nanoscale. The Division has a strong commitment to undergraduate education, not least in the Master's programme \"Engineering Nanoscience\" at LTH. Work duties In this position, you will be responsible for the development of nanowire solar cells for space applications. The ZEUS project focuses on advancing the development of innovative and radiation-resistant nanowire solar cells with high efficiency. While current space-tested nanowire solar cells offer around 15% efficiency with single-bandgap cells, ZEUS aims to significantly improve this efficiency, potentially up to 47%, by using triple-junction nanowire cells using III-V semiconductor materials. The project aims to achieve scalability by transferring nanowire solar cells to lightweight, flexible substrates. The main objectives include: Increase the efficiency of radiation-resistant nanowire solar cells. Scale up the substrate size to 100 mm^2 and develop modules with a size of 1x1 cm2. Reduce weight and material usage through nanowire peeling and substrate reuse. The project is an EIC pathfinder challenge project, which may require travel for project meetings and collaboration with the other partners within the project. Description of the work duties: The tasks as a researcher mainly include conducting research. The purpose of the position is to develop your independence as a researcher and create conditions for further qualifications. You will work with the synthesis of nanowires, surface passivation and to process these into solar cells for space applications. Characterization of the nanowires and their evaluation with respect to external quantum efficiency (EQE) and current-voltage characterization (IV), also inside a scanning electron microscope, will be part of the project. Qualifications Appointment to a position as a researcher requires that the applicant has a PhD degree. Proof that the eligibility requirement has been met must be received no later than the time the employment decision is made. Required qualifications : a PhD in physics or chemistry very good oral and written proficiency in English. experience in epitaxy, MOVPE and nanowire growth of III-V materials. experience in cleanroom and semiconductor sample processing, like wet chemical etching, photolithography, metal evaporation, etc. strong independence excellent collaboration skills Additional requirements: previous meritorious post doc position, experience of research in a laboratory environment after dissertation. electro-optical characterization of nanowire-based structures (I-V, EQE, PL, EBIC, photocurrent measurements) nano scale device fabrication. material characterisation by use of EDX, SEM, TEM. We Offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee . Further information The position is a fixed term position for 20270116 \u2013 20271230\u00a0 at 100 per cent of full time. Researchers are covered by a local collective agreement on annual working hours for researchers and assistant researchers. The planning of annual working hours is done in dialogue between the manager and the employee. How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University\u2019s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.)\u201d We welcome your application! LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. The Department of Physics is with a staff of about 400 scientists and educators one of the largest departments within Lund University. There are seven research divisions and a number of research centra within the department. The research activities at the department cover a broad spectrum of modern physics. www.fysik.lu.se/english. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Employment expires 2027-12-31 Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-01-16 Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2777 Contact Magnus Borgstr\u00f6m, Professor, +46462221494, magnus.borgstrom@fysik.lu.se Emmy Heidenblad, HR-partner, +46462229294, emmy.heidenblad@lth.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:963933/": {"title": "Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML", "description": "Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace LUNARC is a centre at Lund University providing services in high-performance computing (HPC), visualisation, and data storage. We support researchers across the university with advanced infrastructure, expertise, and training. This position is part of a national investment in AI within the Swedish AI Factory, the Swedish node of the EuroHPC AI Factory initiative. In this role, you will work at the intersection of advanced AI research, research infrastructure, and education, in close collaboration with national and international partners. Work duties As a Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML, you will play a key role in strengthening the use of AI within Swedish research, with a particular focus on education and skills development. Your responsibilities will include: Developing and delivering training activities in AI/ML (courses, workshops, seminars) for LU researchers and users of Swedish AI Factory. Contributing to the development of educational materials and long-term training initiatives in AI Supporting researchers in applying AI methods at Swedish AI Factory resources. Contributing to the development and optimisation of AI workflows on HPC infrastructure Participating in national and international collaborations within Swedish AI Factory and EuroHPC Contributing to outreach and dissemination of knowledge in AI and its applications Qualifications Requirements PhD in a relevant field such as Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Computer Science, Computational Science or other field that the employer finds relevant for the position Documented experience using and developing AI tools and models. Hands-on experience with modern AI frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or equivalent Strong programming skills in Python and experience working in Linux/Unix environments Documented experience in teaching, training, or course development Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with researchers and research groups Excellent communication skills in English, both written and spoken Merits Experience in developing and delivering courses or training programmes in AI/ML Experience working with research infrastructure, e.g. HPC, large-scale storage, or distributed systems Experience supporting users or researchers in AI-related projects Experience from international collaborations, e.g. EU or EuroHPC projects Experience collaborating with industry or public sector organisations Experience with generative AI and large language models Further information The position is a permanent poisition full-time (100%). Start date by agreement, at the latest April 2027. The position is based in Lund, Sweden. Application Applications should be submitted through Lund University\u2019s recruitment system and include a CV, a cover letter describing your qualifications and motivation, and relevant supporting documents. LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment By agreement, at the latest April 2027 Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2512 Contact Jonas Lindemann, Avdelningsf\u00f6rest\u00e5ndare, jonas.lindemann@lunarc.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 01.Oct.2026 Last application date 29.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:969247/": {"title": "Utbildningskoordinator", "description": "Utbildningskoordinator Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Utbildningskoordinator Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Utbildningskoordinator \u00c4r du noggrann, strukturerad och van vid att snabbt s\u00e4tta dig in i administrativa system? Trivs du i en f\u00f6r\u00e4nderlig milj\u00f6 med n\u00e4ra kontakt med studenter och l\u00e4rare? Vi s\u00f6ker dig som \u00e4r serviceinriktad och initiativrik, arbetar v\u00e4l b\u00e5de sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt och tillsammans med andra samt kan prioritera vid h\u00f6g arbetsbelastning. D\u00e5 kan du vara den utbildningskoordinator vi s\u00f6ker till Institutionen f\u00f6r psykologi. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Som utbildningskoordinator ansvarar du f\u00f6r att planera, organisera, administrera och samordna olika aspekter av utbildning s\u00e5 som antagningsarbete, studiedokumentation och studieplanering. Du har b\u00e5de ett helhets- och detaljperspektiv. Du samarbetar med kollegor f\u00f6r att bedriva och utveckla utbildning och processer. Arbetet sker i olika administrativa team. Arbetet inneb\u00e4r exempelvis att: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0planera och genomf\u00f6ra antagningsarbete \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0ansvara f\u00f6r utbildnings- och studieadministration i universitetets administrativa system \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0handl\u00e4gga studieadministrativa \u00e4renden och utf\u00e4rda intyg \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0ge information, service och st\u00f6d till nuvarande och presumtiva studenter \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0uppdatera utbildningsinformation p\u00e5 webben \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0administrera utbildningsutbud, kurser och kursplaner \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0bidra till utveckling av utbildningsadministrativa processer och arbetss\u00e4tt \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0till\u00e4mpa regler och riktlinjer inom utbildningsomr\u00e5det \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0hantera dokumentation, informationshantering och diarief\u00f6ring \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0samverka med l\u00e4rare, studierektorer, program- och kursansvariga samt \u00f6vriga administrativa funktioner \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0delta i relevanta interna n\u00e4tverk inom Lunds universitet \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0ansvara f\u00f6r viss samordning inom ekonomiadministrativa system \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0 koordinera, administrera och \u00e5terrapportera anst\u00e4llningsformer samt samordna avtals- och anst\u00e4llningsfr\u00e5gor med studierektor, kursansvariga, ekonomiansvarig och anst\u00e4llda \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0 boka resor/hotell. Kvalifikationer Krav: \u2022\u00a0 \u00a0 Kandidatexamen inom samh\u00e4llsvetenskapligt \u00e4mne, eller annan utbildning/erfarenhet som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer som likv\u00e4rdig \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0God f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka dig p\u00e5 svenska och engelska i tal och skrift \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0God datorvana och erfarenhet av att arbeta i IT-system och digitala verktyg Meriterande: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av administrativa och/eller koordinerande arbetsuppgifter \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Erfarenhet av serviceinriktat arbete \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Personliga egenskaper som initiativtagande, ansvarstagande och att vara utvecklingsorienterad samt god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att snabbt s\u00e4tta dig in i nya arbetsuppgifter, ta till dig instruktioner och se b\u00e5de helhet och detaljer Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Institutionen f\u00f6r psykologi \u00e4r en hybrid arbetsplats d\u00e4r m\u00f6jlighet att arbeta p\u00e5 distans upp till 2 dagar i veckan finns. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld vid Lunds universitet: Jobba hos oss. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en tillsvidaretj\u00e4nst med tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Provanst\u00e4llning p\u00e5 6 m\u00e5nader kan komma att till\u00e4mpas . Tj\u00e4nstens uppgifter kan komma att f\u00f6r\u00e4ndras \u00f6ver tid. Ans\u00f6kan Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra f\u00f6r forskning och utbildning inom samh\u00e4lls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg, \u00f6ver 700 anst\u00e4llda och cirka 5 700 hel\u00e5rsstudenter \u00e4r fakulteten en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. V\u00e5r huvuduppgift \u00e4r att utveckla, f\u00f6rmedla och f\u00f6rvalta kunskap om samh\u00e4lle, m\u00e4nniska och organisationer i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av \u00f6ppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Institutionen f\u00f6r psykologi kombinerar utbildning med forskning och har under senare \u00e5r varit mycket framg\u00e5ngsrik i konkurrensen om externa forskningsmedel. Centrala forskningsomr\u00e5den \u00e4r bl.a. arbets- och organisationspsykologi, klinisk psykologi, kognition, neuropsykologi, personlighet- och social psykologi samt utvecklingspsykologi. M\u00e5nga av v\u00e5ra kurser \u00e4r utvecklade i anslutning till forskningsprojekt och studenterna f\u00e5r m\u00f6jlighet att ta del av aktuella forskningsr\u00f6n fr\u00e5n l\u00e4rare som sj\u00e4lva \u00e4r aktiva forskare inom sina respektive omr\u00e5den. V\u00e5r utbildningsmilj\u00f6 \u00e4r sedan l\u00e4nge starkt internationaliserad. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidare med provanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-01 L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2686 Kontakt Caroline Hansson, HR-Administrat\u00f6r, caroline.hansson@sam.lu.se Sofia Bunke, Prefekt, +46462221537, sofia.bunke@psy.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-01 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973191/": {"title": "Ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r till medicinska institutionskansliet i Malm\u00f6", "description": "Ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r till medicinska institutionskansliet i Malm\u00f6 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r till medicinska institutionskansliet i Malm\u00f6 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Medicinska fakulteten Inst f\u00f6r kliniska vetenskaper Malm\u00f6 Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Medicinska institutionskansliet i Malm\u00f6 \u00e4r ett gemensamt kansli f\u00f6r tv\u00e5 av Medicinska fakultetens institutioner vilka \u00e4r placerade i Malm\u00f6; Institutionen f\u00f6r kliniska vetenskaper Malm\u00f6 och Institutionen f\u00f6r translationell medicin. H\u00e4r finns patientn\u00e4ra forskningsmilj\u00f6er f\u00f6r de forskargrupper som \u00e4r aktiva vid institutionerna. Dessa har sammanlagt ca 400 anst\u00e4llda, d\u00e4ribland \u00e4ven associerade medarbetare som \u00e4r anst\u00e4llda inom Region Sk\u00e5ne. Institutionerna bedriver forskning och utbildning, b\u00e5de inom medicinsk grundutbildning och forskarutbildning Kansliets huvudsakliga uppgift \u00e4r att avlasta k\u00e4rnverksamheten och m\u00f6jligg\u00f6ra forskning och utbildning av h\u00f6g kvalitet. Kansliet ansvarar f\u00f6r att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla att l\u00e4ros\u00e4tet uppfyller b\u00e5de externa krav och lagar samt interna regler och riktlinjer. Arbetet bedrivs med fokus p\u00e5 att anv\u00e4nda resurserna effektivt utifr\u00e5n verksamhetens behov och tillg\u00e4ngliga medel. Kansliet \u00e4r placerat p\u00e5 Clinical Research Center (CRC) i Malm\u00f6 och best\u00e5r idag av 11 personer, vilka jobbar inom ekonomi, HR, administration och kommunikation och leds av en administrativ chef. Inom v\u00e5rt kansli v\u00e4rnar vi om en god arbetsmilj\u00f6 med respekt och omtanke i v\u00e5ra relationer med varandra och vi arbetar st\u00e4ndigt f\u00f6r att skapa \u00e4nnu b\u00e4ttre f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r arbetsgl\u00e4dje, utveckling och delaktighet f\u00f6r alla medarbetare. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara anst\u00e4lld vid Lunds universitet Jobba hos oss Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Som ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r kommer du ha en stor bredd av olika arbetsuppgifter och rollen \u00e4r omv\u00e4xlande och sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndig. Vi s\u00f6ker dig som uppskattar att arbeta med ekonomiadministration i s\u00e5v\u00e4l stort som sm\u00e5tt. I rollen som ekonomiadministrat\u00f6r kommer du bland annat vara granskare av reser\u00e4kningar samt \u00e4ven uppr\u00e4tta reser\u00e4kningar, hantera v\u00e5rt anl\u00e4ggningsregister inkluderande administration vid \u00e5rlig inventering, hantera diarief\u00f6ring, hantera fakturering och rekvirering, ekonomiska avst\u00e4mningar, arvodering, hantera stipendier samt andra ekonomiadministrativa arbetsuppgifter. Du kommer vara st\u00f6d till chefer, forskare och andra medarbetare i ekonomiadministrativa fr\u00e5gor. Dina arbetsuppgifter kan \u00e4ven komma att innefatta andra administrativa arbetsuppgifter som kan f\u00f6rekomma p\u00e5 v\u00e5rt kansli. I takt med verksamhetens f\u00f6r\u00e4ndrade behov kan tj\u00e4nstens inneh\u00e5ll utvecklas och f\u00f6r\u00e4ndras \u00f6ver tid. Kvalifikationer F\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen kr\u00e4vs: L\u00e4gst gymnasiekompetens. Fler\u00e5rig erfarenhet av ekonomiadministrativt arbete s\u00e5som bokf\u00f6ring, hantera reskontra, hantera avst\u00e4mningar. Erfarenhet av att arbeta i olika ekonomisystem. Mycket god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt. Mycket god kommunikativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga. God f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka dig p\u00e5 svenska och engelska i b\u00e5de tal och skrift. God samarbets-, service- och initiativf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, noggrann, flexibel, strukturerad och van att arbeta med flera arbetsuppgifter parallellt. God datorvana och erfarenhet av IT-system och verktyg, inklusive Office 365 och olika administrativa system. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Tidigare erfarenhet av ekonomiadministrativa och administrativa system inom universitets- och h\u00f6gskolesektorn eller annan offentlig sektor. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning p\u00e5 100 %, med tilltr\u00e4de 1 januari 2027. Provanst\u00e4llning i sex m\u00e5nader kan komma att till\u00e4mpas. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.) Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Medicinska fakulteten \u00e4r ett verksamhetsomr\u00e5de inom Lunds universitet, med ansvar f\u00f6r utbildning och forskning inom medicin, v\u00e5rd och h\u00e4lsa. Utbildningen sker i n\u00e4ra samverkan med sjukv\u00e5rden och \u00e4r v\u00e4l f\u00f6rankrad i fakultetens starka forskningstradition. Fakultetens forskning sp\u00e4nner \u00f6ver ett brett f\u00e4lt inom experimentell grundforskning, patientn\u00e4ra klinisk forskning och h\u00e4lsovetenskaplig forskning. Medicinska fakulteten, med drygt 1800 anst\u00e4llda och 3000 studenter i Lund, Malm\u00f6 och Helsingborg, \u00e4r en kunskapsintensiv m\u00f6tesplats f\u00f6r studenter, l\u00e4rare och forskare fr\u00e5n hela v\u00e4rlden. Institutionen f\u00f6r kliniska vetenskaper i Malm\u00f6 \u00e4r en av de sex institutionerna vid Lunds universitets medicinska fakultet. Vi har ett starkt fokus p\u00e5 klinisk och epidemiologisk forskning, och bedriver \u00e4ven en omfattande preklinisk laboratorieforskning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidare med provanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 1 januari 2027 L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Malm\u00f6 L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2793 Kontakt Katarina Westrin Sj\u00f6berg, Rekryterande chef, +4640391050, katarina.westrin_sjoberg@med.lu.se Sarah Quist, HR-partner, +4640391055, sarah.quist@med.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-01 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-16 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974401/": {"title": "Universitetsadjunkt i offentlig r\u00e4tt", "description": "Universitetsadjunkt i offentlig r\u00e4tt Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetsadjunkt i offentlig r\u00e4tt Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett fullskaligt och forskningsintensivt universitet, och ing\u00e5r som enda svenska universitet i de starka internationella n\u00e4tverken League of European Research Universities (LERU) och Universitas 21 (U21). Lunds universitet har partneruniversitet i n\u00e4rmare 70 l\u00e4nder, och attraherar flest internationella studenter av alla svenska universitet. Juridiska fakulteten k\u00e4nnetecknas av internationalisering, sammanfl\u00e4tning av utbildning och forskning, tv\u00e4rvetenskap samt n\u00e4ra och gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande samverkan med det omgivande samh\u00e4llet. Fakultetens forskningsmilj\u00f6 och utbildning p\u00e5 forskarniv\u00e5 pr\u00e4glas av internationalisering, och vid sidan av juristprogrammet erbjuds ocks\u00e5 flera internationella mastersprogram. Lunds universitet och den Juridiska fakulteten erbjuder en utvecklande och inkluderande arbetsmilj\u00f6 i den bredare dynamiska vetenskaps- och innovationsregion som \u00d6resundsregionen utg\u00f6r. \u00c4mne Offentlig r\u00e4tt \u00c4mnesbeskrivning Offentlig r\u00e4tt omfattar den del av juridiken som r\u00f6r maktut\u00f6vningen i riksdag, regering, kommuner och annan offentlig f\u00f6rvaltning. Till den offentliga r\u00e4tten r\u00e4knas framf\u00f6r allt \u00e4mnena statsr\u00e4tt (konstitutionell r\u00e4tt), allm\u00e4n f\u00f6rvaltningsr\u00e4tt inklusive f\u00f6rvaltningsprocessr\u00e4tt, kommunalr\u00e4tt samt omr\u00e5den inom speciell f\u00f6rvaltningsr\u00e4tt. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna inneb\u00e4r att genom undervisning vidareutveckla en stimulerande utbildningsmilj\u00f6. I arbetsuppgifterna ing\u00e5r undervisning inom ramen f\u00f6r juristprogrammets grundniv\u00e5 och avancerade niv\u00e5. Det kan ocks\u00e5 ing\u00e5 undervisning inom ramen f\u00f6r fakultetens distans- och uppdragsutbildningar. Undervisningen omfattar fr\u00e4mst f\u00f6rel\u00e4sningar, seminarier, uppsatshandledning, kursutveckling och administration samt att utarbeta och spela in videof\u00f6rel\u00e4sningar. \u00c4ven annan undervisning kan ing\u00e5. D\u00e4rut\u00f6ver innefattar arbetsuppgifterna att aktivt verka f\u00f6r en pedagogisk utveckling av utbildningen p\u00e5 grund- och avancerad niv\u00e5. Undervisningen sker i huvudsak p\u00e5 svenska men engelska kan \u00e4ven f\u00f6rekomma. De \u00e4mnesomr\u00e5den som fr\u00e4mst aktualiseras \u00e4r allm\u00e4n f\u00f6rvaltningsr\u00e4tt, inklusive f\u00f6rvaltningsprocessr\u00e4tt, kommunalr\u00e4tt, statsr\u00e4tt och milj\u00f6r\u00e4tt inklusive speciell fastighetsr\u00e4tt. Som universitetsadjunkt f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas du undervisa brett inom i f\u00f6rsta hand juristprogrammet samt annan utbildningsverksamhet vid fakulteten. Arbetsuppgifterna utf\u00f6rs i n\u00e4ra samarbete med studenter, doktorander, l\u00e4rare och forskare s\u00e5v\u00e4l vid Lunds universitet som vid andra l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten samt med andra externa akt\u00f6rer. Beh\u00f6righet Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som universitetsadjunkt \u00e4r den som dels har visat pedagogisk skicklighet, dels har avlagt juristexamen eller p\u00e5 annat inh\u00e4mtat motsvarande kunskaper samt har annan kompetens som \u00e4r av betydelse med h\u00e4nsyn till anst\u00e4llningens \u00e4mnesinriktning och de arbetsuppgifter som ing\u00e5r i anst\u00e4llningen. F\u00f6r universitetsadjunkt g\u00e4ller som allm\u00e4nt beh\u00f6righetskrav att vara l\u00e4mplig f\u00f6r och ha den f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga i \u00f6vrigt som beh\u00f6vs f\u00f6r att v\u00e4l fullg\u00f6ra arbetsuppgifterna i den aktuella anst\u00e4llningen. Enligt Lunds universitets anst\u00e4llningsordning m\u00e5ste den s\u00f6kande \u00e4ven ha genomg\u00e5tt h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller p\u00e5 annat s\u00e4tt ha inh\u00e4mtat motsvarande kunskaper f\u00f6r att vara beh\u00f6rig. Om det finns s\u00e4rskilda sk\u00e4l kan den som inte har h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor \u00e4nd\u00e5 anses vara beh\u00f6rig. Bed\u00f6mningsgrunder Som bed\u00f6mningsgrunder vid anst\u00e4llning av en universitetsadjunkt ska graden av s\u00e5dan skicklighet som \u00e4r ett krav f\u00f6r beh\u00f6righet f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llning g\u00e4lla. Vid anst\u00e4llning som universitetsadjunkt ska f\u00f6ljande utg\u00f6ra grund f\u00f6r bed\u00f6mning: Goda och breda \u00e4mneskunskaper av relevans f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningens inneh\u00e5ll och de arbetsuppgifter som ing\u00e5r God pedagogisk f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, vilket inneb\u00e4r god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att bedriva och utveckla undervisning och annan pedagogisk verksamhet p\u00e5 olika niv\u00e5er och med varierande undervisningsmetoder Mycket god yrkeserfarenhet eller annan erfarenhet av relevans f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen Synnerligen god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att undervisa p\u00e5 svenska eller annat skandinaviskt spr\u00e5k p\u00e5 juristprogrammet \u00e4r ett krav liksom f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att undervisa p\u00e5 engelska S\u00e4rskild vikt kommer att f\u00e4stas vid: Stor bredd inom de \u00e4mnesomr\u00e5den som f\u00f6rekommer inom juristprogrammet Goda \u00e4mneskunskaper i processr\u00e4tt, milj\u00f6r\u00e4tt och fastighetsr\u00e4tt Omfattande och kvalificerad yrkeserfarenhet som jurist Dokumenterad och aktuell erfarenhet av att undervisa i juridik p\u00e5 grund- och avancerad niv\u00e5 Vikt kommer att f\u00e4stas vid: Administrativ och annan skicklighet samt personliga f\u00f6rm\u00e5gor som \u00e4r av betydelse f\u00f6r att fullg\u00f6ra arbetsuppgifterna v\u00e4l. N\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga personliga f\u00f6rm\u00e5gor \u00e4r exempelvis god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndighet samt att vara initiativtagande och drivande F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att samverka med det omgivande samh\u00e4llet Anvisningar f\u00f6r ans\u00f6kan Ans\u00f6kan till anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks elektroniskt via Lunds universitets s\u00f6kandeportal. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla f\u00f6ljande: Personligt brev Kortfattad curriculum vitae (CV) Fullst\u00e4ndig publikationslista upp till fem vetenskapliga publikationer kan bil\u00e4ggas ans\u00f6kan Beskrivning av pedagogiska meriter med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning av den pedagogiska verksamheten, kort pedagogisk sj\u00e4lvreflektion, pedagogisk meritf\u00f6rteckning) Beskrivning av meriter r\u00f6rande ledarskap och administration med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning, kort sj\u00e4lvreflektion och meritf\u00f6rteckning av administrativa erfarenheter och ledningsuppdrag) Beskrivning av meriter r\u00f6rande samverkan med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning, kort sj\u00e4lvreflektion och meritf\u00f6rteckning av insatser och \u00e5taganden r\u00f6rande samverkan) \u00d6vriga handlingar som s\u00f6kanden \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa V\u00e4nligen notera att de handlingar som inkommer eller uppr\u00e4ttas med anledning av denna ledigf\u00f6rklarade anst\u00e4llning (s\u00e5som ans\u00f6kningar, sakkunnigutl\u00e5tanden och protokoll) som huvudregel \u00e4r allm\u00e4nna och d\u00e4rmed offentliga. Detta inneb\u00e4r att handlingarna f\u00e5r (med undantag f\u00f6r sekretessbelagda handlingar) l\u00e4sas av den som s\u00e5 beg\u00e4r det. Villkor Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Juridiska fakulteten \u00e4r en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 och avancerad niv\u00e5 och ett 160-tal anst\u00e4llda varav ett 40-tal \u00e4r doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns p\u00e5 v\u00e5r hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2837 Kontakt Jenny Lindskog, HR-chef, +46462221004, jenny.lindskog@jur.lu.se Ellika Sevelin, Prefekt, 0462221099, ellika.sevelin@jur.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-01 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-12 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968024/": {"title": "Postdoctoral position in Electrical Engineering focusing on Nanoelectronics and Cryogenic and Ferroelectric materials", "description": "Postdoctoral position in Electrical Engineering focusing on Nanoelectronics and Cryogenic and Ferroelectric materials Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral position in Electrical Engineering focusing on Nanoelectronics and Cryogenic and Ferroelectric materials Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Department of Electrical and Information Technology (EIT) at Lund University, The Faculty of Engineering (LTH), is one of the larger departments with about 120 employees and conducts research and teaching mainly in electrical engineering and computer technology. We are located on LTH's campus in northern Lund. Within the Division of Electromagnetics and Nanoelectronics we develop and study new generations of electronics based on advanced semiconductor technology. In particular, we develop and characterize new generations of electronic and optoelectronic devices based on III-V technology. Part of the effort is related to exploratory material investigations for cryogenic applications. Subject description Ferroelectric materials like HZO show promising properties at cryogenic temperatures with strong polarization and attractive switching characteristics. The interface properties play a critical role but the reduced thermal activation allows different optimization criteria. We will introduce new ALD materials and evaluate their use at the ferroelectric interfaces. The research will be performed in collaboration with researchers within the competence centre ACT and within the strategic research areas in Advanced materials. Work duties The main duties involved in a postdoctoral position is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position includes the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. The purpose of the position is to develop the independence as a researcher and to create the opportunity of further development. You will be responsible for the investigations of novel interface structures for cryogenic ferroelectric operation. The studies will also include structural characterization at the synchrotron beam lines. Some of the work may be carried out at Brunnsh\u00f6g, close to the large infrastructures MAX IV and ESS. Detailed description of the work duties: Design of experiment and sample preparation. ALD deposition of ferroelectric films. Measurements, data analysis and interpretation. Structural interface characterization. Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Appointment to a postdoctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position. The certificate proving the qualification requirement is met, must be received before the employment decision is made. Priority will be given to candidates who have graduated no more than three years ago before the last day for application. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: Documented experience in material deposition techniques. Experience in clean-room processing. Documented experience in structural film characterization, preferable using synchrotron based techniques. Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Good ability to work with others. Good ability to work independently. Assessment criteria This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a postdoctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high quality research. Teaching skills. Other qualifications: Experience in ALD technology. Consideration will also be given to how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee . Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of two years, the start date is as soon as possible by agreement, however no later than April 1, 2027. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d). How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University\u2019s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.)\u201d We welcome your application! About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible by agreement, however no later than April 1, 2027 Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2649 Contact Lars-Erik Wernersson, Professor, +46462229003, lars-erik.wernersson@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 30.Sep.2026 Last application date 21.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970808/": {"title": "Doctoral student in Astronomy and Astrophysics", "description": "Doctoral student in Astronomy and Astrophysics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Astronomy and Astrophysics Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Planet Formation Group at the Department of Physics (Division of Astrophysics) at Lund University is seeking a PhD student to work on models of planet formation on a galactic scale. Research within the division encompasses galaxy formation, galactic dynamics and evolution, star formation and dynamics, stellar evolution, stellar spectroscopy and astrometry, planet formation and dynamics, as well as exoplanet atmospheres. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at the Faculty of Science at naturvetenskap.se . Allm\u00e4n studieplan f\u00f6r forskarutbildning Work duties We are seeking a PhD student in theoretical astrophysics. The PhD student will study how planets form at different times and in different regions of our galaxy. The PhD student will also calculate how certain planetesimals are ejected from planetary systems to become free-flying interstellar planetesimals. The PhD project will give astronomers new insight into where interstellar comets came from. Your primary responsibility will be to pursue your doctoral studies, which will mainly consist of conducting research and writing a doctoral thesis. In addition, you will be expected to: Conduct research within the subject area. Publish results in high-quality scientific journals. Present research results at national and international conferences. In addition, you are expected to participate in doctoral courses, seminars and conferenes. In addition to studies, a maximum of 20% of working time may be spent on teaching and other departmental work Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific admission requirements To be admitted to the third-cycle programme in Astronomy and Astrophysics the student must have earned credits in first and second-cycle programmes in which physics, mathematics and/or corresponding engineering subjects have been substantial elements. In addition to 60 credits in basic physics, there is a requirement for at least 60 credits in subjects of relevance to Astronomy and Astrophysics, e.g., courses in astronomy or other physics subjects, or engineering subjects such as space technology and automatic control. The 120 credits must include at least 60 second-cycle credits. Equivalent knowledge acquired through corresponding programmes will be assessed individually. In order to enable interdisciplinary initiatives and important specialisations in certain areas, students with qualifications in subjects other than Astronomy and Astrophysics may be considered for admission. Finally, the student must be judged to have the potential to complete the programme. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Strong ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle scientific problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Strong collaborative and teamwork skills. Very good proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Merits Experience in analyzing and working with models of planet formation or galaxy formation Excellent numerical and analytical problem-solving skills, as well as experience with programming languages (e.g. Python and Fortran). Extensive knowledge of galaxy formation and galaxy formation. Selection criteria The selection of eligible applicants will be made taking into account the ability to benefit from the training based on the following criteria: Relevant qualifications and expertise (see the requirements and merit criteria listed above). Demonstrated ability to handle complex research problems and to work both collaboratively and independently, as well as to complete tasks on schedule. Consideration will also be given to strong collaborative skills, motivation, and independence, as well as to how the applicant\u2019s experience and qualifications demonstrate the abilities required to successfully complete doctoral studies. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se. About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as agreed. Third cycle studies consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staffpages . Other Any other information such as where and when interviews will be held. How to apply The application should be written in English and you must attach to your application: CV and personal letter with a justification of why you are interested in the training place/employment and in what way the research project matches your interests and your educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or diplomas. These should prove your basic and special eligibility for the doctoral education subject and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral education project. Other information that you wish to refer to (copies of grades, information for references, letters of recommendation, etc.). We welcome your application. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. The Department of Physics is one of Lund University's largest departments with approximately 400 employees. The department is shared between the Faculty of Science and Faculty of Engineering. At the department there are seven research divisions and a number of major research centra. The research at the department covers a wide range of modern physics. www.fysik.lu.se/en/ We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment After agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2727 Contact Anders Johansen, Professor, anders.johansen@fysik.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 29.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Dec.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:971322/": {"title": "Bibliotekarie till Universitetsbiblioteket", "description": "Bibliotekarie till Universitetsbiblioteket - Statlig visstidsanst\u00e4llning Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Bibliotekarie till Universitetsbiblioteket - Statlig visstidsanst\u00e4llning Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Kravprofil Avdelning Samlingar ansvarar f\u00f6r universitetsbibliotekets fysiska samlingar, inklusive tillg\u00e4ngligg\u00f6rande f\u00f6r anv\u00e4ndarna. Avdelningen hanterar donationsf\u00f6rfr\u00e5gningar och ink\u00f6p, samt st\u00f6der fakulteternas dep\u00e5l\u00e4ggning av material. Arbetet utf\u00f6rs b\u00e5de p\u00e5 Universitetsbiblioteket och p\u00e5 v\u00e5ra dep\u00e5er. P\u00e5 avdelningen arbetar cirka 20 personer, uppdelade i olika team. Team Vardagstryck, d\u00e4r denna tj\u00e4nst \u00e4r placerad, hanterar de lagstadgade pliktleveranserna av vardagstryck, som utg\u00f6r en stor del av v\u00e5ra samlingar. Vardagstryck \u00e4r material fr\u00e5n f\u00f6retag, institutioner, organisationer och f\u00f6reningar som till exempel reklam, broschyrer, medlemsinformation, personaltidskrifter, \u00e5rsredovisningar och affischer. Teamet ansvarar f\u00f6r att ordna och tillg\u00e4ngligg\u00f6ra detta material f\u00f6r anv\u00e4ndarna. Hos oss arbetar vi f\u00f6r en god arbetsmilj\u00f6. H\u00e4r kan du l\u00e4sa mer om Universitetsbiblioteket. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Universitetsbiblioteket har beviljats medel till ett 2-\u00e5rigt projekt f\u00f6r att arbeta med ouppordnat material (restantier). Vi s\u00f6ker nu en bibliotekarie f\u00f6r att arbeta med att ordna vardagstryck. Arbetet passar dig som gillar struktur, och vill bidra till att tillg\u00e4ngligg\u00f6ra detta sp\u00e4nnande material. Det kan bli aktuellt med schemalagda pass i n\u00e5gon av v\u00e5ra informationsdiskar, d\u00e4r du m\u00f6ter anv\u00e4ndarna. Arbetsveckan \u00e4r f\u00f6rdelad mellan Universitetsbiblioteket Helgonabacken, och UB:s dep\u00e5 f\u00f6r vardagstryck. Periodvis kan arbetet vara fysiskt kr\u00e4vande, med hantering av tungt material. Du arbetar i ett team av kollegor med liknande arbetsuppgifter. Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen Examen i biblioteks- och informationsvetenskap eller likv\u00e4rdig annan utbildning som av arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6ms som relevant Goda kunskaper om det svenska samh\u00e4llet och det svenska medielandskapet Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska (tal och skrift) Goda kunskaper i engelska (tal och skrift) Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen B-k\u00f6rkort f\u00f6r manuell v\u00e4xel (f\u00f6r vissa transporter kan det bli aktuellt att k\u00f6ra n\u00e5gon av universitetsbibliotekets bilar) Erfarenhet av arbete i forskningsbibliotek Personliga egenskaper Vi s\u00f6ker dig som: Har ett noggrant och systematiskt arbetss\u00e4tt Snabbt kan s\u00e4tta dig in i nya omr\u00e5den och komplexa uppgifter Har god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och Kan arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt/har ett gott sj\u00e4lvledarskap. Stor vikt kommer att l\u00e4ggas vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en visstidsanst\u00e4llning p\u00e5 100 procent under 2 \u00e5r, med tilltr\u00e4de snarast. Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer om att arbeta hos oss p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du: Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. I ans\u00f6kan skriver du inget personligt brev. I st\u00e4llet ans\u00f6ker du genom att bifoga ett CV som beskriver dina meriter f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten, samt genom att besvara ett antal urvalsfr\u00e5gor kopplade till anst\u00e4llningen. Universitetsbiblioteket vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett tv\u00e4rvetenskapligt bibliotek med bas i omfattande samlingar av s\u00e5v\u00e4l tryckt som elektroniskt material. Biblioteket erbjuder ocks\u00e5 en studiemilj\u00f6 med cirka 400 l\u00e4splatser. Universitetsbiblioteket har cirka 100 anst\u00e4llda. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de Snarast L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2747 Kontakt Miriam Bj\u00f6rkhem, Avdelningschef, 046-2229810, miriam.bjorkhem@ub.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-29 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-19 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972485/": {"title": "Ekonom vid Institutionen f\u00f6r energivetenskaper", "description": "Ekonom vid Institutionen f\u00f6r energivetenskaper Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Ekonom vid Institutionen f\u00f6r energivetenskaper Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Tj\u00e4nsten som ekonom \u00e4r placerad vid Institutionen f\u00f6r energivetenskaper, LTH, Lunds universitet. V\u00e5rt uppdrag \u00e4r att forska och utbilda om hur energisystemen kan utvecklas f\u00f6r en h\u00e5llbar framtid. Institutionen har en omfattande experimentell verksamhet bland annat best\u00e5ende av ett av Europas st\u00f6rsta drivlinelaboratorier med 13 testceller med motorer, br\u00e4nsleceller och hybrida system, en unik h\u00f6gtrycksrigg f\u00f6r gasturbintestning, samt jetmotorriggar. Institutionen har \u00e4ven omfattande verksamhet med avancerad modellutveckling och simuleringar av olika energisystem och energirelaterade processer. Utbildningsverksamheten \u00e4r omfattande och vi ser det som ett hedersuppdrag att vara en del av unga m\u00e4nniskors utveckling till v\u00e4lutbildade och attraktiva medarbetare inom n\u00e4ringsliv och samh\u00e4lle. Som ekonom ing\u00e5r du i institutionens administrativa grupp, som svarar f\u00f6r administrativt verksamhetsn\u00e4ra st\u00f6d till den undervisande och forskande personalen p\u00e5 institutionen. Tillsammans med den tekniska personalen omfattar det teknisk-/administrativa st\u00f6det sju personer, och gruppens arbete och attityd genomsyras av ett genuint servicet\u00e4nk. En positiv och tillm\u00f6tesg\u00e5ende stomme, som driver och utvecklar processer f\u00f6r att ge bra, kontinuerlig och effektiv service till ledningen, institutionen och dess medarbetare. Verksamheten i sin helhet \u00e4r v\u00e4lm\u00e5ende och vi har tillsammans en oerh\u00f6rt sp\u00e4nnande framtid inom energiomr\u00e5det som \u00e4r s\u00e5 viktig f\u00f6r samh\u00e4llets utveckling. Vill du vara en del av en verksamhet som bidrar till samh\u00e4llsutvecklingen och en h\u00e5llbar framtid? Arbetsuppgifter Vi s\u00f6ker en ekonom som tar ett helhetsansvar f\u00f6r institutionens ekonomiska struktur och rutiner samt deltar i verksamhetsplaneringen. I detta ing\u00e5r ekonomisk planering och budgetarbete f\u00f6r institutionen som helhet, s\u00e5v\u00e4l som enskilda mindre och st\u00f6rre forskningsprojekt. Du sk\u00f6ter l\u00f6pande bokf\u00f6ring och g\u00f6r ekonomisk uppf\u00f6ljning av helhet och delar, bland annat genom f\u00e4rdigst\u00e4llande och analys av bokslut. Projektst\u00f6d till forskarna i alla faser s\u00e5som; ans\u00f6kning, rapportering, uppf\u00f6ljning, samt h\u00e5ller dig informerad om olika bidragsgivares och andra f\u00f6r yrkesrollen relevanta regelverk. Du analyserar verksamheten och dess f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar och g\u00f6r prognoser p\u00e5 b\u00e5de kort och l\u00e5ng sikt. I anst\u00e4llningen ing\u00e5r \u00e4ven att ansvara f\u00f6r anl\u00e4ggningsregister och inventering, samt fakturering och kontraktshantering. Vi har internationella medarbetare och kontakter, s\u00e5 engelska anv\u00e4nds dagligen. Kvalifikationer F\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten kr\u00e4vs: ekonomisk utbildning p\u00e5 h\u00f6gskoleniv\u00e5, g\u00e4rna civilekonom. god ekonomisk kompetens och erfarenhet g\u00e4llande ekonomisk planering, bokf\u00f6ring, redovisning och uppf\u00f6ljning/analys. vana vid redovisningssystem och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att ta till sig nya tekniska system. goda kunskaper i Excel p\u00e5 avancerad niv\u00e5 och i Word. god pedagogisk och kommunikativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga n\u00e4r du f\u00f6rklarar ekonomi f\u00f6r icke-ekonomer. mycket god kunskap i svenska och god engelska, i tal och skrift. Meriterande f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r: bred erfarenhet fr\u00e5n kvalificerat ekonomiarbete. erfarenheter av prognosskapande. kunskap om statliga regelverk inom det ekonomiska omr\u00e5det. erfarenhet fr\u00e5n ekonomihantering inom offentlig verksamhet eller stora organisationer. kunskap om EU-projekt. Vi l\u00e4gger stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. Vi s\u00f6ker en ekonom som \u00e4r analytisk, pedagogisk, noggrann, strukturerad, serviceinriktad, och som \u00e4r bra p\u00e5 att samarbeta och ta initiativ, samt har f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att se helheter och sammanhang. Vi kommer \u00e4ven att ta h\u00e4nsyn till hur den s\u00f6kande genom sin erfarenhet och kompetens bed\u00f6ms komplettera och st\u00e4rka institutionen samt bidra till dess framtida utveckling. Villkor Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning med omfattning 100%. Provanst\u00e4llning kan bli aktuell. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla ett personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc). Du kommer att f\u00e5 besvara urvalsfr\u00e5gor i systemet. Om Lunds Tekniska H\u00f6gskola LTH \u2013 Lunds Tekniska H\u00f6gskola \u2013 \u00e4r en del av Lunds universitet. P\u00e5 LTH utbildar vi m\u00e4nniskor, bygger kunskap f\u00f6r framtiden och arbetar h\u00e5rt f\u00f6r att utveckla samh\u00e4llet. Vi skapar utrymme f\u00f6r briljant forskning och inspirerar till kreativ utveckling av teknik, arkitektur och design. H\u00e4r l\u00e4ser n\u00e4rmare 12 000 studenter. Varje \u00e5r publicerar v\u00e5ra forskare \u2013 varav m\u00e5nga verkar inom v\u00e4rldsledande profilomr\u00e5den \u2013 omkring 100 avhandlingar och 2 000 vetenskapliga r\u00f6n. En rad forskningsresultat och studentarbeten f\u00f6r\u00e4dlas till innovationer. Tillsammans utforskar och skapar vi \u2013 till nytta f\u00f6r v\u00e4rlden. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de Snarast enligt \u00f6k L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2775 Kontakt Martin Tun\u00e9r, +46462224050, martin.tuner@energy.lth.se Publicerat 2026-09-29 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-22 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973268/": {"title": "Universitetslektor", "description": "Universitetslektor Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetslektor Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Institutionen f\u00f6r kulturgeografi och ekonomisk geografi \u00e4r i behov av en tidsbegr\u00e4nsad universitetslektor med en omfattning om 100% under perioden 1 januari 2027 till och med 26 december 2027. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna omfattar undervisning och handledning i humanekologi. Undervisning och handledning inom kulturgeografi och ekonomisk geografi kan ocks\u00e5 f\u00f6rekomma. Administrativa uppgifter kan ocks\u00e5 utg\u00f6ra en del av arbetsuppgifterna. Undervisning och handledning p\u00e5 b\u00e5de engelska och svenska f\u00f6rekommer. Kvalifikationer F\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen kr\u00e4vs avlagd doktorsexamen i humanekologi. Anst\u00e4llningen kr\u00e4ver \u00e4ven att den s\u00f6kande har undervisningserfarenhet inom \u00e4mnet humanekologi framf\u00f6r allt fr\u00e5n svenskt universitet eller h\u00f6gskola samt dokumenterad f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att undervisa p\u00e5 engelska och svenska. En av de viktigaste bed\u00f6mningsgrunderna utg\u00f6rs av f\u00f6rm\u00e5gan att snabbt s\u00e4tta sig in i och utf\u00f6ra undervisningsuppdraget. Ans\u00f6kan Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla: - CV - Personligt brev - F\u00f6rteckning \u00f6ver pedagogiska meriter Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra f\u00f6r forskning och utbildning inom samh\u00e4lls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg, \u00f6ver 700 anst\u00e4llda och cirka 5 700 hel\u00e5rsstudenter \u00e4r fakulteten en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. V\u00e5r huvuduppgift \u00e4r att utveckla, f\u00f6rmedla och f\u00f6rvalta kunskap om samh\u00e4lle, m\u00e4nniska och organisationer i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av \u00f6ppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Institutionen f\u00f6r kulturgeografi och ekonomisk geografi vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r en forskningsintensiv akademisk enhet inom Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten. Den kombinerar l\u00e5nga akademiska traditioner med modern och starkt internationaliserad forskning och utbildning. Institutionen erbjuder ett brett utbud av utbildning p\u00e5 grund-, master- och doktorsniv\u00e5, inklusive internationellt inriktade program s\u00e5som mastersprogrammet i Human Geography. Institutionen har en m\u00e5ngsidig akademisk personal. Den exakta personalstyrkan varierar, men institutionen har f\u00f6r n\u00e4rvarande 55\u201360 akademiska och administrativa medarbetare. Institutionen utbildar cirka 400 heltidsstuderande p\u00e5 kandidat- och mastersprogram och har cirka 15 doktorander. Forskningsmilj\u00f6n \u00e4r starkt inriktad p\u00e5 extern finansiering och har varit framg\u00e5ngsrik i konkurrensen p\u00e5 nationell och europeisk niv\u00e5. Institutionens forsknings- och utbildningsverksamhet har f\u00e5tt mycket positiva omd\u00f6men i interna och externa utv\u00e4rderingar, vilket placerar den bland Lunds universitets ledande disciplin\u00e4ra milj\u00f6er. Lunds universitet som helhet presterar framg\u00e5ngsrikt i globala rankningar. Enligt den senaste QS World University Rankings ligger Lunds universitet p\u00e5 plats 72 globalt och uppn\u00e5r starka positioner p\u00e5 \u00e4mnesniv\u00e5, bland annat inom omr\u00e5den som r\u00f6r kulturgeografi och milj\u00f6vetenskap. Lunds universitet rankas ocks\u00e5 som nummer 1 i v\u00e4rlden inom h\u00e5llbarhet i samma ranking, vilket \u00e5terspeglar dess styrkor inom socialt och milj\u00f6m\u00e4ssigt relevant forskning och utbildning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2027-12-26 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de Januari 2027 L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100% Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2799 Kontakt Ola Hall, Prefekt, ola.hall@keg.lu.se Natalie Nyman, HR-partner, natalie.nyman@sam.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 0462229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 0462229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 0462220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-29 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-20 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:963476/": {"title": "Doctoral student in Biomedical Engineering specializing in engineering acoustics", "description": "Doctoral student in Biomedical Engineering specializing in engineering acoustics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Biomedical Engineering specializing in engineering acoustics Login and apply Lund University, Faculty of Engineering, LTH, Dep. of Biomedical Engineering Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The position is based at the Department of Biomedical Engineering and is linked to researchers working in marine biology, medical ultrasound, biomechanics, physics, e-science, and the strategic research area eSSENCE in Lund. The research group you will join conducts research in areas including engineering acoustics, medical ultrasound, acoustic measurement technology, non-destructive testing based on acoustic methods, signal processing, and numerical modelling, with applications in, among other fields, biomedical engineering, civil engineering, and biological systems. The working environment is highly interdisciplinary and is characterized by close collaboration between doctoral students, researchers, and academic staff, often with very different technical and scientific backgrounds and areas of expertise. The group strives to provide an open and inclusive working environment with good access to supervision, knowledge exchange, and broad scientific and interdisciplinary collaborations. More about the strategic research area eSSENCE - on Lund University's website Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. We are looking for a candidate who is curious, focused, and highly motivated by scientific questions. You have a creative and open-minded approach and enjoy combining methods and perspectives from different fields, such as physics, acoustics, computational modelling, and biology. You are driven by a desire to understand complex phenomena and to contribute new knowledge that is relevant to technology and society, as well as to our understanding of biological systems. More about being a doctoral student at LTH - lth.se Work duties You will primarily devote your time to your doctoral studies, which include participation in research projects as well as doctoral-level courses, seminars, and conferences. You will be part of an interdisciplinary research project investigating the physical mechanisms underlying dolphin echolocation. The overall aim of the project is to develop and apply computational models in acoustics and structural mechanics to describe how the short, broadband ultrasonic pulses generated in the dolphin\u2019s head propagate through tissues and other anatomical structures and are thereby shaped into a forward-directed echolocation beam. Particular emphasis will be placed on how variations in acoustic material properties, geometry, and potential reflective or refractive structures influence the direction, frequency-dependent shape, and temporal structure of the beam. The work is interdisciplinary and lies at the interface of engineering acoustics, computational physics, biomedical engineering, and zoology/bioacoustics. The project also includes developing the technical aspects of the results into practically useful concepts for human-made technologies, for example medical applications in diagnostic ultrasound, underwater acoustic sonar systems, or non-destructive testing of civil engineering structures. The work duties include: research on the acoustic properties of relevant tissues and anatomical structures, for example by measuring sound speeds, densities, and attenuation properties, as well as assisting with anatomical CT imaging of the physiology of stranded harbour porpoises and related specimens development of computer-based three-dimensional finite element models (FEM) of acoustic wave propagation in the sound-generating organs of dolphins and surrounding tissues, with the aim of creating a physically accurate so-called digital twin collection and analysis of acoustic, mechanical, and anatomical data from toothed whales development and use of computational and analysis code, with or without machine-learning components, in MATLAB and COMSOL or equivalent environments for model setup, post-processing, signal analysis, visualisation, and comparison between simulations and measurement data collaboration with researchers in, among other fields, physics, marine mammal research, and computational sciences, acting as an interdisciplinary knowledge bridge between different scientific disciplines communication of research results at scientific conferences and through the publication of scientific articles. The duties may also include participation in teaching and other departmental work, up to a maximum of 20% of working hours. Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Biomedical Engineering if the applicant has: at least 45 credits at second-cycle level relevant to the subject area Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Knowledge and skills relevant to the doctoral project and the subject area (e.g. engineering or theoretical physics, wave propagation, engineering acoustics, programming, modelling, bioacoustics, computational methods, electronics, applied mathematics, zoology, materials physics, etc.). Very good analytical skills, including problem-solving and data analysis. Goal-oriented approach, which may be demonstrated through perseverance and the ability to work methodically, in a structured manner, and with focus. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good collaborative skills (i e manifested as a willingness to share ideas, constructive approach to challenges etc). Very good written and oral communication skills. Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written Other qualifications (advantages) For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in engineering physics or theoretical physics, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, mathematics, computer engineering, engineering acoustics, or another subject relevant to the research area Knowledge of numerical computational methods and/or FEM-based modelling of physical problems Experience of finite element modelling in acoustics and multiphysics Knowledge of marine mammals, toothed-whale echolocation or other areas of bioacoustics Practical experience of acoustic or measurement systems Practical experience of measurement technology and electronics Programming experience beyond introductory-level courses Experience of working with computing clusters Experience of classical machine-learning or deep-learning-based signal analysis. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on Lund University's website About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s staff pages. Other Job interviews will be held online and on site at the Faculty of Engineering, Lund University, during the autumn semester of 2026. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We look forward to receiving your application! LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment As soon as possible, as agreed. Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2501 Contact Josefin Starkhammar, josefin.starkhammar@bme.lth.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 09.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968843/": {"title": "PostDoc in Scientific Imaging Data Reduction and Compression", "description": "PostDoc in Scientific Imaging Data Reduction and Compression Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PostDoc in Scientific Imaging Data Reduction and Compression Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. The Scientific Data Group You will join the Scientific Data Group within the Technical Division of MAX IV Laboratory. We develop and operate high-performance data acquisition systems for cutting-edge detectors and provide data processing, visualisation and analysis solutions that enable researchers to rapidly interpret results from X-ray scattering, imaging and spectroscopy experiments. Our systems routinely handle data rates of several GB/s and support large-scale scientific data workflows. To support sustainable data management at next-generation photon science facilities, we are seeking a Postdoctoral Researcher to advance scientific data reduction and compression workflows for tomography and imaging applications in collaboration with European research infrastructures. The Position The rapid growth of data volumes generated by modern imaging experiments is creating significant challenges for data storage, transfer, processing and long-term preservation. Through a collaborative European initiative involving leading photon science facilities, MAX IV is developing sustainable approaches to scientific data reduction and scientifically validated lossy-compression methods for tomography and imaging applications. As a PostDoc you will contribute to the evaluation, development, validation and deployment of advanced data reduction and compression methodologies for large-scale imaging datasets. Working at the interface between scientific computing, image analysis and research infrastructures, you will collaborate closely with scientists, software engineers, beamline scientists and computing specialists across the European photon science community. The project is carried out in close collaboration with leading European photon science facilities through the LEAPS community. The position offers a unique opportunity to engage directly with MAX IV's full-field X-ray imaging and tomography activities. These span the established tomography capabilities at DanMAX and ForMAX, together with the development of TomoWISE, a dedicated next-generation tomography beamline currently under construction. The successful candidate will work closely with scientists and engineers developing future imaging capabilities at MAX IV while collaborating with experts in tomography, scientific computing, data management and research software engineering across Europe. Your work will contribute to practical solutions that significantly reduce data volumes while preserving scientific quality and reproducibility. The project combines scientific research, software development and international collaboration, offering opportunities to influence community-wide best practices for data handling at large-scale research facilities. Activities include benchmarking and validating compression algorithms, developing software tools and workflows, establishing quality metrics and best practices, collaborating with partner facilities, organising workshops and training activities, and disseminating results through publications and presentations. Your primary responsibilities will include Evaluate and benchmark data reduction and lossy-compression methods using representative tomography and imaging datasets from MAX IV and collaborating facilities. Develop software tools, workflows and validation methodologies that support the adoption of compression technologies in scientific environments. Collaborate with beamline scientists to evaluate the impact of data reduction methods on scientific outcomes and data quality. Contribute to community guidelines, best practices and knowledge resources related to scientific data reduction, compression and FAIR data management. Work with researchers and technical experts at European photon science facilities to facilitate knowledge exchange and technology transfer. Support and coordinate project workshops, training activities and dissemination events. Disseminate project outcomes through reports, technical documentation, presentations, workshops, and scientific publications, as appropriate. To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications A PhD in Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Scientific Computing, Image Processing, Data Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated experience in scientific programming, scientific software development, or data-intensive computing. Experience with Python and at least one high-performance programming language such as C++, Rust, or Julia. Experience working with large-scale scientific datasets, image processing, computational imaging, tomography data analysis, or data compression. Experience with Linux-based computing environments and modern software development practices, including version control and collaborative software development. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English. Ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary and international research environment The following qualifications are considered an advantage Experience with synchrotron, neutron, electron microscopy, medical imaging, or other large-scale imaging facilities. Experience with scientific data formats and technologies such as HDF5, NeXus and Zarr. Knowledge of FAIR data principles and research data management. Experience with high-performance computing, cloud computing, GPU acceleration, or distributed data processing. Experience participating in international scientific collaborations and/or multi-institutional research projects. Eligibility Appointment to the position of postdoc requires that the applicant has a PhD or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the application deadline. Under special circumstances the PhD can have been completed previous to the aforementioned three years. Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment for two years. A postdoctoral fellow is employed under a period of at least two years and at most three years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor-2022-02-01\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow, 2022-02-01\u201d). What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you enter a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world, generating scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer you a multicultural work environment with great opportunities for personal development with respect for a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supporting environment? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference! For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2670 Contact Paul Bell, +46706700506, paul.bell@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 18.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968981/": {"title": "PhD student position in Surgery", "description": "PhD student position in Surgery Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD student position in Surgery Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Sciences, Lund Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the Workplace Lund University was founded in 1666 and is consistently ranked among the world's leading universities. The University has approximately 47,000 students and more than 8,800 employees in Lund, Helsingborg, and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain, and improve our world and the conditions of humankind. The Faculty of Medicine is one of Lund University's faculties and is responsible for education and research in medicine, nursing, and health sciences. Education is conducted in close collaboration with the healthcare sector and is firmly rooted in the Faculty's strong research tradition. The Faculty's research spans a broad range of areas, including experimental basic research, patient-oriented clinical research, and health sciences research. With more than 1,800 employees and 3,000 students in Lund, Malm\u00f6, and Helsingborg, the Faculty of Medicine is a knowledge-intensive environment where students, teachers, and researchers from all over the world meet and collaborate. The Department of Clinical Sciences Lund (IKVL) is one of six departments within the Faculty of Medicine. The department maintains extensive collaborations both within the Faculty and with other parts of the University. IKVL also has well-established collaborations with Sk\u00e5ne University Hospital (SUS), Region Sk\u00e5ne, and external partners in society and industry. These collaborations aim to promote clinical and experimental translational research, development, and education. The research group is now recruiting a doctoral student (full-time, 100%) with a start date of 1 November 2026, or as otherwise agreed. Description of the Doctoral Project and Research Group The doctoral position is based in the Pancreatology Research Group within the Division of Surgery at Lund University. The group's research focuses on pancreatic cancer, one of the most aggressive forms of human malignancy. Pancreatic cancer is often detected at an advanced stage, and effective treatments remain limited. Our strategy combines clinical patient materials with advanced protein research to identify novel biomarkers for earlier diagnosis and treatment response. The research group consists of two research engineers, several full-time and part-time doctoral students, and clinicians affiliated with the group. We value a positive work environment characterized by respect and consideration in our interactions with one another. We continuously strive to create conditions that promote job satisfaction, professional development, and participation for all employees. Duties and Responsibilities The doctoral student will work within a translational research project on pancreatic cancer, focusing on disease biology and prognosis. The project combines data from cancer registries and clinical materials with histopathological analyses and spatial proteomics. The overall aim is to identify novel prognostic and predictive biomarkers and to improve our understanding of pancreatic cancer progression and treatment response. The duties will include: Managing data from cancer registries and clinical databases and integrating these with histopathological and molecular data. Interpreting histopathological findings and spatial proteomics data in relation to tumour characteristics, metastatic patterns, and clinical outcomes. Conducting statistical analyses of prognostic and predictive factors and investigating associations between tumour biology, biomarkers, metastasis, and survival. Compiling and presenting research findings in scientific manuscripts and at national and international conferences. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate a strong ability and willingness to collaborate with colleagues within the research group. Additional duties related to the position may be assigned. We Offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that employees are entitled to a range of attractive benefits, generous annual leave, and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. We also offer flexible working hours that support a healthy work-life balance. Read more about working at Lund University on the University's website. Work at Lund University Qualifications Applicants must meet the general entry requirements for third-cycle (doctoral) studies. A person meets the general entry requirements if they have: completed a second-cycle degree; completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 credits are at second-cycle level; or acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way, either in Sweden or abroad. Required Qualifications Previous research experience in pancreatic cancer research is required. Excellent command of spoken and written English. Ability to conduct and document research in a structured and systematic manner. We are looking for a curious, motivated, and highly engaged candidate with a strong interest in translational cancer research. The position involves close collaboration with colleagues, and therefore strong interpersonal and teamwork skills are essential. Meritorious Qualifications A publication record in peer-reviewed journals within the field of pancreatic cancer is considered an asset. Eligibility Applicants must meet the general entry requirements for third cycle (doctoral) studies. A person meets the general entry requirements if they have: completed a second-cycle degree; completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 credits are at second-cycle level; or acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way, either in Sweden or abroad. Assessment Criteria Regulations concerning employment as a doctoral student are set out in the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance (SFS 1998:80). Only applicants who are admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral studentship. In the appointment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant's ability to successfully complete doctoral studies. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral education, the holder of the position may be required to undertake duties related to education, research, and administrative work in accordance with the provisions of the Ordinance. Terms of Employment This is a fixed-term position of four years in accordance with Chapter 5, Section 7 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance. How to Apply Applications must be submitted through Lund University's recruitment system. The application should include: A cover letter describing how you meet the qualification requirements and why you are interested in the position. A curriculum vitae (CV). Degree certificates, academic transcripts, and any other relevant supporting documentation. Any additional documents you wish to submit in support of your application. Contact information for at least two professional references. The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Employment expires 2030-10-31 First day of employment 2026-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2676 Contact Anneli Karlsson, anneli.karlsson@med.lu.se Bobby Tingstedt, tomas.jansson@med.lu.se Daniel Ansari, daniel.ansari@med.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362 SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366 Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 19.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973185/": {"title": "Post-doctoral fellow in AI-based design of de novo protein biofilm systems", "description": "Post-doctoral fellow in AI-based design of de novo protein biofilm systems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Post-doctoral fellow in AI-based design of de novo protein biofilm systems Login and apply Lunds universitet Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Subject description AI-based protein design and synthetic biology for developing programmable living materials, with a particular focus on the de novo design of proteins biofilm systems. The research combines computational protein design with synthetic biology to develop new molecular functions and mechanisms for controlling the formation, organization, and functional properties of living materials. The work may include development and application of AI-based protein design methods, experimental characterization of designed proteins, microbial engineering, biofilm design, and high-throughput functional screening. We are committed to translating fundamental discoveries into technologies with real-world impact. The lab first spinout company is already funded and operational, with additional translational opportunities under development. This provides a unique environment for researchers interested in pursuing future careers in either academia targeting hard basic research problems or technology development and entrepreneurship. We value community spirit, dedication, and the pursuit of innovative science with the potential to make a meaningful impact on sustainability and future technologies. For more information: https://saragovi.science/ Work duties The main duties involved in a post-doctoral posistion is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position shall include the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. Detailed description of the work duties, such as: Research within AI-based protein design, synthetic biology, biofilm engineering, and programmable living materials. Development and implementation of computational pipelines for the de novo design of proteins and protein-based systems. Development and implementation of high-throughput experimental approaches for screening and characterization of designed systems. Engineering of microbial systems with de novo biofilms. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students Actively seeking external research funding Collaboration with researchers from different scientific disciplines and with external partners, including industry. Administration related to the work duties listed above Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the date of employment decision. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: Very good oral and written proficiency in English. A doctoral degree, or equivalent research experience, in a field relevant to the position, such as protein design, computational biology, structural biology, synthetic biology, biotechnology, bioengineering, microbiology, molecular biology, or a closely related field. Assessment criteria and other qualifications This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: Documented scientific excellence and the quality of the applicant's previous research, including their individual contribution to published or ongoing work. Demonstrated ability to independently formulate scientific questions, solve research problems, and drive research projects forward. Research experience and demonstrated expertise in at least one of the following areas: computational or de novo protein design; synthetic biology; microbial or yeast engineering; biofilm engineering; or high-throughput functional screening. The relevance of the applicant's previous research experience and technical expertise to the development of programmable microbial and biofilm systems. Ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary research environment combining computational and experimental approaches. Teaching skills. Additional assessment criteria: Research experience spanning two or more of the scientific areas relevant to the project. Experience with AI-based or computational protein design, including modern methods for protein structure prediction, sequence design, or generative protein design. Experience with experimental production and characterization of designed proteins. Experience with genetic engineering of bacteria or yeast and the development of engineered microbial systems. Experience with the engineering, characterization, or functional screening of biofilms. Experience with high-throughput experimentation, automation, screening, or iterative design\u2013build\u2013test\u2013learn workflows. Experience developing or implementing computational pipelines for biological or protein design. A strong publication record relative to career stage, with particular consideration given to evidence of substantial individual contributions to high-quality research. Demonstrated scientific creativity, initiative, and ability to develop new experimental or computational approaches. Experience of interdisciplinary collaboration and the ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with researchers from different scientific backgrounds and with external partners . Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant\u2019s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of a maximum of 2 years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow\u201d) between Lund University, SACO-S and OFR/S, dated 1st February 2022. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English and be compiled into a PDF-file containing: r\u00e9sum\u00e9/CV, including a list of publications, a general description of past research and future research interests (no more than three pages), contact information of at least two references, copy of the doctoral degree certificate, and other certificates/grades that you wish to be considered. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-01-01 or as agreed Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2792 Contact Amijai Saragovi, +46736419771, amijai.saragovi@chem.lu.se Jessica Edwinsson, jessica.edwinsson@chem.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 31.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970477/": {"title": "Doctoral student in traffic safety focusing on data analysis and traffic simulation", "description": "Doctoral student in traffic safety focusing on data analysis and traffic simulation Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in traffic safety focusing on data analysis and traffic simulation Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace Transport and Roads offer a unique and open environment for advanced research on traffic safety and behaviour. The group counts five senior researchers (postdocs and senior lecturers) and two PhD students. On the availability of the group, there is a traffic simulation lab with an advanced driving simulator . The group has several active projects in the field of traffic safety, European and national. As a doctoral student, you will contribute to research intended to improve the understanding and prevention of road crashes and injuries. You will work closely with senior researchers while developing an independent research profile. The position provides opportunities for interdisciplinary and international collaboration, conference participation and research visits where relevant to the project. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Subject and project description The doctoral project concerns the development and application of quantitative methods for traffic-safety analysis. The research will combine empirical crash and traffic data with statistical modelling, machine learning and traffic or driving simulation to study crash occurrence, injury severity and road-user behaviour. Particular attention may be given to heterogeneous effects across road users and environments, the interpretation and validation of predictive models, and the safety effects of infrastructure or policy interventions. The precise research questions and balance between methods will be developed with the doctoral student in relation to the project's data, facilities and collaborations. The work is expected to produce both scientific contributions and knowledge relevant to traffic-safety practice and policy. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to doctoral studies through research, third-cycle courses, seminars and conferences. You will plan and carry out studies with increasing independence, in collaboration with the supervisory team and project partners. The work duties include: Review and synthesise research on traffic safety, crash analysis, road-user behaviour and relevant modelling methods. Acquire, document, clean and analyse crash, traffic, infrastructure, behavioural or simulation data in accordance with research-ethics and data-management requirements. Develop, implement, compare and validate quantitative models, which may include statistical, econometric, machine-learning and simulation-based approaches. Interpret results in relation to traffic-safety theory, human behaviour and practical decision-making, including uncertainty, bias and limitations. Prepare scientific articles and a doctoral thesis, and present results at seminars, conferences and meetings with project partners. Contribute to the group's collaborative research environment and, where relevant, undertake research visits or field and laboratory work. The duties may also include teaching and other departmental work, up to a maximum of 20% of working hours. Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Technology and Society if the applicant has: at least 30 credits awarded in the second cycle relevant to the subject area. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: a master's degree, or equivalent, in transportation engineering, civil engineering, traffic engineering, applied statistics, data science, computer science or another field relevant to the project. documented second-cycle coursework or thesis work involving quantitative analysis of transport, traffic-safety, mobility or comparable complex empirical data. experience of using programming languages or statistical computing environments, such as Python, R, MATLAB or an equivalent tool, for data processing and analysis. good ability to work independently, formulate research questions and select appropriate methods. good written and oral communication skills, including the ability to communicate methods and results clearly. good ability to cooperate in interdisciplinary and international research settings. very good command of English, spoken and written. you are structured, analytical and persistent. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme and project, the following are considered advantageous: knowledge of traffic-safety theory, crash and injury analysis, road-user behaviour, transport planning or road-infrastructure safety. experience of advanced quantitative methods, such as regression or discrete-choice models, latent-class or random-parameter methods, machine learning, explainable AI, causal or intervention evaluation. experience of working with large, multi-source or international transport datasets, including data preprocessing, reproducible analysis and model validation. experience of scientific writing, peer-reviewed publication, conference presentation or experience of teaching. experience of collaboration with researchers and stakeholders across disciplines or countries. We offer Lund University is a public authority, and employees receive benefits including generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. The Transport and Roads division offers access to an active traffic-safety research environment, advanced simulation facilities, research seminars and established Swedish and international collaborations. More about working at Lund University on lu.se . About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staff pages . Other We plan to hold interviews at the end of October. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2716 Contact Carmelo D'Agostino, associate professor, carmelo.dagostino@tft.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 25.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972280/": {"title": "PhD position in Dermatology", "description": "PhD position in Dermatology Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD position in Dermatology Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Sciences, Lund Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the Workplace The PhD project will be conducted within the field of peptidomics. The research group is based at the Biomedical Centre (BMC), Division of Dermatology and Venereology, Department of Clinical Sciences Lund, Lund University, and conducts translational research on how innate defense mechanisms regulate infection, inflammation, and tissue repair. A particular focus is placed on proteolytically released endogenous peptides and their role in wound healing, as well as on the development of novel peptide-based therapeutic concepts. The research group is led by Professor Artur Schmidtchen. The group consists of approximately seven members, including senior researchers, PhD students, and research staff, with complementary expertise in clinical and translational dermatology, microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, and biochemistry. Research is carried out in close collaboration with clinical departments, BioMS, and experts in proteomics, peptidomics, and bioinformatics at Lund University. The Department of Clinical Sciences Lund is now announcing a PhD position within the doctoral programme subject area Medical Science \u2013 Dermatology within the doctoral project \u201cPeptidomics of Wound Fluid Guides the Discovery of Endogenous Peptides.\u201d The position is based at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University, and is conducted in an international and interdisciplinary research environment. We Offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that you will benefit from special employment benefits, generous annual leave, and an attractive occupational pension scheme. We also offer flexible working hours that support a healthy work-life balance. Read more about working at Lund University on our website: Work at Lund University. Duties and Responsibilities The PhD student will carry out a defined research project focused on identifying and characterizing bioactive endogenous peptides involved in infection, inflammation, and wound healing. The project forms a central part of the group's ongoing research and will be conducted in collaboration with BioMS and experts in proteomics and peptidomics at Lund University. The duties include: Planning and conducting experiments. Developing and optimizing methods for sample preparation, peptide enrichment, and fractionation. Performing LC-MS/MS analyses using both DDA and DIA methodologies. Conducting bioinformatic and statistical analyses of peptidomic datasets to identify peptide patterns, proteolytic signatures, and candidate peptides with potential roles in infection, inflammation, and wound healing. Characterizing selected peptides in microbiological and cell-based assays, both individually and in combination, with regard to antimicrobial and immunomodulatory effects. Documenting, quality assuring, and compiling research results. Presenting and publishing research findings in scientific forums. Participating in research group seminars, collaborations, and other scientific activities. Completing courses and other components required within the doctoral education programme. Qualifications Requirements The successful applicant must have: A Master of Science in Engineering degree in Biotechnology, with specialization in Pharmaceutical Biotechnology or Molecular Biotechnology. Documented experience in basic biochemistry, including SDS-PAGE, LC-MS/MS mass spectrometry (DDA and DIA), and handling of human samples. Knowledge and experience in peptide biology and peptidomics, including analysis of complex datasets using specialized peptidomics tools. Experience in MS data analysis using software such as FragPipe and DIA-NN, as well as basic programming skills in Python. Practical experience in antibacterial assays based on dilution or diffusion methodologies. Excellent proficiency in both Swedish and English, spoken and written. Good collaborative skills combined with a high degree of accuracy and responsibility. Meritorious Qualifications The following qualifications are considered advantageous: Previous experience working with mass spectrometry-based analyses. Experience from project work in international or multicultural environments. Experience in method development and experimental troubleshooting. Experience in combinatorial analyses of antimicrobial peptides. Eligibility Applicants must meet the general entry requirements for third-cycle studies, meaning they must have: Completed a second-cycle degree, or Completed at least 240 credits (ECTS), including at least 60 credits at the second-cycle level, or Acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in another way. Assessment Criteria Provisions regarding employment as a doctoral student are laid down in the Higher Education Ordinance (SFS 1998:80). Only applicants admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral studentship. When selecting among qualified applicants, particular emphasis will be placed on: Scientific maturity and analytical ability. Motivation, independence, and ability to collaborate. Capacity to successfully complete doctoral education. How the applicant\u2019s background and experience are assessed to contribute to the execution of the project. Terms of Employment The employment is a fixed-term full-time position as a PhD student for four years (48 months), in accordance with Chapter 5, Section 7 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance. The planned starting date is 1 December 2026, or as otherwise agreed. The Department of Clinical Sciences Lund is one of six departments within the Faculty of Medicine. The department maintains extensive collaborations both within the faculty and with other units at Lund University. It also has well-established partnerships with Sk\u00e5ne University Hospital (SUS), Region Sk\u00e5ne, and external stakeholders in society and industry. These collaborations support clinical and experimental translational research, development, and education. The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Employment expires 2030-11-30 First day of employment 2026-12-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2766 Contact Artur Schmidtchen, professor, 046-2224522, artur.schmidtchen@med.lu.se Jessica H\u00f6rngren, HR partner, 073-6361904, jessica.horngren@med.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362 SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366 Published 25.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:902067/": {"title": "Professor of Medical Virology (with the possibility of a combined position)", "description": "Professor of Medical Virology (with the possibility of a combined position) Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Professor of Medical Virology (with the possibility of a combined position) Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Employment A permanent position as a professor of medical virology. This post is based in the Department of Translational Medicine (ITM). It may be possible to combine this position with clinical duties. This will be decided at the time of appointment. Duties The role involves conducting research and providing postgraduate training and teaching on the faculty\u2019s programmes in medical virology. Other duties associated with a professorship include administrative work, as well as internal and external positions of trust at a national and international level. Applicants must be prepared to take on leadership responsibilities for research and teaching within the subject area. The successful candidate will carry out their research at Lund University\u2019s Virus Centre (LUVC) . This newly established research centre facilitates experimental virological research and includes a biosafety level 3 laboratory for the study of risk class 3 airborne viruses. LUVC's primary objective is to foster collaboration between researchers, healthcare providers, industry, and the public to enhance our understanding of viral diseases and contribute to the development of new preventive, therapeutic, and diagnostic tools. A key part of the role will be to conduct and develop research that is competitive both nationally and internationally in the field of experimental medical virology, with a view to broadening and strengthening existing research at LUVC . The successful candidate is expected to take up the position of Research Group Leader at ITM. This role involves delegated responsibility for health and safety, finance, and human resources. In the event of a combined position, the role will involve working as part of the medical staff at the Department of Clinical Microbiology at Region Sk\u00e5ne. Responsibilities will include teaching, development work and virological diagnostics. You may also be required to perform other duties. Eligibility A person who has demonstrated both research and teaching expertise shall be qualified for employment as a professor ( Higher Education Ordinance, Chapter 4 Section 3). Unless there are special reasons to the contrary, the applicant must have completed training in higher education pedagogy equivalent to at least five weeks or acquired equivalent knowledge in some other way. If the holder is deemed to have special reasons for not having completed five weeks' training in higher education pedagogy when they take up the post, they must complete the training within two years (see Lund University Appointment Rules ) . In the event of a combined position, applicants must have language skills in Swedish, or another Nordic language (Danish or Norwegian) deemed to be equivalent to Swedish, at a minimum of level C1 according to the Council of Europe\u2019s proficiency scale. For teachers at Lund University, the general eligibility requirement is that they must be suitable for the role and possess the other abilities required to perform their duties effectively. Assessment criteria The applicant must demonstrate excellent academic and teaching skills relevant to the subject. Particular emphasis will be placed on academic ability in the assessment. The applicant\u2019s scientific expertise is demonstrated through up-to-date, pioneering and independent research in experimental medical virology at a high international level. Furthermore, applicants must demonstrate their ability to initiate and lead national and international research collaborations. They must also demonstrate their potential to contribute to the development of experimental medical virology research. Future plans and vision will be taken into account. Relevant and up-to-date experience of translational and/or clinically oriented research and research collaborations would be advantageous. The applicant must demonstrate a track record of publishing high-quality work in reputable international scientific journals and must have secured significant national and international competitive research grants as the principal investigator. They must also demonstrate the ability to initiate and lead national and international research collaborations. The applicant must demonstrate relevant teaching skills in the context of undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral-level teaching and supervision. This is demonstrated by the ability to plan, implement and lead training, and to develop training modules that incorporate clinical expertise. In addition, great importance will be attached to demonstrated academic leadership and collaboration skills . The ability and potential to lead and develop the organisation are demonstrated through documented evidence of strong leadership qualities, such as positions of trust, leadership training and assessed leadership ability. This may also be demonstrated through experience gained from previous management roles and other administrative skills, such as leadership within interdisciplinary projects, research environments and consortia. Experience of leadership in an international context is an advantage. Leadership skills are also demonstrated through communication skills, the ability to foster staff\u2019s professional development, and the ability to contribute positively to the working environment. Skills relating to participation in organisational development and collaboration, as well as the ability to interact with the wider community, will also be important. This can be demonstrated through experience of communicating research findings and establishing collaborations with researchers from different disciplines and relevant stakeholders outside academia. The ability to disseminate knowledge and contribute to the implementation of research findings in society or clinical practice will be an asset. In the case of a combined position, clinical experience and expertise in the subject area of the post will be taken into account. For teaching staff at Lund University, the general eligibility requirement is that they are suitable for the role and possess the other abilities necessary to perform their duties effectively. When appointing teaching staff, in addition to the provisions set out in The Higher Education Ordinance , Lund University Appointment Rules and The Faculty of Medicine\u2019s general requirements and assessment criteria for appointment as a professor . Further information For furhter information, please contact Head of Department Jan Astermark, phone: +46 70-551 66 19, jan.astermark@med.lu.se or Dean Maria Bj\u00f6rkqvist, phone: +46 72-700 71 63, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Information regarding the application process can be obtained from the recruitment co-ordinator, Eva Nilsson, phone: + 46 46-222 17 89, eva_a.nilsson@med.lu.se The post will be filled following a recommendation from the Medical Staff Appointments Committee. Application procedure Applications for this post must be submitted online via Lund University\u2019s applicant portal Varbi by 26 November 2026 at the latest The application must be submitted in accordance with The Faculty of Medicine\u2019s guidelines for applicants for teaching posts (see List of qualifications for lecturers ). Please note that the application should be written in English. However, academic transcripts and certificates of employment do not need to be translated. The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Translational Medicine is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We conduct basic science in a laboratory setting, point-of-care and clinical research as well as carry out epidemiological studies. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent Heltid City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/470 Union representative Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:967692/": {"title": "Amanuens till avdelningen f\u00f6r Teknisk vattenresursl\u00e4ra", "description": "Amanuens till avdelningen f\u00f6r Teknisk vattenresursl\u00e4ra Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens till avdelningen f\u00f6r Teknisk vattenresursl\u00e4ra Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r placerad vid Lunds universitet, Lunds Tekniska H\u00f6gskola, Institutionen f\u00f6r bygg- och milj\u00f6teknologi, avdelningen f\u00f6r teknisk vattenresursl\u00e4ra. Avdelningen bedriver undervisning och forskning kring vattenresurser, hydrologi och hydraulik. Vid avdelningen arbetar cirka 30 personer uppdelade p\u00e5 kategorierna l\u00e4rare/forskare, doktorander, teknisk-administrativ personal samt studentmedarbetare. Amanuenser utf\u00f6r arbetsuppgifter inom grundutbildning, forskning samt administration. Arbetsplatsen \u00e4r bel\u00e4gen i V-huset, p\u00e5 LTHs campus i Lund. Arbetsuppgifter Som amanuens kan dina arbetsuppgifter variera och arbetsuppgifterna ska ge en inblick i den akademiska v\u00e4rlden p\u00e5 den fakultet d\u00e4r du bedriver studier. Arbetsuppgifterna innefattar: undervisning i form av \u00f6vningsledare i kursen Vatten (VVRA05) viss medverkan i p\u00e5g\u00e5ende forskningsprojekt viss administration Kvalifikationer Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som amanuens \u00e4r den som \u00e4r antagen till utbildning p\u00e5 grund- eller avancerad niv\u00e5 vid fakulteten (eller n\u00e4rliggande \u00e4mne f\u00f6r de gemensamma institutionerna). Examen f\u00e5r ej vara uttagen. Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: P\u00e5g\u00e5ende heltidsstudier inom V-utbildningen eller motsvarande utbildning som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer relevant mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska, i tal och skrift God f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att samarbeta Sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndighet och initiativf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga Godk\u00e4nt p\u00e5 alla kurser p\u00e5 V-utbildningens \u00e5rskurs 1 och 2 eller motsvarande kurser p\u00e5 utbildning som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer relevant Kursbetyget 5 p\u00e5 kursen VVRA05 Vatten eller motsvarande betyg p\u00e5 kurs som bed\u00f6ms som relevant av arbetsgivaren Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Kunskaper inom vattenresursteknik i form av h\u00f6ga kursbetyg Tidigare undervisningserfarenhet T\u00e5lamod och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att utrycka sig tydligt Det \u00e4r viktigt att du har t\u00e5lamod och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att uttrycka dig tydligt. Du beh\u00f6ver ha god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att samarbeta, men \u00e4ven kunna arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att ta egna initiativ. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet som erbjuder goda anst\u00e4llningsvillkor. Med en anst\u00e4llning som amanuens f\u00e5r du som student en m\u00f6jlighet att f\u00f6rena studier med arbete f\u00f6r att komplettera dina teoretiska kunskaper med praktisk arbetslivserfarenhet inom akademin. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss . \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tidsbegr\u00e4nsad under perioden 2027-01-18 till 2027-05-30 och avser en omfattning p\u00e5 10 % av heltid, vilket i genomsnitt motsvarar 4 h i veckan. En anst\u00e4llning som amanuens f\u00e5r vara h\u00f6gst 50% av full arbetstid och f\u00e5r vara tidsbegr\u00e4nsad till h\u00f6gst ett \u00e5r, sammanlagt max tre \u00e5r. Anst\u00e4llningen f\u00e5r inte p\u00e5verka amanuensens studier negativt. Best\u00e4mmelser g\u00e4llande utbildningsanst\u00e4llning som amanuens finns i H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8-12 \u00a7\u00a7. Anst\u00e4llningen omfattas av Arbetstidsavtal f\u00f6r l\u00e4rare. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla CV och personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Vi ber dig bifoga utdrag fr\u00e5n LADOK som intygar din beh\u00f6righet. Ans\u00f6kan b\u00f6r \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.). V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! LTH \u2013 Lunds Tekniska H\u00f6gskola \u2013 \u00e4r en del av Lunds universitet. P\u00e5 LTH utbildar vi m\u00e4nniskor, bygger kunskap f\u00f6r framtiden och arbetar h\u00e5rt f\u00f6r att utveckla samh\u00e4llet. Vi skapar utrymme f\u00f6r briljant forskning och inspirerar till kreativ utveckling av teknik, arkitektur och design. H\u00e4r l\u00e4ser n\u00e4rmare 12 000 studenter. Varje \u00e5r publicerar v\u00e5ra forskare \u2013 varav m\u00e5nga verkar inom v\u00e4rldsledande profilomr\u00e5den \u2013 omkring 100 avhandlingar och 2 000 vetenskapliga r\u00f6n. En rad forskningsresultat och studentarbeten f\u00f6r\u00e4dlas till innovationer. Tillsammans utforskar och skapar vi \u2013 till nytta f\u00f6r v\u00e4rlden. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 270118 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 10% Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2631 Kontakt Magnus Persson, +46462228990, magnus.persson@tvrl.lth.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-24 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-21 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:966737/": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems", "description": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Assistant Professor in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The assistant professor will be working at the Department of Computer Science, in the Software Engineering (SE) division (until recently known as the SERG research group), headed by division head Emelie Engstr\u00f6m. SE comprises around 15 people: two professors, two associate professors/senior lecturers, additional lecturers and adjunct staff (some part-time, with ties to industry), one assistant professor and six doctoral students. The division is based in the E-building on LTH's campus in Lund. As the new assistant professor, you will be the division's second assistant professor, working closely with both senior researchers and the doctoral students, tasked with building up and leading the new research track on verification, validation and quality assurance of autonomous systems. SE's research builds on decades of empirical studies of large-scale software development, requirements, testing and quality assurance at industrial scale, with contributions from, among others, Per Runeson, Bj\u00f6rn Regnell, Emelie Engstr\u00f6m, Elizabeth Bjarnason and Markus Borg. In recent years, this has, among other things, been directed towards autonomous and safety-critical systems. A current example is VerSACE, a Vinnova FFI project (2025\u20132028) in which Lund University participates together with, among others, Chalmers, KTH and several leading players in the automotive industry and automotive software, on how frequent software updates in self-driving vehicles can be continuously tested, verified and safety-monitored. Supported by the group's established funding channels through the strategic research area ELLIIT and WASP (Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program), as well as through the network around the NextG2Com competence centre (theme \"Software Platforms and Continuous Engineering\", led by Emma S\u00f6derberg in the SDE division and Emelie Engstr\u00f6m), there are good prospects for the position to grow into a more long-term research track, with good opportunities for new collaborations. Read more: NextG2Com: https://www.nextg2com.lu.se/ , WASP: https://wasp-sweden.org/ , Elliit: https://elliit.se/ . Assistant professors in SE receive ongoing support in their development towards promotion to senior lecturer. The group holds regular seminars and meetings where research is presented and discussed in a friendly and generous spirit, and members collaborate extensively, both among themselves and with colleagues in other parts of the department. As an assistant professor, we welcome you taking your own initiative for new collaborations, both within and outside the department, and building up your own research direction within this track over time. Subject Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems Subject description The position focuses on methods, tools and studies (empirical as well as analytical and design-oriented) for the verification, validation, quality assurance and certification of large-scale, industrial autonomous systems with AI and ML components, for example autonomous vehicles, robotics in industrial operation, and other deployed cyber-physical systems, as well as autonomous systems with no physical counterpart, for example AI agents and automated decision-support systems, seen from a systems perspective. The subject area includes, among other things: Scenario-based and simulation-based testing of autonomous systems. Statistical and data-driven verification under uncertainty and non-determinism. Model-based systems engineering and architecture for autonomous systems. Safety argumentation and assurance cases. Regulatory compliance and requirements management related to, for example, the EU AI Act and relevant safety standards. What these approaches have in common is that they address the behaviour of the whole system in its operational context, including its interaction with the environment, rather than the formal verification of individual ML models or components. The subject thus complements related, more component-level/mathematically oriented ML verification research at LTH, and builds on SE's expertise in empirical and applied software and systems engineering, as well as the department's established collaborations within, among others, NextG2Com, ELLIIT, WASP and the profile area AI and Digitalisation. Work duties Employment as an assistant professor is a tenure track position, which aims for the holder to develop their independence as a researcher and educator. The work duties mainly involve research and teaching. The position includes the opportunity to undertake five weeks of training in teaching and learning in higher education. Work duties include: Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Qualification requirements for employment as an assistant professor are fulfilled by someone who has been awarded a doctorate or has the corresponding research competence. Primary consideration should be given to someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent competence within seven years of the deadline for application for employment as an assistant professor. However, someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent expertise at an earlier date may also be considered if there are special grounds. Special grounds are sick leave, parental leave or other similar circumstances. Assessment criteria For appointment to assistant professor, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and carry out high quality research. Teaching ability. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Significant documented research experience (e.g. from postdoc or doctoral studies) from another university/institute or relevant experience from industry/public sector. Documented research competence in verification, validation, quality assurance and/or certification of autonomous and/or AI-based systems, or a related area. Documented proficiency in using empirical, analytical, and/or design science methods, as well as the ability to collaborate and work across methodological and knowledge domains. Documented research that is applied to, or grounded in, real, large-scale industrial systems and problems, rather than purely theoretical research lacking such application or grounding. Ability to contribute to a good, inclusive and respectful research and working environment. Collaborative skills, initiative and the ability to solve work tasks independently, as well as a demonstrated interest in leadership. Other qualifications Ability to collaborate in interdisciplinary and international research environments. Ability to establish and develop collaborations, for example with industry, other universities and institutes. Significant documented research experience (e.g. from postdoc or doctoral studies) from another university/institute or relevant experience from industry/public sector. The extent to which the applicant, through their experience and skills, may complement and strengthen ongoing research, undergraduate education, departmental innovation, and how they can contribute to the future development of the department will also be taken into consideration. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 6 years. The employment is regulated in accordance with Chapter 4 Section 12a\u00a7 HEA. The purpose of the appointment is for the teacher to be given the opportunity to develop research autonomy and acquire the scholarly and teaching qualifications required for eligibility for appointment as a senior lecturer. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English. Please draw up the application in accordance with LTH\u2019s Academic qualifications portfolio \u2013 see link below. Upload the application as PDF-files in the recruitment system. Read more: h ttp://www.lth.se/english/working-at-lth/to-apply-for-academic-positions-at-lth/ We welcome your application! ***************************************************************** Promotion to Senior Lecturer in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems During the period of employment, an assistant professor can apply for promotion to a permanent position as Senior Lecturer if he or she has the required qualifications listed below, and is deemed suitable. An assistant professor can only apply for promotion once. Qualification requirements Appointment to senior lecturer requires that the applicant has: A PhD or corresponding research competence or professional expertise considered important with regard to the subject matter of the post and the work duties it will involve. Demonstrated teaching expertise. Completed five weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning, or acquired equivalent knowledge by other means. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria specify the aspects to be considered, and the level to be achieved, for the assessment criteria to be deemed fulfilled. The following assessment criteria must be fulfilled for appointment to senior lecturer: A good national and international standing as a researcher. The requirement for international experience shall be assessed with consideration to the character and traditions of the subject. Good teaching ability, including a good ability to conduct, develop and lead teaching and other educational activities on different levels and using a variety of teaching methods. An ability to supervise doctoral students to achieve a PhD. An ability to collaborate with wider society and communicate his or her activities. A general ability to lead and develop activities. Additional requirements Good ability to collaborate, independence and drive. Progression in research and teaching expertise. Demonstrated ability to contribute to the research community, for example as a reviewer or organiser of conferences and workshops, and to the department's shared goals. LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2602 Contact Emelie Engstr\u00f6m, emelie.engstrom@cs.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364,kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362,st@st.lu.se Published 22.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968016/": {"title": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Cybersecurity", "description": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Cybersecurity Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Cybersecurity Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Division for Secure and Networked Systems within the Department of Electrical and Information Technology works broadly with research within cryptography, computer security, wireless and fixed networks. The division runs several research projects through different research collaboration platforms and arranges workshops and seminar series, making the research at the division visible to larger audiences. Cross-disciplinary projects are formed through our research collaboration platforms and national and international research networks, contributing to a dynamic research environment. We are now looking for a doctoral student to work within cybersecurity and software engineering in a project funded by the Swedish Foundation for Strategic Research, SSF. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Project description You will work in the RESIST project and primarily contribute to the area of \u200b\u200bprotection of distributed AI. RESIST is in collaboration with Link\u00f6ping University, \u00d6rebro University and the research institute RISE and is a multidisciplinary research center that works with the rapidly growing area of \u200b\u200bdeveloping conditions and techniques to protect future AI-based systems. The center is led by Link\u00f6ping University with Lund University as a partner. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. The main duties are to conduct research and teaching at the intersection of cyber-security and software engineering. The research focuses on automated principles for analysing program code. This includes how AI models can be used to analyze and correct software to ensure that it does not contain vulnerabilities. For example, it has been shown that AI-generated code often has significant security flaws. In order to use AI-generated code in high-security applications, the code generation process therefore needs to be made much more robust. The duties include evaluating existing techniques from a security perspective and identifying principles for automatic analysis and code correction. Case studies and experimental research are expected to be central research methods in the doctoral project. The duties also include participation in teaching and other departmental work (however, a maximum of 20% of working hours). Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in\u00a0Electrical Engineering if the applicant has: at least 60 second-cycle credits in subjects of relevance to Electrical Engineering, or an MSc in Engineering in Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Engineering Mathematics, Nanoengineering, Engineering Physics, or Information and Communication Engineering. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Very good software development skills. Experience of working with complex computer and communication systems. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Good ability to cooperate. Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Completed courses and/or master thesis work within Computer Security. Documented software engineering skills. Documented software development skills. Documented artificial intelligence technology skills. Documented teaching and communication skills. Industrial experience. We offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave, and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee Work at Lund University . About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staffpages . How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2645 Contact Christian Gehrmann, Professor, +46462220000, christian.gehrmann@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 17.Sep.2026 Last application date 23.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968020/": {"title": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Applied Cryptography and Privacy", "description": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Applied Cryptography and Privacy Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Applied Cryptography and Privacy Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Secure and Networked Systems Division within the Department of Electrical and Information Technology works broadly with research within Cryptography, Computer Security, Wireless and Fixed Networks. The security group within the Division has around 20 members. The main research directions are Cryptography, Privacy and System Security for Connected Systems. The division runs several research projects through different large research collaboration platforms and arranges extensive workshops and seminar series, making the research at the division visible to larger audiences. Cross-disciplinary projects are formed through our research collaboration platforms and national and international research networks, contributing to a dynamic research environment. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Subject and project description Through the Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program (WASP) we now offer a new doctoral student position in the field of Applied Cryptography and Privacy. WASP is Sweden\u2019s largest individual research program ever, a major national initiative for strategically motivated basic research, education and faculty recruitment. The program addresses research on artificial intelligence and autonomous systems acting in collaboration with humans, adapting to their environment through sensors, information and knowledge, and forming intelligent systems-of-systems. More about WASP (wasp-sweden.org). The primary duties of the doctoral student positions are to perform research and teaching within the Applied Cryptography and Privacy area. The research is devoted to the broader area of privacy-preserving communication and computation outsourcing. Communication over the internet is susceptible to surveillance and censorship. Privacy preserving communication techniques (e.g., Tor, Nym, Snowflake) allow users to circumvent such surveillance and censorship. The research scope would include designing, analysing and implementing such systems; additionally, studying different attacks and countermeasures are expected to be part of the research method. Privacy-preserving computation outsourcing allows users to outsource computation tasks to a cloud server without revealing to the server anything about the user data or even what kind of computations the user is performing. There are different techniques for such privacy-preserving computation outsourcing such as Trusted Execution Environment (e.g., Intel SGX) and Fully Homomorphic Encryption (TFHE, BGV). Furthermore, the specific functions/tasks can be subject to attacks, and identifying attacks and countermeasures is expected to be studied. The research method will be a combination of system studies, design, and experimental research. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. The work duties include: Research in applied cryptography and privacy. Contributing to research projects. Taking doctoral students courses. The duties also include participation in teaching and other departmental work (however, a maximum of 20% of working hours). Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Electrical Engineering if the applicant has: at least 60 second-cycle credits in subjects of relevance to Electrical Engineering, or a MSc in Engineering in Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Engineering Mathematics, Nanoengineering, Engineering Physics, or Information and Communication Engineering. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Good programming skills. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Good ability to cooperate. Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Completed courses and/or master thesis work within Computer Security and/or Cryptology. Industrial experience. Documented software development skills. Documented teaching and communication skills. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se . About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staffpages . How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/ employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2647 Contact Debajyoti Das, Associate senior lecturer, +46462220000, debajyoti.das@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 17.Sep.2026 Last application date 23.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:966816/": {"title": "Universitetslektor i processr\u00e4tt", "description": "Universitetslektor i processr\u00e4tt Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetslektor i processr\u00e4tt Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett fullskaligt och forskningsintensivt universitet, och ing\u00e5r som enda svenska universitet i de starka internationella n\u00e4tverken League of European Research Universities (LERU) och Universitas 21 (U21). Lunds universitet har partneruniversitet i n\u00e4rmare 70 l\u00e4nder, och attraherar flest internationella studenter av alla svenska universitet. Juridiska fakulteten k\u00e4nnetecknas av internationalisering, sammanfl\u00e4tning av utbildning och forskning, tv\u00e4rvetenskap samt n\u00e4ra och gr\u00e4ns\u00f6verskridande samverkan med det omgivande samh\u00e4llet. Fakultetens forskningsmilj\u00f6 och utbildning p\u00e5 forskarniv\u00e5 pr\u00e4glas av internationalisering, och vid sidan av juristprogrammet erbjuds ocks\u00e5 flera internationella mastersprogram. Lunds universitet och den Juridiska fakulteten erbjuder en utvecklande och inkluderande arbetsmilj\u00f6 i den bredare dynamiska vetenskaps- och innovationsregion som \u00d6resundsregionen utg\u00f6r. \u00c4mne Processr\u00e4tt med s\u00e4rskild inriktning mot civilprocess \u00c4mnesbeskrivning \u00c4mnet processr\u00e4tt omfattar fr\u00e4mst f\u00f6rfaranden i tvistem\u00e5l, brottm\u00e5l och f\u00f6rvaltningsm\u00e5l vid allm\u00e4nna domstolar, allm\u00e4nna f\u00f6rvaltningsdomstolar och specialdomstolar samt f\u00f6rfarandet vid exekutiv myndighet. \u00c4mnet omfattar ocks\u00e5 medling, f\u00f6rlikningsf\u00f6rhandlingar, skiljef\u00f6rfaranden och andra alternativa privatr\u00e4ttsliga r\u00e4ttsskipningsf\u00f6rfaranden. \u00c4mnet processr\u00e4tt begr\u00e4nsar sig i stort till att avse i Sverige g\u00e4llande r\u00e4tt, vare sig denna har ett nationellt, nordiskt, europeiskt eller ett vidare internationellt ursprung. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna omfattar ett s\u00e4rskilt ansvar f\u00f6r undervisning och examination i fr\u00e4mst svensk processr\u00e4tt inom ramen f\u00f6r juristprogrammet med s\u00e4rskild betoning p\u00e5 civilprocessr\u00e4tt. I arbetsuppgifterna ing\u00e5r att undervisa p\u00e5 juristprogrammets grund- och f\u00f6rdjupningskursniv\u00e5, att handleda och examinera examensarbeten, samt att handleda doktorander. D\u00e4rut\u00f6ver ing\u00e5r handledning och examination av uppsatser inom kursen R\u00e4ttsvetenskaplig uppsats p\u00e5 juristprogrammets sj\u00e4tte termin. \u00c4ven annan undervisning kan ing\u00e5. D\u00e4rut\u00f6ver innefattar arbetsuppgifterna att aktivt verka f\u00f6r en pedagogisk utveckling av utbildningen p\u00e5 alla niv\u00e5er. Undervisningen sker i f\u00f6rsta hand p\u00e5 svenska men \u00e4ven undervisning p\u00e5 engelska kan f\u00f6rekomma. I arbetsuppgifterna ing\u00e5r vidare att genom undervisning, handledning och samarbete med l\u00e4rare, forskare, doktorander och studenter samt samverkan med det omgivande samh\u00e4llet vidmakth\u00e5lla och vidareutveckla en stimulerande forsknings- och utbildningsmilj\u00f6. Till dessa arbetsuppgifter h\u00f6r s\u00e4rskilt att aktivt bedriva forskning och medverka till en utveckling av forskningsmilj\u00f6n i processr\u00e4tt. Fakultetens forskare och l\u00e4rare f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas bidra till en levande forskningsmilj\u00f6 och fakultetens \u00f6vriga verksamhet och i huvudsak bedriva arbetet p\u00e5 arbetsplatsen. Beh\u00f6righet Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som universitetslektor \u00e4r den som dels har visat pedagogisk skicklighet, dels har avlagt juris doktorsexamen eller utl\u00e4ndsk examen som bed\u00f6ms motsvara en juris doktorsexamen eller har uppn\u00e5tt motsvarande vetenskaplig kompetens eller n\u00e5gon annan yrkesskicklighet som \u00e4r av betydelse med h\u00e4nsyn till anst\u00e4llningens \u00e4mnesinneh\u00e5ll och de arbetsuppgifter som ska ing\u00e5 i anst\u00e4llningen. F\u00f6r universitetslektor g\u00e4ller som allm\u00e4nt beh\u00f6righetskrav att vara l\u00e4mplig f\u00f6r och ha den f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga i \u00f6vrigt som beh\u00f6vs f\u00f6r att v\u00e4l fullg\u00f6ra arbetsuppgifterna i den aktuella anst\u00e4llningen. Enligt Lunds universitets anst\u00e4llningsordning m\u00e5ste den s\u00f6kande \u00e4ven ha genomg\u00e5tt h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller p\u00e5 annat s\u00e4tt ha inh\u00e4mtat motsvarande kunskaper f\u00f6r att vara beh\u00f6rig. Om det finns s\u00e4rskilda sk\u00e4l kan den som inte har h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor \u00e4nd\u00e5 anses vara beh\u00f6rig. Bed\u00f6mningsgrunder Som bed\u00f6mningsgrunder vid anst\u00e4llning av en universitetslektor ska graden av s\u00e5dan skicklighet som \u00e4r ett krav f\u00f6r beh\u00f6righet f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llning g\u00e4lla. Pr\u00f6vningen av den pedagogiska skickligheten ska \u00e4gnas lika stor omsorg som pr\u00f6vningen av andra beh\u00f6righetsgrundande f\u00f6rh\u00e5llanden. Vid anst\u00e4llning som universitetslektor ska f\u00f6ljande utg\u00f6ra grund f\u00f6r bed\u00f6mning: God nationell och internationell niv\u00e5 som forskare, d\u00e4r kravet p\u00e5 internationell meritering ska bed\u00f6mas med h\u00e4nsyn till \u00e4mnets karakt\u00e4r och tradition God pedagogisk f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, vilket inneb\u00e4r god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att bedriva, utveckla och leda undervisning och annan pedagogisk verksamhet p\u00e5 olika niv\u00e5er och med varierande undervisningsmetoder F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att delta i handledning av doktorander i studier till doktorsexamen F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att samverka med det omgivande samh\u00e4llet och att informera om sin verksamhet F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga i \u00f6vrigt att leda och utveckla verksamhet F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att undervisa p\u00e5 svenska eller annat skandinaviskt spr\u00e5k p\u00e5 juristprogrammet \u00e4r ett krav liksom f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att undervisa p\u00e5 engelska Dokumenterad erfarenhet av undervisning inom svensk civilprocessr\u00e4tt S\u00e4rskild vikt kommer att f\u00e4stas vid: Goda \u00e4mneskunskaper i svensk civilprocessr\u00e4tt Erfarenhet av kursansvar p\u00e5 grund- och/eller avancerad niv\u00e5 Kreativitet och visad innovativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga avseende utveckling av kurser, l\u00e4randemoment och l\u00e4romedel Vikt kommer ocks\u00e5 att f\u00e4stas vid i processr\u00e4tt: Bred \u00e4mnesm\u00e4ssig kompetens Dokumenterad f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att formulera forskningsans\u00f6kningar om externa medel Dokumenterade internationella forsknings- och undervisningserfarenheter, exempelvis i form av publikationer, forsknings- och undervisningsvistelser i utlandet, forskningssamarbeten och konferenspresentationer Anvisningar f\u00f6r ans\u00f6kan Ans\u00f6kan till anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks elektroniskt via Lunds universitets s\u00f6kandeportal. Kompletteringar i form av inbundna publikationer/motsvarande, skickas i tre exemplar till: Juridiska fakulteten vid Lunds universitet, att: Helena Josefsson, Box 207, 221 00 Lund. Ans\u00f6kan ska utformas i enlighet med f\u00f6ljande mall (f\u00f6r akademisk meritportf\u00f6lj, inneh\u00e5llande beskrivningar av meriter, se l\u00e4nk) och inneh\u00e5lla f\u00f6ljande: Personligt brev Kortfattad curriculum vitae (CV) Beskrivning av vetenskapliga meriter med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning av forskningen, forskningsprofil, forskningsverksamhet inkl. nationella och internationella meriter, forskningserfarenheter och meriter) Fullst\u00e4ndig publikationslista F\u00f6rteckning \u00f6ver doktorsavhandlingen och de \u00f6vriga 5 vetenskapliga arbeten som s\u00f6kanden \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa. De \u00e5beropade 6 publikationerna ska bil\u00e4ggas ans\u00f6kan. DOI-kod f\u00f6r varje publikation ska anges om s\u00e5dan finns. Beskrivning av pedagogiska meriter med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning av den pedagogiska verksamheten, kort pedagogisk sj\u00e4lvreflektion, pedagogisk meritf\u00f6rteckning) Beskrivning av meriter r\u00f6rande ledarskap och administration med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning, kort sj\u00e4lvreflektion och meritf\u00f6rteckning av administrativa erfarenheter och ledningsuppdrag) Beskrivning av meriter r\u00f6rande samverkan med bilagor (s\u00e5som sammanfattning, kort sj\u00e4lvreflektion och meritf\u00f6rteckning av insatser och \u00e5taganden r\u00f6rande samverkan) \u00d6vriga handlingar som s\u00f6kanden \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa V\u00e4nligen notera att de handlingar som inkommer eller uppr\u00e4ttas med anledning av denna ledigf\u00f6rklarade anst\u00e4llning (s\u00e5som ans\u00f6kningar, sakkunnigutl\u00e5tanden och protokoll) som huvudregel \u00e4r allm\u00e4nna och d\u00e4rmed offentliga. Detta inneb\u00e4r att handlingarna f\u00e5r (med undantag f\u00f6r sekretessbelagda handlingar) l\u00e4sas av den som s\u00e5 beg\u00e4r det. Villkor Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Vi ser j\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet och m\u00e5ngfald som en styrka och tillg\u00e5ng. V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Juridiska fakulteten \u00e4r en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 och avancerad niv\u00e5 och ett 160-tal anst\u00e4llda varav ett 40-tal \u00e4r doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns p\u00e5 v\u00e5r hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-06-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2605 Kontakt Ellika Sevelin, Prefekt, 0462221099, ellika.sevelin@jur.lu.se Helena Josefsson, Kanslichef, 046-2221095, helena.josefsson@jur.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-15 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-15 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964482/": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry", "description": "Assistant Professor in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Assistant Professor in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Department of Chemistry at Lund University, Faculty of Engineering, invites applications for a position as Assistant Professor in Polymer technology with focus on polymer chemistry. Placed at the Centre for Analysis and Synthesis (CAS) at the Department of Chemistry, the recruited Assistant Professor will be supported by funding of a PhD student. The Department of Chemistry conducts research across all core areas of chemistry with a broad theme of research in support of a sustainable society. Focus areas include the environment, renewable resources, energy and health. Of special relevance are molecular design and synthesis, and understanding of the interplay between structure and properties, chemical and physical processes, and application performance. Advanced characterization of material properties by, e.g., electron microscopy and X-ray characterization (in particular at the synchrotron MAX IV) is also a focal area of the Department. Current research within polymer technology at CAS is mainly directed towards polymers for energy and the environment, including polymeric materials for energy storage and conversion, and sustainable biobased polymers. We synthesize and characterize new monomers, polymer structures, and materials to establish fundamental structure-property relationships relevant for specific application areas. In our work we emphasize a creative environment characterized by scientific excellence, diversity, generosity and freedom. We are now expanding and need to further strengthen our capacity and competence in polymer chemistry. In this context, the successful candidate may develop new synthetic pathways to meet demanding polymer properties for specific application areas. The choice of research approach, application area, etc., will be determined by the research interests of the candidate. Combinations of experimental techniques and theory are most welcome. The position therefore offers an excellent opportunity to develop an independent research programme at the interface of polymer chemistry, material science and sustainability, supported by a strong research environment and dedicated PhD-student funding. Subject Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry . Subject description Deep knowledge in polymer technology and polymer chemistry is crucial for the development, production, application and recyclability of the next generation of efficient and environmentally benign polymeric materials. Polymer technology is an interdisciplinary subject including the chemistry and physics of polymers, polymers from renewable resources, processing and use of polymer materials, and degradation and environmental aspects of polymer materials. Polymer chemistry comprises polymerisations and chemical modifications of polymers, combined with polymer characterisation to determine fundamental structure-property relationships. Work duties Employment as an assistant professor is a tenure track position, which aims for the holder to develop their independence as a researcher and educator. The work duties mainly involve research and teaching. The position includes the opportunity to undertake five weeks of training in teaching and learning in higher education. Work duties include: Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Qualification requirements for employment as an assistant professor are fulfilled by someone who has been awarded a doctorate or has the corresponding research competence. Primary consideration should be given to someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent competence within seven years of the deadline for application for employment as an assistant professor. However, someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent expertise at an earlier date may also be considered if there are special grounds. Special grounds are sick leave, parental leave or other similar circumstances. Assessment criteria For appointment to assistant professor, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and carry out high-quality research. Teaching ability. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Extensive documented experience within polymer chemistry, including the synthesis and characterization of structure and fundamental properties of polymers. Experience of postdoctoral research in a research environment other than the university at which the applicant obtained their PhD degree A submitted research plan (1500-2000 words) that can form the basis for external funding Collaborative skills, initiative and the ability to solve work tasks independently, as well as a demonstrated interest in leadership. Other qualifications Documented ability to acquire competitive external research funding. As part of the application, the applicant is to submit a research plan (1500-2000 words) clearly describing the research that will be conducted during the employment within the topic of Polymer Chemistry . The plan should also describe how the applicant\u2019s research could complement and reinforce research at the Department of Chemistry. The quality of the research plan shall be given substantial weight in the selection of candidates. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 6 years. The employment is regulated in accordance with Chapter 4 Section 12a\u00a7 HEA. The purpose of the appointment is for the teacher to be given the opportunity to develop research autonomy and acquire the scholarly and teaching qualifications required for eligibility for appointment as a senior lecturer. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English. Please draw up the application in accordance with LTH\u2019s Academic qualifications portfolio \u2013 see link below. Upload the application as PDF-files in the recruitment system. Read more: http://www.lth.se/english/working-at-lth/to-apply-for-academic-positions-at-lth/ We welcome your application! ***************************************************************** Promotion to Senior Lecturer in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry During the period of employment, an assistant professor can apply for promotion to a permanent position as Senior Lecturer if he or she has the required qualifications listed below, and is deemed suitable. An assistant professor can only apply for promotion once. Qualification requirements Appointment to senior lecturer requires that the applicant has: A PhD or corresponding research competence or professional expertise considered important with regard to the subject matter of the post and the work duties it will involve. Demonstrated teaching expertise. Completed five weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning, or acquired equivalent knowledge by other means. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria specify the aspects to be considered, and the level to be achieved, for the assessment criteria to be deemed fulfilled. The following assessment criteria must be fulfilled for appointment to senior lecturer: A good national and international standing as a researcher. The requirement for international experience shall be assessed with consideration to the character and traditions of the subject. Good teaching ability, including a good ability to conduct, develop and lead teaching and other educational activities on different levels and using a variety of teaching methods. An ability to supervise doctoral students to achieve a PhD. An ability to collaborate with wider society and communicate his or her activities. A general ability to lead and develop activities. Additional requirements Demonstrated scientific independence, shown among other things by several publications published without their previous supervisors or mentors, where the applicant has clearly had a leading (PI) role. Good ability to collaborate, independence and drive. Sufficient knowledge of Swedish to carry out administrative and educational tasks that require an understanding of Swedish. Progression in research and teaching expertise. Ability to actively, independently, and successfully seek external funding as main applicant. This means that the applicant has received multi-year research grants from large national or international funders such as ERC, Wallenberg Foundations, Swedish Research Council, Formas, Swedish Energy Agency, etc. If the applicant has not received such funding as main applicant, they must be able to show very good evaluations from the application process. LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2526 Contact Ola Wendt, +46462228153, ola.wendt@chem.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 09.Sep.2026 Last application date 03.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:930481/": {"title": "Senior Lecturer in technical GIS", "description": "Senior Lecturer in technical GIS Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in technical GIS Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Research and education at the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences (MGeo) addresses fundamental and applied questions on the Earth\u2019s past, present and future climate and environment, including people\u2019s interactions with the natural world and consequences for human wellbeing. MGeo advances and deploys cutting-edge methods, models and technologies in environmental science, quaternary sciences, bedrock geology, paleontology, physical geography, biodiversity and ecosystem science, remote sensing, Geographic Information Science (GIS), and computational science for health and environment, to study processes spanning from the microscopic to the planetary, across all time scales. Lund University welcomes applicants with different backgrounds and experiences. Gender equality, equal opportunities and diversity are fundamental principles in all parts of the University\u2019s activities. Find more reasons why Lund University and the Faculty of Science are right for you here and here , and learn more about what it is like to Working in Lund , Moving to Lund and Living in Lund . Research and education at the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences (MGeo) address fundamental and applied questions on the Earth\u2019s past, present and future climate and environment, including people\u2019s interactions with the natural world and consequences for human wellbeing. MGeo advances and deploys cutting-edge methods, models and technologies in environmental science, quaternary sciences, bedrock geology, paleontology, physical geography, biodiversity and ecosystem science, remote sensing, Geographic Information Science (GIS), and computational science for health and environment, to study processes spanning from the microscopic to the planetary, across all time scales. Job description The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the department\u2019s core activities in research, teaching and collaboration, as well as, where appropriate, academic leadership roles. The post involves research in geographic information science, with an emphasis on the technical aspects of GIS. The successful candidate is expected to actively seek and secure external research funding, publish in peer-reviewed scientific journals, and contribute to the development of the department\u2019s research environment, including interdisciplinary collaborations. The duties also include teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in geographic information science (GIS), with a particular focus on technically oriented courses such as geographic databases, Web GIS, GIS algorithms and data structures, geospatial artificial intelligence (GeoAI), and the collection and analysis of 3D geodata. The position includes course coordination, course development and participation in pedagogical development within the subject area. Within the framework of outreach, the successful candidate is expected to engage with the wider community, including public authorities, industry and other societal stakeholders, and to contribute to the application of GIS and geospatial technologies in relevant societal areas. The duties may also include participation in departmental and faculty-wide administrative and management-related tasks, such as committee work, programme development and coordination assignments. The allocation of time between research, teaching, outreach and administrative duties follows the faculty\u2019s working hours model, under which teaching normally accounts for approximately 25\u201335% of a full-time position, with the remaining time divided between research, outreach and other duties. The content, distribution and scope of the duties may change over time in line with the development of the organisation, strategic priorities and external conditions. To support the establishment of a research group, resources equivalent to a PhD student position will be attached to the post. Qualification requirements A person is qualified to be employed as a senior lecturer if they have demonstrated teaching expertise and been awarded a PhD in subject matter of relevance to the position, or equivalent research expertise, in accordance with the Higher Education Ordinance, Chapter 4 Section 4. For this position, applicants must hold a PhD in Geographic Information Systems, Geographic Information Science, Geoinformatics, Engineering Surveying, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related or equivalent subject area. The position requires at least five weeks\u2019 training in teaching and learning in higher education or corresponding knowledge that has been obtained in some other way. An exception to this requirement may be made in special cases. Applicants who do not possess training in teaching and learning in higher education are to undergo such training within two years of taking up the position. Teaching staff at Lund University are required to be suitable for the position and to have the general ability to fulfil their work duties well. Assessment criteria The requirements for the position are: The applicant must demonstrate a strong academic background in the technical aspects of geographic information science (GIS). Academic competence must be evidenced by publications in reputable, peer-reviewed scientific journals. The applicant must demonstrate a proven ability to successfully secure external research funding in a competitive environment, as well as experience of leading their own research projects. The applicant must demonstrate documented experience of teaching at advanced level in GIS, particularly in areas such as geographic databases, web GIS, GIS algorithms and data structures, geospatial artificial intelligence (GeoAI), and the collection and analysis of 3D geodata. The applicant must have experience of teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. The applicant must demonstrate experience of supervising undergraduates and PhD students. The applicant must demonstrate a strong ability to engage with the wider community, including experience of applying GIS and geospatial technologies in areas such as the environment and climate, urban planning, health and epidemiology, and disaster management, preferably in collaboration with public sector bodies, industry or other societal stakeholders. The applicant must have a very good command of spoken and written English. The applicant must have experience of research and/or teaching outside Lund University. The applicant must have very good collaborative skills and well-developed communication skills. Merits for the position are: Experience and knowledge of geospatial artificial intelligence (GeoAI) and/or digital twins. Leadership skills, including experience of leading research projects or research teams. Proven experience of interdisciplinary collaboration. Experience of developing innovative teaching methods in GIS. Active participation in international research and education networks. Good command of Swedish, both spoken and written. Experience of distance learning at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level. Personal qualities The applicant should demonstrate creativity, strong drive and the ability to familiarise themselves with new fields of research. The ability to share knowledge and contribute to a collegial and collaborative academic environment is of great importance. The applicant must have the ability to interact effectively with research, teaching and administrative staff, both internally and externally, including stakeholders in academia, industry and the public sector. Further considerations As much attention will be given to the assessment of teaching expertise as to the assessment of research expertise. When appointing teaching staff, Lund University\u2019s Appointment Rules apply, in addition to the provisions set out in the Higher Education Ordinance. For a non-Swedish speaking staff members, language level B2* must be achieved in Swedish within three years. *Common European Framework of Reference for Language, CEFR. What we offer Lund University is a public authority which means that you receive special benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension. Read more on the University website about working with us. Design and content of the application We recommend you write your application in English, as it may be reviewed by international external experts. The application is to be completed according to the Faculty of Science\u2019s application instructions for teaching positions . Upload the application to the recruitment system as PDF files. Please note that it is very important that you follow the application instructions. An application that is incomplete will be rejected. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/1439 Contact Ali Mansourian Ali Mansourian, Professor, ali.mansourian@mgeo.lu.se Ying Pan, Recruitment Coordinator, +46462228917, ying.pan@science.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 08.Sep.2026 Last application date 04.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:961545/": {"title": "Doctoral Student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control", "description": "Doctoral Student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Doctoral student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control Lund University, The Faculty of Engineering, Department Description of the workplace Automatic Control is an exciting and broad subject, covering both advanced mathematics and hands-on engineering. Historically, it has been instrumental in many areas, from the early development of telecommunications to the space race. Today, driven by the need to engineer ever larger systems, Automatic Control is more relevant than ever. The department of Automatic control has a stimulating and international environment with PhD students, postdocs, and teachers coming from all corners of the world. Research and teaching are conducted in an open and progressive atmosphere with collaborations both within academia and with industry, nationally as well as internationally. A PhD degree from the Department of Automatic control gives you the perfect base for an exciting career, be it in academia or industry. Lund University and the Department of Automatic Control welcome applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences. We regard equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. For more information on being a doctoral student at the department, please have a look at our research videos: Research | Department of Automatic Control (lth.se). Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se. https://www.lth.se/english/study-at-lth/phd-studies/ AEGIS \u2014 Adaptive Grid-Interactive Edge Datacenter Fleets\u00a0is a European Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Action (MSCA) research and training network. It is funded by the EU and trains 15 PhD students from 2026 to 2030. The main host for this position is Department of Automatic Control at Lund University. As part of the program you will spend two 3-months visits with partners in the network: \u00c9cole Polytechnique F\u00e9d\u00e9rale de Lausanne (Switzerland) and Elisa\u00a0(Finland). Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie fellowships are among the most respected PhD positions in Europe. The position is only open to applicants that have not lived, studied, or worked in Sweden for more than 12 months in the 36 months before applying. More information about the project is available at the website https://aegis-dn.eu Subject and project description The AEGIS project sits where two fast-growing fields meet: datacentres and AI infrastructure on one side, energy and power systems on the other. Few people today can work across both, so the skills you build here are scarce and in high demand. Specifically there is a gap between a high-level goal like \u201ccut carbon now\u201d and the low-level controls of a site\u2019s cooling, batteries, and compute hardware. In this project you close that gap. You will build a control layer that takes \u201cintents\u201d and translates them into a coordinated set of actions across the site\u2019s physical assets. The models close the loop and tune themselves online using both classical control, AI, and reinforcement learning. In the project you will work on: Designing an intent language that captures carbon, flexibility, and cost. Breaking high-level intents down into control actions. Tuning power-performance and thermal models online. What you will deliver: Control software that turns intents into commands, with measured latency. Practical control systems using real-world data from experiments. A telemetry system that reports headroom and runs without breaking service-level limits in test scenarios. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. The PhD position consists of three main aspects, and the work duties include: research project, including authoring papers and traveling to conferences, seminars etc. postgraduate courses, given locally, nationally and internationally (90 ECTS credits) teaching (no more than 20%), including lab supervision and exam responsibilities. This part may also include departmental services, such as working with equality and diversity, arranging events etc Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantial equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Automatic Control if the applicant has: knowledge corresponding to course FRTF05 (previously FRT010) Automatic Control, Basic Course and a second cycle specialisation of relevance to the subject, and an MSc in engineering or corresponding qualification The standard MSCA eligibility criteria also apply: No doctoral degree.\u00a0At the date of recruitment you must not yet hold a PhD. Mobility rule.\u00a0You must not have lived or done your main activity (work or studies) in Sweden for more than 12 months in the 36 months just before you are recruited. Short stays such as holidays do not count. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Good language-analytical ability. Curiosity about research and teaching in general, and motivation for the particular research project. Creativity with good ability for cooperation and networking. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Strong mathematical knowledge as demonstrated through university transcripts. Other qualifications (advantages) For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Strong foundations in Machine learning and reinformement learning. Cloud computing and cloud technology. Low-level programming and Linux kernel experience. are meriting. Consideration will be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant,through experience and skills, is deemed to have the abilities necessary for successfully completing the third cycle programme. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se. https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible or March 1, 2027, at the latest. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 \u00a7\u00a7. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University\u2019s Staffpages. https://www.staff.lu.se/research-and-education/research-support/doctoral-education/terms-employment-doctoral-students Other We intend to offer employment to 1 PhD student. A doctoral student will receive a competitive monthly salary of 35 900 SEK with yearly raise. Those applicants who will be called for interview, might be asked to perform a small test to demonstrate basic competence. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2448 Contact Johan Eker, +46462228780, johan.eker@control.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 08.Sep.2026 Last application date 23.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:943541/": {"title": "Senior Lecturer in Experimental Medical Science", "description": "Senior Lecturer in Experimental Medical Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in Experimental Medical Science Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Employment This is permanent employment as a senior lecturer in experimental medical science, with placement at either the Department of Experimental Medical Science (EMV) or the Department of Laboratory Medicine (ILM). The department to which the employment is attached will be decided upon appointment. Duties The main responsibilities will be to lead and develop undergraduate and second cycle education in experimental medicine. The successful candidate will therefore be expected to be prepared to take on key leadership roles at course or program level within the Medical Programme or Biomedicine Programmes. The position also involves teaching and evaluation within the Biomedicine Programmes and/or the first cycle of the Medical Programme (semesters 1-5) using various forms of active learning. As a guideline, teaching, educational management and educational development work is expected to account for approximately 70% of the time over time. Tasks related to third cycle studies may also be included. The teaching role is therefore the main focus of employment. In addition to teaching, the position involves active research in experimental medicine. The position also includes the responsibilities normally associated with the position of Senior Lecturer, such as administrative duties and internal and external elected offices at the national and international levels. Other duties may also be required. Eligibility A person is eligible for employment as a senior lecturer under Chapter 4, Section 4 of the Higher Education Ordinance if he/she has demonstrated teaching ability and has either a doctoral degree or equivalent academic or other professional competence relevant to the subject matter of the employment and the duties to be performed in the position. The applicant must have completed a course in higher education pedagogy lasting at least five weeks. Should the appointee be assessed to have valid reasons for not having completed a five-week course in higher education pedagogy upon taking up the position, they must complete such a course within two years of taking up the position (see Lund University\u2019s Staff Regulations ). Language proficiency equivalent to at least level C2 in Swedish, as per the Council of Europe\u2019s proficiency scale, is a requirement for employment. For teaching staff members at Lund University, the general requirements are that they are suitable for the role and possess the other abilities necessary to carry out their duties effectively.\u00a0l Assessment criteria The applicant must have demonstrated teaching, academic, and administrative competence relevant to the discipline; particular emphasis will be placed on teaching competence during the review process. The applicant must demonstrate teaching expertise relevant to the subject area, both in teaching and in supervision at undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral levels. This is demonstrated by a proven ability to deliver teaching and summative assessment through various forms of active learning, in accordance with the Faculty of Medicine\u2019s educational plan. The ability to lead and develop university-level education at first- and second cycle level is advantageous. The candidate\u2019s own development work in higher education pedagogy or research projects is also advantageous. In addition, the applicant must demonstrate research expertise by conducting his/her own current research. Research expertise is demonstrated by publications in international scientific journals, competitive grants, and experience in national and international research collaborations. In addition, research expertise is demonstrated by relevant research programs and the potential for long-term career development. The candidate must demonstrate strong leadership skills and the ability to work collaboratively and externally with the broader community. When employing teaching staff, in addition to the consequences of the Higher Education Ordinance , Lund University\u2019s Staff Regulations and the Faculty of Medicine\u2019s general requirements and assessment criteria for Senior Lecturer shall apply. Further information For further information, please contact Dean Maria Bj\u00f6rkqvist, tel. +46 72 700 71 63, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se or Head of Department Karolin Hans\u00e9n Nord, tel. +46 70 283 1827, karolin.hansen_nord@med.lu.se or Head of Department Tomas Deierborg, tel. +46 70 970 8212, tomas.deierborg@med.lu.se Further information on the application process can be obtained from the recruitment coordinator, Eva A Nilsson, tel. +46 46 222 17 89, eva_a.nilsson@med.lu.se The employment will be filled following a recommendation from the Medical Academic Appointment Board. Application procedure Applications for this employment must be submitted online via Lund University\u2019s application portal by 27 November 2026 at the latest. Applications must be submitted in accordance with the Faculty of Medicine's guidelines for applicants for faculty positions (see \"Summary of Qualifications and CV\"). The university applies a system of individual salary-setting. Please state your salary expectations in your application. Lund University welcomes applicants from a variety of backgrounds and with a range of experiences. We regard gender equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. We look forward to receiving your application! The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment Enligt \u00f6verenskommelse Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/1950 Contact Maria Bj\u00f6rkqvist, Dekan, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Karolin Hans\u00e9n Nord, Prefekt ILM, karolin.hansen_nord@med.lu.se Tomas Deierborg, Prefekt EMV, tomas.deierborg@med.lu.se Eva Nilsson, Rekryteringskoordinator, eva_a.nilsson@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:902060/": {"title": "Senior Lecturer in Gynaecology combined with a position as Specialist Physician/Consultant", "description": "Senior Lecturer in Gynaecology combined with a position as Specialist Physician/Consultant Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in Gynaecology combined with a position as Specialist Physician/Consultant Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r placerad vid Institutionen f\u00f6r kliniska vetenskaper i Malm\u00f6. Den kliniska tj\u00e4nstg\u00f6ringen sker vid Kvinnokliniken, Sk\u00e5nes universitetssjukhus. Arbetsuppgifter Anst\u00e4llningen utlyses f\u00f6r att s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla grundutbildningens behov inom \u00e4mnet obstetrik och\u00a0 gynekologi. Den huvudsakliga arbetsuppgiften \u00e4r att leda och driva utbildningen inom obstetrik och gynekologi i Malm\u00f6 samt vara en av tre \u00e4mneansvariga inom l\u00e4karprogrammet. Innehavaren ska dessutom vara beredd att ta p\u00e5 sig ytterligare ledningsuppdrag inom \u00e4mnet p\u00e5 l\u00e4karprogrammet, liksom andra utbildningsuppdrag p\u00e5 grund- och avancerad niv\u00e5 vid Medicinska fakultetens utbildningsprogram samt inom forskarutbildningen. Ut\u00f6ver utbildningsuppdraget ing\u00e5r att bedriva forskning inom obstetrik och gynekologi samt att medverka i forskarutbildningen. Innehavaren f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas ocks\u00e5 vara beredd att bist\u00e5 ledningsgruppen i utbildningsfr\u00e5gor och medverka till strategisk utveckling av b\u00e5de utbildning och forskning inom \u00e4mnesomr\u00e5det. Anst\u00e4llningen innefattar \u00e4ven arbetsuppgifter som normalt \u00e4r f\u00f6rknippade med en tj\u00e4nst som universitetslektor, s\u00e5som administration samt interna och externa f\u00f6rtroendeuppdrag p\u00e5 nationell och internationell niv\u00e5. I anst\u00e4llningen ing\u00e5r sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndig klinisk tj\u00e4nstg\u00f6ring inklusive jourtj\u00e4nstg\u00f6ring. \u00c4ven andra arbetsuppgifter kan f\u00f6rekomma. Beh\u00f6righet Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som lektor enligt H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen 4 kap 4 \u00a7 \u00e4r den som dels har visat pedagogisk skicklighet, dels har avlagt doktorsexamen eller har motsvarande vetenskaplig kompetens eller n\u00e5gon annan yrkesskicklighet som \u00e4r av betydelse med h\u00e4nsyn till anst\u00e4llningens \u00e4mnesinneh\u00e5ll och de arbetsuppgifter som ska ing\u00e5 i anst\u00e4llningen. Enligt Lunds universitets anst\u00e4llningsordning m\u00e5ste den s\u00f6kande ha genomg\u00e5tt h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller p\u00e5 annat s\u00e4tt ha inh\u00e4mtat motsvarande kunskaper f\u00f6r att vara beh\u00f6rig, om det inte f\u00f6religger s\u00e4rskilda sk\u00e4l. I den h\u00e4ndelse att innehavaren bed\u00f6ms ha s\u00e4rskilda sk\u00e4l f\u00f6r att inte ha genomg\u00e5tt fem veckors h\u00f6gskolepedagogisk utbildning vid tilltr\u00e4det av tj\u00e4nsten, ska innehavaren genomf\u00f6ra s\u00e5dan utbildning inom tv\u00e5 \u00e5r fr\u00e5n tilltr\u00e4det. D\u00e5 arbetsuppgifterna inneb\u00e4r att leda och utveckla samt att undervisa inom grundutbildningen p\u00e5 fr\u00e4mst l\u00e4karprogrammet, \u00e4r svensk eller nordisk l\u00e4karlegitimation och specialistkompetens i obstetrik och gynekologi samt mycket goda kunskaper i svenska ett krav vid tilltr\u00e4det. Spr\u00e5kkunskap i svenska l\u00e4gst niv\u00e5 C2 enligt Europar\u00e5dets niv\u00e5skala \u00e4r ett krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen. F\u00f6r l\u00e4rare vid Lunds universitet g\u00e4ller som allm\u00e4nt beh\u00f6righetskrav att vara l\u00e4mplig f\u00f6r och ha den f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga i \u00f6vrigt som beh\u00f6vs f\u00f6r att fullg\u00f6ra arbetsuppgifterna v\u00e4l. Bed\u00f6mningsgrunder Den s\u00f6kande ska ha visat pedagogisk, vetenskaplig, administrativ och klinisk skicklighet av betydelse f\u00f6r \u00e4mnet och vid bed\u00f6mningen kommer s\u00e4rskild vikt att tillm\u00e4tas den pedagogiska skickligheten. Den s\u00f6kande ska uppvisa pedagogisk skicklighet av relevans f\u00f6r \u00e4mnesomr\u00e5det s\u00e5v\u00e4l inom utbildning som inom handledning p\u00e5 grund-, avancerad- och forskarutbildningsniv\u00e5. Detta visas genom en god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att planera, leda, utveckla, driva och genomf\u00f6ra utbildning samt f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att oms\u00e4tta klinisk kompetens i utbildningsmoment. F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att leda universitetsutbildning p\u00e5 grund- och avancerad niv\u00e5 kommer att vara s\u00e4rskilt meriterande. Vidare ska den s\u00f6kande uppvisa vetenskaplig skicklighet genom att bedriva egen aktuell forskning p\u00e5 h\u00f6g nationell eller internationell niv\u00e5. Vetenskaplig skicklighet visas genom publikationer i internationella vetenskapliga tidskrifter, anslag erh\u00e5llna i konkurrens samt erfarenhet av nationellt och internationellt forskningssamarbete. Vidare visas vetenskaplig skicklighet genom forskningsprogram av relevans f\u00f6r \u00e4mnet och f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r l\u00e5ngsiktig karri\u00e4rutveckling. Den s\u00f6kande ska visa god f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga till ledarskap, samarbete och samverkan med det omgivande samh\u00e4llet. Vid anst\u00e4llning av l\u00e4rare g\u00e4ller, ut\u00f6ver vad som f\u00f6ljer av H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen, Lunds universitets anst\u00e4llningsordning samt Medicinska fakultetens allm\u00e4nna kravprofil och bed\u00f6mningsgrunder vid anst\u00e4llning: https://www.medicin.lu.se/medicinska-fakulteten-vid-lunds-universitet/jobba-hos-oss/instruktioner-sokande-till-lararanstallningar \u00d6vrig information Upplysningar l\u00e4mnas av prefekt Patrik Midl\u00f6v, tel. +46 73 079 13 63, patrik.midlov@med.lu.se och av dekan Maria Bj\u00f6rkqvist, tel +46 72 700 71 63, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Upplysningar om ans\u00f6kningsf\u00f6rfarande l\u00e4mnas av rekryteringskoordinator Robert Norrman tel. +46 46 222 44 10, robert.norrman@med.lu.se Anst\u00e4llningen tills\u00e4tts efter f\u00f6rslag fr\u00e5n Medicinska l\u00e4rarf\u00f6rslagsn\u00e4mnden. Ans\u00f6kningsf\u00f6rfarande Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks elektroniskt via Lunds universitets s\u00f6kandeportal senast 2026-11-01. Ans\u00f6kan redovisas enligt Medicinska fakultetens anvisningar f\u00f6r s\u00f6kande till l\u00e4raranst\u00e4llning (se https://www.medicin.lu.se/medicinska-fakulteten-vid-lunds-universitet/jobba-hos-oss/instruktioner-sokande-till-lararanstallningar under rubrik Meritsammanst\u00e4llning och CV). Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Vi ser j\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet och m\u00e5ngfald som en styrka och tillg\u00e5ng. V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty\u2019s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malm\u00f6, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Clinical Sciences, Malm\u00f6 is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We have a strong focus on clinical and epidemiological research and also conduct an extensive preclinical laboratory research. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment In accordance with the agreed terms Salary Monthly payment Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Malm\u00f6 County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/468 Contact Patrik Midl\u00f6v, Head of Department, +4640391363, patrik.midlov@med.lu.se Maria Bj\u00f6rkqvist, Dean, +46727007163, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Robert Norrman, Recruitment officer, +46462224410, robert.norrman@med.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, kansli@saco-s.lu.se, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 01.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975187/": {"title": "Vikariat som studiev\u00e4gledare", "description": "Vikariat som studiev\u00e4gledare Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Vikariat som studiev\u00e4gledare Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Institutionen f\u00f6r kommunikation s\u00f6ker nu en studiev\u00e4gledare f\u00f6r ett vikariat. L\u00e4s mer om Lunds universitet och Institutionen f\u00f6r kommunikation h\u00e4r: Start | Institutionen f\u00f6r kommunikation Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Institutionen f\u00f6r kommunikation finns p\u00e5 tre orter, Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Din placering kommer till st\u00f6rsta delen att vara p\u00e5 Campus Helsingborg. N\u00e5gon arbetsdag per vecka arbetar du i Lund. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. Vi erbjuder en varierad och studentn\u00e4ra roll i en akademisk milj\u00f6 och kollegialt samarbete med andra studiev\u00e4gledare och administrat\u00f6rer. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att vara\u00a0anst\u00e4lld hos oss . Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsomr\u00e5den Som studiev\u00e4gledare vid Institutionen f\u00f6r kommunikation f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas du s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla en professionell studiev\u00e4gledning med h\u00f6g kvalitet p\u00e5 s\u00e5v\u00e4l v\u00e4gledning som bem\u00f6tande av v\u00e5ra studenter. I rollen kommer du bland annat att ha uppgifter som: mottagning av presumtiva och nuvarande studenter v\u00e4gledning av program och kursval studieadministration studieuppf\u00f6ljning karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledning bereda student\u00e4renden ta fram intyg och information till studenter I uppgifterna ing\u00e5r \u00e4ven marknadsf\u00f6ring av kurser och program. Du kommer ocks\u00e5 att delta i olika n\u00e4tverk och grupper tillsammans med andra studiev\u00e4gledare inom Lunds universitet. \u00c4ven andra arbetsuppgifter kan komma att ing\u00e5. Kvalifikationer Vi s\u00f6ker dig som har: Erfarenhet av studiev\u00e4gledning vid universitet eller h\u00f6gskola. Akademisk examen inom studie- och karri\u00e4rv\u00e4gledning eller annan universitets- eller h\u00f6gskoleutbildning som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer som likv\u00e4rdig. F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt, strukturerat och med h\u00f6g grad av ansvarstagande. Du tar ansvar f\u00f6r dina uppgifter och driver dina processer vidare. God initiativf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga och ett l\u00f6sningsorienterat arbetss\u00e4tt. H\u00f6g noggrannhet och god administrativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga. Ett lyh\u00f6rt, serviceinriktat och ut\u00e5triktat f\u00f6rh\u00e5llningss\u00e4tt. Mycket god kommunikativ f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, s\u00e5v\u00e4l muntligt som skriftligt. Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska, b\u00e5de i tal och skrift. Det \u00e4r meriterande om du dessutom: har erfarenhet av arbete i Ladok, NyA, Canvas och W3D3 har kunskap om Lunds universitet \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r ett vikariat fr\u00e5n och med januari 2027 till och med 30e juni 2027. Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning \u00e4r 75% - 100%. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitets rekryteringssystem och din ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla CV och ett personligt brev med motivering p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt dina meriter \u00f6verensst\u00e4mmer med uppst\u00e4llda krav. Bifoga examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vriga handlingar som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, kontaktuppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.). V\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. Samh\u00e4llsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra f\u00f6r forskning och utbildning inom samh\u00e4lls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i b\u00e5de Lund och Helsingborg, \u00f6ver 700 anst\u00e4llda och cirka 5 700 hel\u00e5rsstudenter \u00e4r fakulteten en av Lunds universitets st\u00f6rsta. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. V\u00e5r huvuduppgift \u00e4r att utveckla, f\u00f6rmedla och f\u00f6rvalta kunskap om samh\u00e4lle, m\u00e4nniska och organisationer i en milj\u00f6 som pr\u00e4glas av \u00f6ppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Institutionen f\u00f6r kommunikation erbjuder en internationell, interdisciplin\u00e4r och dynamisk milj\u00f6 f\u00f6r utbildning och forskning inom journalistik, strategisk kommunikation samt medie- och kommunikationsvetenskap. V\u00e5ra utbildningar kombinerar teoretiska insikter med praktiska f\u00e4rdigheter f\u00f6r att rusta studenter f\u00f6r arbetslivet och vidare studier. Vi arbetar n\u00e4ra mediebranschen, civilsamh\u00e4llet, f\u00f6retag och offentlig sektor f\u00f6r att ge studenter och forskare m\u00f6jlighet att bidra till och dra nytta av verksamhet utanf\u00f6r akademin. V\u00e5ra forskare studerar kommunikations- och medielandskapets utveckling p\u00e5 lokal, nationell och global niv\u00e5. De utforskar och analyserar kritiskt hur kommunikation och digitala medieteknologier p\u00e5verkar organisationer, politik, samh\u00e4lle och kultur. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid/Deltid L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 75-100 Ort Helsingborg L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2859 Kontakt Tobias Linn\u00e9, Prefekt, tobias.linne@iko.lu.se Emelie Larenhjelm, HR-administrat\u00f6r, emelie.larenhjelm@sam.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-30 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:976668/": {"title": "Serviceassistent vid BMC", "description": "Serviceassistent vid BMC Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Serviceassistent vid BMC Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Verksamhetsst\u00f6d \u00e4r Medicinska fakultetens gemensamma support- och serviceorganisation. Vi ger samordnat och behovsanpassat st\u00f6d till fakultetens verksamheter inom flera olika omr\u00e5den \u2013\u00a0och bidrar till en v\u00e4l fungerande vardag f\u00f6r forskning, utbildning och administration. Verksamhetsst\u00f6d omfattar fem verksamhetsomr\u00e5den: Bibliotek, Lokalservice , Lokalplanering, IT samt Universitetsveterin\u00e4ren. H\u00e4r finns \u00e4ven en stab och ett HMS-team som samordnar fakultetens arbete med h\u00e4lsa, milj\u00f6 och s\u00e4kerhet. Avdelningen f\u00f6r Lokalservice ansvarar f\u00f6r teknik och service p\u00e5 BMC (Lund) och CRC (Malm\u00f6).\u00a0 Avdelningens uppdrag \u00e4r att verkst\u00e4lla underh\u00e5ll, fastighetssk\u00f6tsel samt leverans av fastst\u00e4llda tj\u00e4nster mot fakultetens egna verksamheter (t ex kansli och institutioner). Avdelningen arbetar \u00e4ven med f\u00f6rebyggande och avhj\u00e4lpande underh\u00e5ll, och tar inom sitt ansvarsomr\u00e5de emot felanm\u00e4lningar och best\u00e4llningar fr\u00e5n verksamheten. Inom Verksamhetsst\u00f6d v\u00e4rnar vi om en god arbetsmilj\u00f6 med respekt och omtanke i relationerna med varandra. Vi s\u00f6ker nu en serviceassistent till avdelningen Lokalservice med placering p\u00e5 BMC i Lund. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats \"https://www.lu.se/om-universitetet/jobba-hos-oss\" om att vara anst\u00e4lld hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter Som serviceassistent kommer du i huvudsak att arbeta med: bokning och m\u00f6blering av m\u00f6teslokaler / lokaler, postsortering och utdelning av post, vid behov vara backup / extra resurs till receptionen. \u00c4ven andra arbetsuppgifter som \u00e4r relevanta f\u00f6r den verksamhet som bedrivs inom Lokalservice kan f\u00f6rekomma. Arbetsuppgifterna kan medf\u00f6ra tunga lyft. Arbetet som serviceassistent inneb\u00e4r kontakter med olika delar av verksamheten och sker till stor del i samarbete med v\u00e5r \u00f6vriga serviceorganisation. Kvalifikationer Krav: genomf\u00f6rd gymnasieutbildning med godk\u00e4nt resultat (betyg), erfarenhet av serviceinriktat arbete, datorvana och god erfarenhet av arbete med MS Office (Word, Excel och Outlook), goda spr\u00e5kkunskaper i svenska och engelska, k\u00f6rkort B - f\u00f6r manuellt v\u00e4xlad bil. Meriterande: erfarenhet av receptions- och konferensarbete erfarenhet av arbete med st\u00f6dsystem; till exempel TimeEdit, Salto och Serix, Stor vikt kommer att l\u00e4ggas vid personliga egenskaper. Arbetsuppgifterna f\u00f6ruts\u00e4tter att du har gott ordningssinne, samordnings- och samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga. Det \u00e4r viktigt att du har en v\u00e4l utvecklad servicek\u00e4nsla samt en professionell och positiv framtoning. Vi ser g\u00e4rna att du tar dig an dina arbetsuppgifter p\u00e5 ett ansvarsfullt s\u00e4tt och har en stark vilja att fr\u00e4mja en god teamk\u00e4nsla \u00d6vrigt anst\u00e4llningen inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas b\u00e4ra tilldelad arbetskl\u00e4dsel, vid behov kan tj\u00e4nstg\u00f6ring i Malm\u00f6 vara aktuellt, provanst\u00e4llning kommer att till\u00e4mpas, startdatum enligt \u00f6verenskommelse, vid erbjudande om anst\u00e4llning kommer ber\u00f6rd s\u00f6kande att beh\u00f6va bekr\u00e4fta sin identitet via pass / nationellt id-kort. Avdelningen str\u00e4var efter en mer j\u00e4mst\u00e4lld arbetsplats varp\u00e5 vi g\u00e4rna ser att b\u00e5de kvinnor och m\u00e4n s\u00f6ker anst\u00e4llningen. Medicinska fakulteten \u00e4r ett verksamhetsomr\u00e5de inom Lunds universitet, med ansvar f\u00f6r utbildning och forskning inom medicin, v\u00e5rd och h\u00e4lsa. Utbildningen sker i n\u00e4ra samverkan med sjukv\u00e5rden och \u00e4r v\u00e4l f\u00f6rankrad i fakultetens starka forskningstradition. Fakultetens forskning sp\u00e4nner \u00f6ver ett brett f\u00e4lt inom experimentell grundforskning, patientn\u00e4ra klinisk forskning och h\u00e4lsovetenskaplig forskning. Medicinska fakulteten, med drygt 1800 anst\u00e4llda och 3000 studenter i Lund, Malm\u00f6 och Helsingborg, \u00e4r en kunskapsintensiv m\u00f6tesplats f\u00f6r studenter, l\u00e4rare och forskare fr\u00e5n hela v\u00e4rlden. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de Snarast eller efter \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2897 Kontakt Joel Johansson, Avdelningschef, +4640391109, joel.johansson@med.lu.se Jeffrey Armstrong, HR-specialist, +46462227103, jeffrey.armstrong@med.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977396/": {"title": "Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research", "description": "Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV, Beamline Office Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is looking for a Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research. The focus will be to document experimental designs and procedures that give reliable and reproducible results, transferrable between research facilities in Europe. Two to three reaction cells based on the most promising designs will be developed and tested at major European synchrotrons. All results (CAD models, performance data, and procedures) will be published in an open data base for the benefit of the European research community. Your team At MAX IV, you will work in the Support Labs team which is part of the Beamline Office group. The Support Labs team is involved in support for sample preparation, installation and maintenance of sample environments, as well as detector support for beamlines. In addition, the team operates ten chemistry and instrumentation labs across MAX IV. This project was granted funding from the EU organisation LEAPS, consisting of all major synchrotron radiation sources in Europe. The motivation for the project comes from academia and industry that seeks standardisation of electrochemical experiments and technical solutions to ensure reproducible and accurate results from all facilities. The project is called SEEQuality and includes close collaboration with a postdoc at ESRF/CEA (France) and an engineer at HZB (Germany). Your main work tasks will be Plan and partake in the development of an expert advisory board in electrochemistry. The board will guide in selecting the best technical solutions. Jointly with ESRF/CEA and HZB review the best designs for electrochemistry experiments, and documenting these in the open database Wayforlight. Take part in the development of electrochemical reaction cells (demonstrators) in collaboration with ESRF/CEA and HZB. Take part in the in the initial testing of the reaction cells and collect data to be published in the Wayforlight database. Take part in a Round-robin test of the developed reaction cells at different synchrotron facilities. To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications PhD in physics, chemistry, or engineering. Demonstrated experience with electrochemistry research at synchrotron radiation sources or similar large research infrastructures. You are interested in interdisciplinary work in collaboration with research groups of very diverse backgrounds as well as engineers and technicians Good command of the English language, good communication and team working skills. Below are seen as merits Demonstrated experience in the development of electrochemical reaction cells. Experience in analysis of data from electrochemical research. Experience with documentation and certification of instrumentation for laboratory experiments. Experience with instrumentation used in synchrotron X-ray based research. As a person you have a demonstrated ability to work independently, as well as having the ability to cooperate with different teams and functions. Eligibility Appointment to the position of postdoc requires that the applicant has a PhD or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the application deadline. Under special circumstances the PhD can have been completed previous to the aforementioned three years. Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment for 2 years. A postdoctoral fellow is employed under a period of at least two years and at most three years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement \u201cAvtal om tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning som postdoktor-2022-02-01\u201d (\u201cAgreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow, 2022-02-01\u201d) What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you step into a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world and enabling scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer a multicultural work environment with opportunities for professional development and a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supportive environment and contribute directly to the reliable operation of one of the world's most advanced synchrotron facilities? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference. For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university https://www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences. We regard gender equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2912 Contact Johan Adell, +46708323357, johan.adell@maxiv.lu.se Stefan Carlson, +46733439550, stefan.carlson@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 08.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977402/": {"title": "RF Technician", "description": "RF Technician Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) RF Technician Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV, Accelerator Division Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is looking for a RF Technician to join the RF Group. Your team The RF Group at MAX IV is responsible for the operation, maintenance and development of several high-power radio-frequency systems that are essential for the MAX IV accelerators. The systems include pulsed S-band RF systems as well as continuous-wave VHF/UHF systems, together with associated high-voltage modulators, diagnostics, instrumentation and control systems. Would you like to work hands-on with advanced accelerator technology at one of the brightest light sources in the world? About the role You will work with the operation, maintenance, repair and installation of RF, electronic and high-voltage equipment used throughout the MAX IV accelerator facility. The position has a strong practical focus and involves troubleshooting, repairing, modifying and maintaining specialised technical equipment. The work includes electronics, electrical systems, cabling and, where needed, basic mechanical fabrication and modification of parts. You will work closely with RF engineers and other technical staff to ensure high reliability and availability of the accelerator RF systems. MAX IV is preparing for MAX 4 U , a major upgrade of the 3 GeV storage ring. As part of the RF Group, you will have the opportunity to contribute to the technical work associated with this upgrade, including installation, modification and commissioning of RF-related equipment. Your main work tasks will be Maintenance, troubleshooting and repair of RF, electronic and high-voltage equipment. Maintenance and repair of high-voltage modulators. Electrical and electronic assembly work. Precision soldering and repair of electronic equipment and circuit boards. Manufacturing, installation and repair of cables and cable assemblies. Installation and modification of RF equipment, electronics and associated infrastructure. Preventive maintenance and inspection of technical systems. Documentation of maintenance, repairs and technical modifications. Participation in fault finding and corrective maintenance during accelerator operation. Collaboration with RF engineers in system upgrades, improvements and new installations. Participate in technical installations, modifications and commissioning activities related to future accelerator upgrades, including MAX 4 U . To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications Relevant technical education in electronics, electrical engineering, RF technology or a related technical field, or equivalent professional experience. Good practical skills in electronics and electrical work. Experience with soldering and assembly of electronic equipment. Ability to read and understand electrical schematics and technical documentation. Experience in troubleshooting and repairing electrical or electronic equipment. A structured and safety-conscious way of working. Good command of spoken and written English. Good communication and teamwork skills. Experience with high-voltage equipment. Experience with high-power electronics. Experience with cable manufacturing, connectors and RF cabling. Experience in the fields below is considered a merit RF systems or RF equipment. Pulsed power systems or modulators. Industrial electronics. Electrical cabinets and installations. Measurement equipment such as oscilloscopes, multimeters and signal generators. Mechanical workshop skills, such as using a milling machine, drill press and other common workshop tools. Basic mechanical fabrication, modification and fitting of components. Maintenance of complex scientific, industrial or accelerator equipment. Experience from accelerator facilities or synchrotron light sources is an advantage, but not a requirement. About you We are looking for someone who enjoys practical technical work and takes pride in solving problems and keeping complex equipment operational. You are systematic, thorough and safety-conscious, and you are comfortable working both independently and together with engineers and technicians. You are curious and willing to learn new systems and technologies, and you enjoy turning technical problems into practical solutions. What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you step into a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world and enabling scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer a multicultural work environment with opportunities for professional development and a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supportive environment and contribute directly to the reliable operation of one of the world's most advanced synchrotron facilities? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference. For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university https://www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ Probationary period may apply. On-call services may apply. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences. We regard gender equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position \u2013 (starting with a temporary contract) Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2913 Contact Robert Lindvall, gruppchef, +46462221598, robert.lindvall@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:978489/": {"title": "PhD in Sociology of Law", "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Islamic Ethics and Governance in Central Asia Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Islamic Ethics and Governance in Central Asia Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures \u2013 Islamic Ethics and Administrative Reform in Central Asia Project description This doctoral project investigates how Islamic ethical principles influence legal and governance reforms in Uzbekistan and Kazakhstan. The doctoral candidate will examine whether religiously informed governance practices and legal strategies strengthen accountability, public trust, and institutional effectiveness, or whether they primarily serve as tools of political legitimation. The project engages with emerging scholarship on Islamic public administration, Islamic legal culture and governance traditions. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia (Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Participate in training events, workshops, and conferences organized by the MINARET Doctoral Network. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA \u2013 Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department\u2019s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic public administration, Islamic legal culture and governance traditions. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of Central Asian legal and political contexts is an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant\u2019s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Islamic Ethics and Administrative Reform in Central Asia . General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master\u2019s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant\u2019s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2939 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:979730/": {"title": "Bibliotekarie till Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek", "description": "Bibliotekarie till Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Bibliotekarie till Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek utg\u00f6r en del av biblioteksverksamheten vid Lunds universitet som best\u00e5r av Universitetsbiblioteket och \u00e5tta fakultetsbibliotek. Biblioteket \u00e4r ett av Nordens st\u00f6rsta juridiska bibliotek och \u00e4r \u00e4ven ett Europeiskt dokumentationscentrum. V\u00e5r verksamhet \u00e4r v\u00e4l integrerad i Juridiska fakultetens forsknings- och utbildningsprocesser. Vi f\u00f6rser fakultetens forskare, l\u00e4rare och studenter med \u00e4mnesanpassat biblioteksst\u00f6d, och tillhandah\u00e5ller \u00e4ven service till Lunds universitet och till allm\u00e4nheten. Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek s\u00f6ker en vikarie f\u00f6r v\u00e5rterminen. Du kommer att ing\u00e5 i ett team av inkluderande och v\u00e4lkomnande kollegor som bidrar med sin kompetens i en kreativ akademisk milj\u00f6 med engagerade medarbetare och studenter. F\u00f6r mer information om biblioteket se: https://www.jur.lu.se/bibliotek Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet vilket inneb\u00e4r att du f\u00e5r s\u00e4rskilda f\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, gener\u00f6s semester och en f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension. Vi har \u00e4ven ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda f\u00f6ruts\u00e4ttningar f\u00f6r balans mellan arbete och fritid. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitetets webbplats om att jobba hos oss Arbetsuppgifter Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r ett vikariat med fokus p\u00e5 mediehantering och anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d d\u00e4r du i ditt arbete b\u00e5de samarbetar med kollegor och f\u00f6rdjupar dig sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt. Kanske har du lagt grunden inom yrket och \u00e4r redo att ta n\u00e4sta steg i rollen som bibliotekarie, eller vill du byta inriktning och testa arbete med \u00e4mnesf\u00f6rdjupning inom akademin? D\u00e5 kan detta vara ett perfekt tillf\u00e4lle f\u00f6r dig. Juridiska biblioteket \u00e4r i inledningsskedet av ett stort gallringsprojekt som ska s\u00e4kerst\u00e4lla samlingarnas relevans och anv\u00e4ndbarhet, och samtidigt uppr\u00e4tta rutiner f\u00f6r konsekvent gallring och ett h\u00e5llbart samlingsarbete p\u00e5 sikt. Med st\u00f6d i riktlinjer och manualer kommer du att f\u00e5 vara med och l\u00e4gga grunden f\u00f6r det praktiska arbetet med systematisk gallring. Arbetsuppgifterna i vikariatet har fokus p\u00e5 mediehantering och anv\u00e4ndarst\u00f6d. Gallring i magasin och p\u00e5 \u00f6ppna hyllor liksom tj\u00e4nstg\u00f6ring i bibliotekets informationsdisk ing\u00e5r. \u00d6vriga allm\u00e4nt f\u00f6rekommande arbetsuppgifter p\u00e5 ett akademiskt bibliotek kan tillkomma. Kvalifikationer Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Akademisk examen i biblioteks- och informationsvetenskap, eller motsvarande som arbetsgivaren bed\u00f6mer likv\u00e4rdigt Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska i tal och skrift Du m\u00e5ste vara kvalitetsmedveten, serviceinriktad, ha en v\u00e4lutvecklad samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga samt ta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt ansvar f\u00f6r dina arbetsuppgifter och ditt l\u00e4rande. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r: Erfarenhet av arbete vid universitets- eller h\u00f6gskolebibliotek Erfarenhet av gallringsarbete Erfarenhet av arbete i informationsdisk Vi vill \u00e4ven att du har helhetsperspektiv och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att prioritera. Vi l\u00e4gger stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet samt hur du genom din erfarenhet och kompetens bed\u00f6ms komplettera och st\u00e4rka verksamheten vid Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek. Villkor Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r ett vikariat p\u00e5 100% under 6 m\u00e5nader med startdatum 2027-01-07 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse, som l\u00e4ngst till och med 2027-06-30. Intervjuer \u00e4r planerade till vecka 47. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r s\u00f6ker du Anst\u00e4llningen s\u00f6ks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ans\u00f6kan ska inneh\u00e5lla personligt brev med motivering till varf\u00f6r du \u00e4r intresserad av anst\u00e4llningen och p\u00e5 vilket s\u00e4tt anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter. Ans\u00f6kan ska \u00e4ven inneh\u00e5lla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt \u00f6vrigt som du \u00f6nskar \u00e5beropa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser etc.) Juridiska fakulteten \u00e4r en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter p\u00e5 grundniv\u00e5 och avancerad niv\u00e5 och ett 160-tal anst\u00e4llda varav ett 40-tal \u00e4r doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns p\u00e5 v\u00e5r hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2027-06-30 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-07 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2978 Kontakt Catarina Carlsson, Bibliotekschef, +46462221096, catarina.carlsson@jur.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-09 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:979777/": {"title": "Grafisk produktionsmedarbetare till Media-Tryck", "description": "Grafisk produktionsmedarbetare till Media-Tryck Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Grafisk produktionsmedarbetare till Media-Tryck Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Vill du arbeta praktiskt med grafisk produktion i en verksamhet d\u00e4r kvalitet, samarbete och leverans st\u00e5r i centrum? Som produktionsmedarbetare p\u00e5 Media-Tryck blir du en viktig del av ett gemensamt produktionsteam som hj\u00e4lper Lunds universitets verksamheter fr\u00e5n f\u00e4rdigt produktionsunderlag till f\u00e4rdig produkt. H\u00e4r f\u00e5r du ett varierat arbete med modern produktionsutrustning, tydliga deadlines och stort ansvar f\u00f6r att uppdragen blir r\u00e4tt utf\u00f6rda och levererade i tid. V\u00e4lkommen till LU Service och Media-Tryck LU Service erbjuder tj\u00e4nster och produkter till hela universitetet inom bland annat lokalservice, reception, konferens, post och grafisk produktion. Media-Tryck \u00e4r universitetets interna leverant\u00f6r av grafiska tj\u00e4nster och arbetar med hela processen \u2013 fr\u00e5n id\u00e9 och original till tryck, efterbehandling, distribution och leverans. Verksamheten kombinerar service, produktion och r\u00e5dgivning och har ett stort fokus p\u00e5 kvalitet, leverans och utveckling. Om rollen Som produktionsmedarbetare arbetar du brett genom flera delar av produktionen. Du planerar och prioriterar ditt arbete utifr\u00e5n inkommande uppdrag och deadlines och s\u00e4kerst\u00e4ller tillsammans med kollegorna att produktionen h\u00e5ller r\u00e4tt kvalitet och anv\u00e4nder verksamhetens resurser effektivt. Rollen \u00e4r inte knuten till en enskild maskin. Arbetsuppgifterna varierar, och du f\u00f6rv\u00e4ntas hj\u00e4lpa till d\u00e4r behovet f\u00f6r tillf\u00e4llet \u00e4r st\u00f6rst. Arbetsuppgifter Digital tryckproduktion, stor- och sm\u00e5formatsproduktion. Efterbehandling. Kontroll av produktionsunderlag inf\u00f6r produktion. Kvalitetskontroll av producerat material. Enklare fels\u00f6kning, underh\u00e5ll och l\u00f6pande tillsyn av produktionsutrustning. Planering och prioritering av det egna arbetet utifr\u00e5n uppdrag och deadlines. Att tillsammans med kollegorna bidra till ordning, struktur och ett effektivt produktionsfl\u00f6de. Kvalifikationer F\u00f6r att vara aktuell f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen ska du ha: Erfarenhet av arbete inom grafisk produktion, tryckproduktion eller annan j\u00e4mf\u00f6rbar produktionsmilj\u00f6. Erfarenhet av att arbeta med maskiner och produktionsutrustning. God digital vana och f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att arbeta i olika system. F\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att f\u00f6rst\u00e5 och f\u00f6lja produktionsinstruktioner och arbetsfl\u00f6den. God f\u00f6rm\u00e5ga att kommunicera p\u00e5 svenska och engelska i tal och skrift. Meriterande Det \u00e4r meriterande om du har erfarenhet av ett eller flera av f\u00f6ljande omr\u00e5den: Digital tryckproduktion. Storformatsproduktion med monteringserfarenhet. Efterbehandling. Produktions- eller ordersystem inom grafisk verksamhet. Grundl\u00e4ggande kunskaper inom prepress och hantering av PDF-filer f\u00f6r tryckproduktion. Vem \u00e4r du? Du arbetar systematiskt och noggrant och kan h\u00e5lla ordning och kvalitet \u00e4ven n\u00e4r flera uppdrag p\u00e5g\u00e5r samtidigt. Du \u00e4r flexibel och kan v\u00e4xla mellan arbetsuppgifter, maskiner och olika typer av produktion. Eftersom vi arbetar som ett gemensamt team beh\u00f6ver du ha god samarbetsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, ta ansvar f\u00f6r helheten och bidra d\u00e4r behovet finns. Du har en praktisk probleml\u00f6sningsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ga, uppm\u00e4rksammar problem i tid och vet n\u00e4r du beh\u00f6ver ta hj\u00e4lp. Du \u00e4r nyfiken p\u00e5 att l\u00e4ra dig nya maskiner, produktionsmetoder och arbetss\u00e4tt. I kontakten med kunder och kollegor \u00e4r du professionell, lyh\u00f6rd och l\u00f6sningsorienterad. Du tar reda p\u00e5 behov, ger tydlig \u00e5terkoppling och f\u00f6ljer upp det ni har kommit \u00f6verens om. Vi kommer att l\u00e4gga stor vikt vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet och hur din erfarenhet och dina egenskaper kompletterar teamet. Vi erbjuder Ett varierat och praktiskt arbete i en unik universitetsmilj\u00f6. M\u00f6jlighet att utveckla din kompetens inom flera delar av grafisk produktion. Engagerade kollegor och ett arbetss\u00e4tt d\u00e4r vi hj\u00e4lper varandra och tar gemensamt ansvar f\u00f6r leveransen. Gener\u00f6s semester, friskv\u00e5rdsf\u00f6rm\u00e5ner, f\u00f6rm\u00e5nlig tj\u00e4nstepension och andra statliga anst\u00e4llningsvillkor. L\u00e4s mer om hur det \u00e4r att jobba hos oss p\u00e5 universitetets hemsida, l\u00e4nk nedan. Jobba hos oss | Lunds universitet \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r en tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning p\u00e5 100 %, med tilltr\u00e4de snarast enligt \u00f6verenskommelse. Provanst\u00e4llning i 6 m\u00e5nader kan komma att till\u00e4mpas. L\u00f6nespannet f\u00f6r tj\u00e4nsten \u00e4r 30 000 - 37 000 kr. Universitetet till\u00e4mpar individuell l\u00f6nes\u00e4ttning. Ange g\u00e4rna l\u00f6neanspr\u00e5k i din ans\u00f6kan. LU Service \u00e4r en sektion inom universitetets gemensamma f\u00f6rvaltning och erbjuder s\u00e5v\u00e4l tj\u00e4nster som produkter till universitetets verksamheter: bl.a. lokalv\u00e5rd, vaktm\u00e4steri, reception, tryckeri, post, parkering, universitetsbutik, konferens och bost\u00e4der. LU Service har ca 240 medarbetare. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tillsvidareanst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Heltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2026-12-01 eller enligt \u00f6verenskommelse L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 100 Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2979 Kontakt Mikael Olofsson, Avdelningschef, mikael.olofsson@service.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-10-30 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:980150/": {"title": "PhD in Sociology of Law", "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Women's Legal Agency in Central Asia and MENA Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Women's Legal Agency in Central Asia and MENA Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures \u2013 Women's Legal Agency Across Post-Imperial Islamic Societies in Central Asia, the Middle East, and North Africa Project description This doctoral project explores how women in Tunisia, Lebanon, and Uzbekistan use both Islamic and secular legal frameworks to claim rights, challenge discrimination, and expand access to justice. The doctoral candidate will analyse legal mobilisation, constitutional reform, and women\u2019s agency as drivers of social and political transformation in post-imperial Islamic societies. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (Uzbekistan, Lebanon and Tunisia) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Participate in training events, workshops, and conferences organized by the MINARET Doctoral Network. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA \u2013 Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department\u2019s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic legal cultures, Islam and gender studies, and legal mobilization scholarship is an asset. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of the legal and political contexts of Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) is considered an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant\u2019s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Women's Legal Agency Across Post-Imperial Islamic Societies in Central Asia, the Middle East, and North Africa . General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master\u2019s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant\u2019s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2991 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:980246/": {"title": "PhD in Sociology of Law", "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures \u2013 Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes: Insights from Central Asia and North Africa Project description This doctoral project investigates how governments in Uzbekistan and Egypt mobilise religious narratives to justify security policies and governance strategies. The doctoral candidate will analyse how religion becomes embedded within state security frameworks and assess the implications of these processes for citizenship, constitutional legitimacy, and state-society relations in hybrid political regimes. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia and North Africa (Uzbekistan and Egypt) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Participate in training events, workshops, and conferences organized by the MINARET Doctoral Network. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA \u2013 Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department\u2019s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic legal culture, security studies and hybrid and authoritarian governance literature. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of the legal and political contexts of Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) is considered an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant\u2019s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes: Insights from Central Asia and North Africa .\u00a0General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master\u2019s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant\u2019s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2993 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:980250/": {"title": "PhD in Sociology of Law", "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Civil Islam and Non-Coercive Governance Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law \u2013 Civil Islam and Non-Coercive Governance Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures \u2013 Civil Islam and Non-Coercive Governance Across Post-Imperial Islamic Societies in Central Asia, Southeast Asia, and North Africa Project description This doctoral project investigates how civil Islam, legal mobilisation, and faith-based movements contribute to non-coercive governance and constitutional participation in Tunisia, Indonesia, and Uzbekistan. The doctoral candidate will examine how religious values can support democratic engagement, strengthen social trust, and foster peaceful political transformation. The project aims to advance understanding of religion as a resource for constitutional legitimacy and civic participation in post-imperial Islamic societies. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia, Southeast Asia and North Africa (Uzbekistan, Indonesia and Tunisia) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA \u2013 Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department\u2019s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Sk\u0142odowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic legal culture, Islamic public administration, comparative constitutional law and hybrid and authoritarian governance literature. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of the legal and political contexts of Central Asia, Southeast Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) is considered an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant\u2019s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Civil Islam and Non-Coercive Governance Across Post-Imperial Islamic Societies in Central Asia, Southeast Asia, and North Africa. General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master\u2019s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant\u2019s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2994 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970106/": {"title": "Teaching assistant", "description": "Teaching assistant at the Department of Electrical and Information Technology for work with coordination of undergraduate laboratories Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Teaching assistant at the Department of Electrical and Information Technology for work with coordination of undergraduate laboratories Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world\u2019s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malm\u00f6. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.\u00a0 We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Department of Electrical and Information Technology at The Faculty of Engineering, LTH, Lund University is one of the larger departments with around 120 employees. The department consists of four divisions and a group of technical and administrative staff. We are situated in the E-building at LTH\u2019s campus in the north of Lund, but we also have teaching activities at campus Helsingborg. We conduct research and education within areas related to semiconductor technology, electromagnetics, electronic systems, communication technology, communication networks, internet and information security. We have 70-75 undergraduate courses over a year, targeting the master\u2019s programmes in Lund and the Bachelor programmes in Helsingborg. At the department we have a lot of laboratory activities, both in research and teaching. We have a research lab dedicated to research within electronics systems, wireless communication and 5G and 6G networks and applications. We also have several equipped laboratories for teaching, for example withing electronic systems and communication networks. We are now looking for a teaching assistant for work with coordination of undergraduate laboratories and their equipment at the department. The work will be under the guidance of the Director of studies. There may also be teaching related duties included in the work. Work duties The duties include: To be contact person for our undergraduate laboratories and their equipment. To assist in the development of our undergraduate laboratory premises and their equipment. Administration in connection with the undergraduate laboratories and their equipment. Qualification requirements Only those admitted to first or second-cycle courses and study programmes at the faculty may be employed as teaching assistants. Required qualifications: Admitted to a master\u2019s programme at LTH. Very good oral and written proficiency in Swedish and English. Good grades from courses at the department, especially in the applied and laboratory courses. Additional requirements: Work experience in related areas. Ability to take responsibility and to be able to work both in a team and individually. Teaching experience. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. With an employment as a teaching assistant, you can combine studies with work and complement your theoretical knowledge with practical work experience. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee Work at Lund University . Further information The position is a fixed term position for the period from November 9, 2026, or as soon as possible after this by agreement, until May 31, 2027, at 20% of full-time. A Teaching Assistant position may be no more than 50% of full-time employment and may be limited to a maximum of one year, with a total maximum of three years. The employment must not affect studies in a negative way. The employment as a Teaching Assistant is regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (SFS 2017:284), 5 chapter 8-12 \u00a7\u00a7. The position is covered by the flexitime agreement for the technical and administrative staff. How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University\u2019s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. We ask you to attach documentation from Ladok certifying your eligibility. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.). Welcome to apply! About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University\u2019s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers \u2013 many of whom work in world-leading profile areas \u2013 publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create \u2013 to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time First day of employment November 9, 2026, or as soon as possible efter this according by agreement Salary M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 20% City Lund County Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2707 Contact Anders J Johansson, Director 1st and 2nd cycle studies, +46462229027, anders_j.johansson@eit.lth.se Stefan H\u00f6st, Head of Department, +46462224278, stefan.host@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 15.Oct.2026 Last application date 29.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement \u00d7 Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973119/": {"title": "Amanuens som SI-ledare i Antikens kultur och samh\u00e4llsliv: Forts\u00e4ttningskurs", "description": "Amanuens som SI-ledare i Antikens kultur och samh\u00e4llsliv: Forts\u00e4ttningskurs Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens som SI-ledare i Antikens kultur och samh\u00e4llsliv: Forts\u00e4ttningskurs Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Institutionen f\u00f6r arkeologi och antikens historia, HT Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Vad \u00e4r SI? SI-PASS ( Supplemental Instruction \u2013 Peer Assisted Study Sessions ) \u00e4r en mycket framg\u00e5ngsrik pedagogisk modell som utvecklades i USA under 1970-talet och har spridits till m\u00e5nga l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten v\u00e4rlden \u00f6ver, inklusive Lunds universitet. Vi erbjuder Som SI-ledare p\u00e5 en kurs p\u00e5 Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna \u00e4r du anst\u00e4lld som amanuens p\u00e5 en av fakulteternas institutioner och f\u00e5r din SI-ledarutbildning fr\u00e5n European Centre for SI-PASS. En anst\u00e4llning som SI-ledare ger dig en inblick i den akademiska v\u00e4rlden och f\u00f6rutom f\u00f6rdjupade \u00e4mneskunskaper och ledarskapserfarenhet f\u00e5r du \u00e4ven m\u00f6jlighet att skapa professionella kontakter inom den aktuella institutionen och fakulteten. Du blir dessutom en del av ett v\u00e4rldsomsp\u00e4nnande n\u00e4tverk som omfattar SI-ledare i ett antal l\u00e4nder v\u00e4rlden \u00f6ver, med bland annat m\u00f6jlighet att delta i internationella konferenser, liksom knyta internationella kontakter. Tidigare SI-ledare har visat sig vara mycket konkurrenskraftiga p\u00e5 arbetsmarknaden. Lunds universitet \u00e4r en statlig myndighet och erbjuder goda anst\u00e4llningsvillkor. Med en anst\u00e4llning som amanuens f\u00e5r du som student en m\u00f6jlighet att f\u00f6rena studier med arbete f\u00f6r att komplettera dina teoretiska kunskaper med praktisk arbetslivserfarenhet inom akademin. L\u00e4s mer p\u00e5 universitets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter Du kommer att arbeta i n\u00e4ra samarbete med s\u00e5v\u00e4l l\u00e4rare som ansvariga f\u00f6r SI-programmet p\u00e5 din avdelning, samt med andra SI-ledare, b\u00e5de inom och utanf\u00f6r samma \u00e4mne. Du kommer \u00e4ven att bjudas in till regelbundna metodhandledningsm\u00f6ten som leds av SI-ansvarig metodhandledare. Som SI-ledare anordnar du regelbundet SI-PASS f\u00f6r studenterna i den aktuella kursen. Genom att tillsammans diskutera begrepp och fr\u00e5gest\u00e4llningar ur kursmaterialet kan studenterna s\u00e5ledes kollaborativt finna svar och l\u00f6sningar, d\u00e4r du som SI-ledare tar rollen som diskussionsledare, bollplank och mentor, snarare \u00e4n l\u00e4rare. I dina arbetsuppgifter som SI-ledare ing\u00e5r i korthet att: f\u00f6rbereda, schemal\u00e4gga och leda SI-pass i det aktuella \u00e4mnet cirka tv\u00e5 g\u00e5nger per m\u00e5nad registrera studenternas n\u00e4rvaro och skriva en reflektiv rapport efter varje SI-PASS regelbundet delta i SI-metodhandledningsm\u00f6ten 1\u20132 g\u00e5nger per termin ge feedback till andra SI-ledarkollegor efter observerat SI-PASS \u00e4ven andra arbetsuppgifter kan f\u00f6rekomma Kvalifikationer Beh\u00f6rig att anst\u00e4llas som amanuens \u00e4r den som aktivt bedriver studier p\u00e5 grund- eller avancerad niv\u00e5 p\u00e5 Lunds universitet och som \u00e4nnu inte tagit ut sin examen. Krav f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r att: du \u00e4r antagen till en utbildning vid Lunds universitet du har deltagit i SI-PASS som student (om det har erbjudits i de kurser du l\u00e4st) du har sj\u00e4lv l\u00e4st och blivit godk\u00e4nd p\u00e5 den aktuella kursen (AKSA32) eller motsvarande du ligger i fas med dina studier du \u00e4r ansvarstagande, kommunikativ och samarbetsvillig du besitter goda spr\u00e5kkunskaper i det spr\u00e5k som kursen bedrivs p\u00e5 Stor vikt kommer att l\u00e4ggas vid personlig l\u00e4mplighet. Meriterande f\u00f6r anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r att: du har mycket goda resultat i den relevanta kursen du har ledarskapserfarenhet du kan arbeta sj\u00e4lvst\u00e4ndigt du har visat engagemang i dina studier du har visat engagemang i tidigare SI-deltagande du \u00e4r intresserad av pedagogik, gruppdynamik och ledarskap du bedriver fortsatt aktivt studier i det aktuella \u00e4mnet \u00d6vrigt Anst\u00e4llningen \u00e4r tidsbegr\u00e4nsad under perioden 2027-01-11 \u2013 2027-06-04 och avser omfattningen 5% av heltid. Anst\u00e4llningen f\u00e5r inte p\u00e5verka amanuensens studier negativt. Best\u00e4mmelser g\u00e4llande utbildningsanst\u00e4llning som amanuens finns i H\u00f6gskolef\u00f6rordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8-12 \u00a7\u00a7. S\u00e5 h\u00e4r ans\u00f6ker du Ans\u00f6kan g\u00f6rs via Lunds universitets rekryteringssystem Varbi och ska inneh\u00e5lla f\u00f6ljande handlingar: CV, personligt brev, Ladok-utdrag samt antagningsbesked f\u00f6r VT27. I det personliga brevet ska du motivera hur anst\u00e4llningen matchar dina meriter och kompetenser samt reflektera \u00f6ver SI:s betydelse f\u00f6r studenterna. Ladok-utdraget ska visa att du har l\u00e4st den aktuella kursen samt att du \u00e4r i fas med dina studier. Antagningsbeskedet ska styrka att du \u00e4r antagen till utbildning vid Lunds universitet. Om du \u00e4r antagen till ett kandidatprogram bifogar du antagningsbeskedet fr\u00e5n antagningstillf\u00e4llet. Om du \u00e4nnu inte har mottagit ditt antagningsbesked f\u00f6r VT27 ansvarar du sj\u00e4lv f\u00f6r att skicka in detta s\u00e5 snart det har utf\u00e4rdats. Varmt v\u00e4lkommen med din ans\u00f6kan! Om Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna har sju institutioner och bedriver en stor och varierad verksamhet inom forskning och utbildning. Vi har ca 700 anst\u00e4llda och ca 4 000 hel\u00e5rsstudenter. Om Institutionen f\u00f6r arkeologi och antikens historia Institutionen f\u00f6r arkeologi och antikens historia vid Lunds universitet \u00e4r en av de \u00e4ldsta och st\u00f6rsta arkeologiska institutionerna i Sverige och erbjuder en vital milj\u00f6 f\u00f6r forskning och undervisning. Institutionen best\u00e5r av fyra \u00e4mnen: antikens kultur och samh\u00e4llsliv, arkeologi, historisk arkeologi och historisk osteologi, vilka delvis arbetar med olika k\u00e4llmaterial, metoder och teoretiska perspektiv. Detta \u00e4r institutionens styrka ur b\u00e5de forsknings- och utbildningssynpunkt. V\u00e5ra studenter kombinerar ofta v\u00e5ra olika \u00e4mnen i sina studier f\u00f6r att f\u00e5 en personligt anpassad examen. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter fr\u00e5n annonsf\u00f6rs\u00e4ljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsf\u00f6retag p\u00e5 grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anst\u00e4llningsform Tidsbegr\u00e4nsad anst\u00e4llning Anst\u00e4llningen avslutas 2027-06-04 Anst\u00e4llningens omfattning Deltid Tilltr\u00e4de 2027-01-11 L\u00f6neform M\u00e5nadsl\u00f6n Antal lediga befattningar 1 Syssels\u00e4ttningsgrad 5% Ort Lund L\u00e4n Sk\u00e5ne l\u00e4n Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2789 Kontakt Nene Agneta Ormes, Metodhandledare, 046-2220000, agneta.ormes@ark.lu.se Facklig f\u00f6retr\u00e4dare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackf\u00f6rbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-r\u00e5det vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-15 Sista ans\u00f6kningsdag 2026-11-05 Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Dela l\u00e4nkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillg\u00e4nglighetsredog\u00f6relse \u00d7 Modal title Vi anv\u00e4nder cookies f\u00f6r inloggning, f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttrad anv\u00e4ndarupplevelse, dela-l\u00e4nkar samt i vissa fall marknadsf\u00f6ring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast n\u00f6dv\u00e4ndiga L\u00e4s mer om v\u00e5ra cookies h\u00e4r \u00d7"}, "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973276/": {"title": "Amanuens som SI-ledare i Arkeologi: Forts\u00e4ttningskurs", "description": "Amanuens som SI-ledare i Arkeologi: Forts\u00e4ttningskurs Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens som SI-ledare i Arkeologi: Forts\u00e4ttningskurs Logga in och s\u00f6k jobbet Lunds universitet, Institutionen f\u00f6r arkeologi och antikens historia, HT Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas \u00e5terkommande som ett av v\u00e4rldens fr\u00e4msta l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten. H\u00e4r finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malm\u00f6. Vi f\u00f6renas i v\u00e5r str\u00e4van att f\u00f6rst\u00e5, f\u00f6rklara och f\u00f6rb\u00e4ttra v\u00e5r v\u00e4rld och m\u00e4nniskors villkor. Lunds universitet v\u00e4lkomnar s\u00f6kande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. J\u00e4mst\u00e4lldhet, lika villkor och m\u00e5ngfald \u00e4r grundl\u00e4ggande principer f\u00f6r alla delar av v\u00e5r verksamhet. Vad \u00e4r SI? SI-PASS ( Supplemental Instruction \u2013 Peer Assisted Study Sessions ) \u00e4r en mycket framg\u00e5ngsrik pedagogisk modell som utvecklades i USA under 1970-talet och har spridits till m\u00e5nga l\u00e4ros\u00e4ten v\u00e4rlden \u00f6ver, inklusive Lunds universitet. Vi erbjuder Som SI-ledare p\u00e5 en kurs p\u00e5 Humanistiska och teologiska fakulteterna \u00e4r du anst\u00e4lld som amanuens p\u00e5 en av fakulteternas institutioner och f\u00e5r din SI-ledarutbildning fr\u00e5n European Centre for SI-PASS. En anst\u00e4llning som SI-ledare ger dig en inblick i den akademiska v\u00e4rlden och f\u00f6rutom f\u00f6rdjupade \u00e4mneskunskaper och ledarskapserfarenhet f\u00e5r du \u00e4ven m\u00f6jlighet att skapa professionella kontakter inom den aktuella institutionen och fakulteten. Du blir dessu